* 6: Human resource development
Mr. Kin Phea emphasized that the development of our human resources is a priority area of Cambodia and remains a strategic point of Cambodia within the framework of the Rectangular Strategic Policy. With strong human resources, the development of developed countries is also strong.
* 7: Strengthening the trade sector
Mr. Kin Phea also said that strengthening trade within the ASEAN region, extra-regional trade, especially internal trade should not be overlooked. In particular, strengthening SMEs means strengthening SMEs so that we can seize the opportunities of the Fourth Industrial Revolution, as well as strengthen the digital economy and broader economic connectivity.
* 8: Expand or continue the culture of cultivation and animal husbandry
Mr. Kin Phea reminded that during the time of the People's Republic of Cambodia and the time of the State of Cambodia, Cambodia was under political pressure and faced many problems, but we were able to solve food security because the government of the People's Republic of Cambodia introduced food production. Family with races, races and animal husbandry. At that time, we have ensured excellent food security.
Abe announced his resignation at a news conference on Friday, explaining his health problems after two recent hospitalizations. On that occasion, the 65-year-old Japanese Prime Minister also apologized and thanked the Japanese people for their support and confidence.
This is the second time in Abe's life that he has resigned due to health problems. In 2007, the Japanese prime minister also announced his resignation due to inflammatory bowel disease. Serious after one year in power.
Abe Shinzo was hospitalized twice a week and was reported to have vomited blood from his mouth in his office on July 6. The term of office of the Prime Minister and President of the Liberal Democratic Party (LDP) will end in September 2021.
Abe Shinzo was elected Prime Minister of Japan in 2006 and re-elected in 2012, making him the longest-serving Prime Minister in Japan. Although the exact timing of Abe's resignation has not been confirmed, he did not name anyone who could take over from him.
Apsara Authority Spokesperson: The whole western view of Angkor Wat is changing to be more beautiful
(Siem Reap): Mr. Long Kosal, Spokesman of APSARA Authority, said on August 28, 2020 that from today onwards, the entire western area of Angkor Wat will be transformed into a more beautiful landscape. Beautiful with greenery of trees, meadows and colorful flowers.
Mr. Kosal stated that now the team of APSARA Authority is busy preparing more gardens by planting grass, planting seedlings, planting flowers, preparing paths, cutting grass and actively taking care of plants that have already been planted.
In addition, the team also set up a water release system, including better arrangements to make the western area of Angkor Wat more orderly and beautiful for tourists who come to visit the Angkor resort area. To relax your mind and take these beautiful pictures as a souvenir.
(Phnom Penh): The United States and the Chinese superpower clashed over a trade war until the Donald Trump administration announced the closure and increase of tariffs on goods imported into China. Now even more intense is the technological trade war.
Mr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that this is a reversal of the global trend that is promoting digital systems and is heading for the fourth generation of the Industrial Revolution.
"If there is such a closure, the world economy will be in turmoil and chaos because we know that now the very dependence of international trade is on digital," Kin Phea said. "Therefore, the closure does not benefit the United States itself, China or any other country."
The president of the Institute of International Relations also stressed that unilateralism or protectionism in the race for power between the superpowers is not conducive to the progress of the world economy. No progress or development for the world economy.
Currently, the Chinese company's Tik Tok program is being severely persecuted by the United States and India. India has banned its citizens from using the program after a border dispute with China.
