Ministry of Interior announces the introduction of the symbol of Pursat province
(Pursat): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, has decided to establish and officially use the symbol "Pursat Province" in accordance with Prakas No. 3471 PRK dated August 14, 2020.
In that proclamation, Article 3 states that the symbol of Pursat province is officially used as follows:
* Put in the workplace * Put on the letterhead, documents and official envelopes * Used in the ceremonies of the Pursat Provincial Administration * Officially used in other cases where necessary.
It should be noted that on June 4, 2020, in the 12th Ordinary Meeting of Pursat Provincial Council, 1st year, 3rd mandate, Pursat Provincial Symbol, the Provincial Council reviewed and approved the decision from the Ministry of Interior. The area to be used on official administrative letters and can be built as a place of worship that attracts tourists.
As for the symbol, there is the element "land, people and history" which shows the rich natural resources in the development, starting from the diligence of the people in the favorable territory, so we can define it as a symbol of the province. Below:
* First: The image of a man riding a horse with a sword represents the brave heroism of Duke Ponhea Sour, Grandpa Khleang Moeung, and his family, who are willing to sacrifice their lives for the cause of the nation, motherland, religion, the King and A good example for the next generation to strive to protect and build a prosperous and prosperous homeland.
* Second: Cardamom mountain range (horse background) Cardamom mountain is the name of a mountain in Pursat province, rich in natural mineral resources, non-timber forest products, plants, traditional medicine and a habitat for all kinds of wildlife. The Cardamom Mountains are a source of water for agriculture, handicrafts, industry, as well as a source of hydropower and a potential natural tourism area of the province.
* 4th: Pursat tree and orange: Pursat tree represents the history of the name of Pursat province, from the original word is (Pursat) has 12 cards representing the mother. Pursat oranges represent the fruits that were grown during the French colonial period in Dob Bat village, Bakan district, Pursat province, the first in Cambodia by the Orange Tree Research Station before 1863, and there are 21 fruits representing the father.
* Sixth: The image of rice in a circle of buffalo horns shows the diversity of rice crops that cover a large area of agricultural land, a solid foundation for the national economy.
* Seventh: Bo (red, blue and green) represents the nation that all the people in Pursat province restore and promote in the development of the nation in all areas.
9th: Cardamom is a plant that provides plants, flowers and fruits for use as food and medicine, famous for a long time with the name Cardamom mountain range and cardamom heart. National Institute of Education recruits 30 students for the second generation of Master of French Teaching Methods
