Ministry of Tourism: If any business establishment follows the safety rules and code of conduct for its business, it will receive a quality certification immediately.
(Kampong Thom): The Ministry of Tourism has reiterated its encouragement that if any business entity complies with the safety rules and codes of conduct for its business, the Ministry will immediately issue a tourism safety certificate or Label for posting. Public at their business location.
This reminder was made during the training program on the implementation of food safety and hygiene rules, the arrangement of hygienic outlets and hospitality to food vendors on the street (Food Street), which was chaired by Mr. Prak Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry. Tourism and Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province on August 28, 2020 at Kampong Thom Provincial Hall.
Mr. Pak Sokhom stated that the new tourism safety rules and codes of conduct for the four major tourism businesses that are active include: accommodation business, restaurant business, restaurant-canteen tourism, tourism resort and community tourism business, transport business, road and road tourism. Water is to be widely disseminated in all capitals and provinces throughout the country.
He requested the provincial administration to set up a working group to monitor the implementation of tourism safety rules, with the provincial governor or deputy governor as the director, the director of the Department of Tourism as the permanent deputy director and the secretariat, with members from relevant units and encourage this working group to reach the local level. To monitor the implementation of this tourism safety rule.
In addition, to inform and disseminate measures to all businesses and to report regularly, especially to educate the people and tourists, individuals working in each destination and tour operators as partners to strengthen the prevention of the spread of Kovid disease. -19.
"If any business establishment complies with the safety rules and codes of conduct for its business, the Ministry of Tourism will provide a tourism safety certificate, or a label for public posting at their business location," he said. .
Mr. Sok Loo said that during the Kovid-19 crisis, which continued for a long time, there was a huge impact on the tourism sector in Cambodia, including the tourism service business in Kampong Thom province was also affected. Also.
General Ith Sarath tells soldiers to take turns and continue to spread the word to families and the public to understand the importance of the value of peace
(Kampong Speu): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF), reminded officers and enlisted men to take turns to prevent any attempt to destroy the peace and to participate in further education. Family, friends and the general public to understand the value of peace and political stability.
This kind of reminder by General Ith Sarath was made at the closing ceremony of the 13th generation officer training course and the opening ceremony of the 6th generation officer training course on August 28, 2020 at the Military Institute The mainland of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces is located in Phnom Sruoch district, Kampong Speu province.
General Ith Sarath reminded: "Whoever wants to destroy the peace, we must all work together to prevent and protect the value of peace. "We must help educate our officers, our families, our friends and the general public about the value of peace."
The General stated that due to the victorious policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the country has completely ended the civil war from 1998 to the present, and this peace factor has made all Cambodians Live in peace, have a good life, the country is prosperous in all areas.
General Ith Sarath also urged all military officers to continue to study and compile all documents, training content and experiences of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to compile documents for further training of our young officers to be more quality. More.
According to Lt. Gen. Mam Yoeun, Director of the Army Institute, and Lt. Gen. Ouk Rattanak, Deputy Director of the Institute in charge of training planning, reported that the Army Institute has been ordered to conduct training courses for the 13th generation of officers. A total of 176 trainees, including 29 female cadets, completed the six-month training period from March 2 to August 28, 2020.
At the end of the training, 176 students of the 13th generation of officers and officers received 120 good marks, 43 good marks and 13 average marks.
