To achieve this miracle, the Khmer ancestors used millions of stones, all of which weighed heavily, stacked with the utmost astonishment.
Mr. Long Kosal said that Angkor Wat is built of sandstone and laterite (inside) a lot. As for the exact weight, it can not be confirmed, but according to the assessment of Angkor Wat experts, we can weigh up to millions of tons, because small stones, small pieces are also very heavy.
He added that according to experts who cite scientific evidence, the factors that make this huge temple can stand strong due to two main factors of the foundation, including:
* First. Sand: This sand is most compacted under the foundation before the construction of Angkor Wat. At this point, experts confirm that when the sand is soaked with sand will bite together, not easy to break apart and have the ability to withstand the weight of the temple firmly.
* Second. Water: Although water is a liquid, it helps to increase the concentration of sand under the foundations of Angkor Wat to remain dense even after hundreds of years, i.e. there is enough water to increase the concentration of sand on the foundations of Angkor Wat. The pagoda also remains strong. The water in the basin around Angkor Wat is also directly related to the water stability under the foundation of Angkor Wat.
Please be informed that Angkor Wat was built to represent "Mount Sumeru", the abode of the deity in Hindu mythology. Surrounded by a pond (moat) with a length of 1,500 meters and a width of 1,300 meters, the current depth of 3 meters. The entrance distance from the dragon ladder across the bridge to the curb is 250 meters. The tallest central tower is 65 meters high.
