(Banteay Meanchey): A man who was a drug addict and had been imprisoned for 5 months in the case of stealing three motorbikes and returning from stealing the victim's motorbike from Poipet City to sell in Siem Reap was handcuffed and sent by the authorities Holds Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court.
Poipet City Police said that the suspect, Roeun Kok, a 29-year-old male resident of Chankiri Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province, was arrested by the authorities of Kralanh District, Siem Reap Province on the afternoon of August 26, 2020. The suspect sold the stolen motorcycle.
Police said that according to the victim's complaint, on the night of August 23, 2020, he came from drinking alcohol and left the motorcycle in front of the house, forgot to remove the keys, and lost the motorcycle in the morning. After receiving a complaint from the victim, the municipal police searched and cooperated with the Kralanh district police in Siem Reap province to arrest the suspect who was selling a motorcycle.
According to Colonel Khem Sophoan, the light police chief, the suspect confessed in front of the police that he had stolen the motorcycle, and that he had left the motorcycle in front of the house with his children. The keys were stolen and sold in Siem Reap province. When they arrived in Kralanh district, they sold them for 5,000 baht. At that time, the buyer asked for his credit card and was arrested by the Kralanh district police.
The suspect, after making a report, was referred to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Court by the light criminal police force for legal action, while the motorcycle was returned to its original owner. Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) bans residents of Lvea Em, Kien Svay and Saang districts in Kandal province from touching and climbing 230 kV transmission lines to avoid accidents
