(Phnom Penh): Donating too much blood up to three times a month puts blood donors at risk for leukemia and bone marrow damage over the next 10 years. This is according to Dr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, speaking on the occasion of the spokesperson of the Royal Government, organizing a press conference on "Blood Donation to Save Lives" this morning, August 27, 2020.
The official said that the correct blood donation must be every three months, but the blood donation is not life-threatening. However, in the past, some crooks have tricked people into selling blood on a regular basis, with some donating blood up to three times a month, and some even donating blood. 5 times during 3 months.
The ability to donate in excess of this limit is due to the fact that the donor is impersonating under the guidance of a crook and that the donation is for money. This is according to Dr. Sok Po.
Seeing the impact on life from improper blood donation, officials have instructed people to stop cheating corrupt people and also to give to corrupt people who sell blood as a profession to stop committing such acts. He stressed that the above-mentioned activities are very serious offenses related to the law on the donation of human cells, tissues and organs.
Mr. Sok Po reminded that those who donate blood incorrectly during the bone marrow disease are just waiting for the day of death and chronic pain. In addition, he will need blood to support his health until the day he dies.
In the past, the National Blood Transfusion Center has explained to the people as well as those who take the opportunity to understand the health effects caused by the sale of blood, both health and legal issues. Mr. Sok Po said that according to short figures, there are about 200 to 300 people who have been educated.
