Mr. Em Chanmakara: The Royal Government is encouraging people with disabilities and their families to participate equally in society
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Em Chanmakara, Secretary General of the Disability Action Council, stated that based on the spirit of high responsibility for people with disabilities in Cambodia, the Royal Government has set the vision: "People with disabilities and their families have a good quality of life. And to participate fully and equally in a society with respect for rights and dignity, as well as to provide an environment for disability in all areas and development. ”
He said that the mindset in society is generally the belief or perception that people with disabilities are unfortunate or people who have committed sins from the past, which makes people with disabilities almost never dare to leave. Home or participate in social activities.
The Secretary-General of the Disability Action Council said this on the occasion of his participation in the opening ceremony of the dissemination workshop on the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2019-2023 and the technical standards of physical infrastructure to facilitate people with disabilities on August 26. 2020.
In addition, Mr. Em Chanmakara said that based on the above vision and based on the protection and promotion of the rights of persons with disabilities, the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to launch the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2019-2023, the second phase for Set a vision and a map to continue to move a society towards the elimination of barriers to people with disabilities in line with the global slogan "Make rights a reality".
He said that in order to ensure the effectiveness of this important document, the National Strategic Plan on Disability 2019-2023 was prepared and coordinated by the Disability Action Council and there was extensive consultation between relevant ministries, institutions, development partners, private sector, social organizations. Civilians, organizations with disabilities, non-governmental organizations, especially people with disabilities.
At the same time, Mr. Soy Sokha, Chairman of the Disability Action Team of the Council of Ministers, stated that the rights of persons with disabilities are also protected by national and international law in order to protect their rights and freedoms, protect their interests, prevent, reduce and eliminate discrimination against people. Disability to ensure equal rights of social activity between people with and without disabilities.
