Royal Academy of Cambodia and Ministry of Tourism Sign a Memorandum of Understanding to Help Develop Human Resources in Tourism
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Academy of Cambodia and the Ministry of Tourism have reached the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to increase closer cooperation in the development of human resources in the field of tourism with quality and efficiency. Stated that this work is the first need to strengthen tourism destinations in the country.
The MoU signing ceremony was signed by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Mr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia on the afternoon of August 26, 2020 at the Ministry of Tourism.
Minister Thong Khon said that the MoU focuses on promoting and strengthening cooperation in partnership in promoting vocational training, tourism, human resource development and research in the field of tourism. Develop tourism and turn Cambodia into a world-class tourist destination and provide warmth to tourists visiting Cambodia.
Dr. Sok Touch said that after the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding, the Royal Academy of Cambodia has established cooperation with the Ministry of Tourism on training in hotel, hospitality, food and beverage, as well as the exchange of national and international experts and experts in Public-private sector that can work together to create a vision for tourism for the nation.
Dr. continued that in this cooperation, the Royal Academy of Cambodia plans to establish a China Ready Center to train Chinese language. In addition, the Royal Academy of Cambodia also has cooperation with 23 branches of the Confucius Institute throughout Cambodia.
He said that from now on, Cambodia not only has human resources to meet the needs of domestic tourism, but also can export human resources trained in the country to work abroad.
In a further interview with the media, the President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia expressed his ambition to cooperate with the Ministry of Tourism, the private sector and development partners to develop tourist destinations in the Tonle Sap Lake area, Techo Sen Russey Trep National Park, ecotourism sites in the provinces. Which can provide high security for tourists in recent times.
(Phnom Penh): The Honorary Minister of the Cambodian Red Cross, Ms. Khuon Sodary, Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross, on behalf of the President of the Cambodian Red Cross, Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, on the morning of August 27, 2020 A mobile phone and a generator of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the National Committee for Disaster Management.
The handover ceremony took place after the Cambodian Red Cross received a water purifier, a car and a generator from Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport.
The handover ceremony was held on August 27, 2020 at the Cambodian Red Cross Headquarters under the chairmanship of HE Dr. Khuon Sodary, Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport and Senior Minister. Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said, "The water machine extracted from the natural environment, along with a mobile car and a set of generators, is a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen." "It has been handed over to the Cambodian Red Cross to support humanitarian activities to help people affected by natural disasters such as droughts and floods."
He said that in the event of a flood disaster, the wells could not be used, so fresh water machines extracted from the natural environment would be able to fill the shortage of clean water anytime and anywhere immediately with water pumps, which are modern technology. Automatic production capacity of pure water from the air in the atmosphere of about 800 liters per day with high quality and safety.
Meanwhile, Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Khuon Sodary, Representative of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and on behalf of the Cambodian Red Cross, expressed her great pleasure to receive the donation of pure water machine from the environment, including A mobile car and a generator are very useful in helping people who lack water due to natural disasters.
The Honorable Dr. Khuon Sodary expressed his deepest gratitude to the Cambodian leader Samdech Techo Hun Sen for sponsoring this water purifier to meet the needs of the most vulnerable people in Cambodia. In addition, Samdech Techo always thinks and strives to mobilize with private companies and partner organizations to provide and find all kinds of solutions to meet the needs of clean water to the people.
"Currently, Cambodia is still facing water shortages, but under the strong leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, we will supply clean water to 90% of the people this year," she said. Up to 2023. "
At the same time, Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Khuon Sodary thanked Senior Minister Sun Chanthol for initiating a good idea to find a high quality natural water machine, including a mobile car and a generator, which can help fill the shortage. Of people all the time and everywhere, even in remote areas.
Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Khuon Sodary stated that the Cambodian Red Cross held a handover ceremony to the National Committee for Disaster Management to help the water purifier with 1 atmosphere, 1 mobile car and 1 generator. People in remote villages and communes across the country who lack clean water for future use.
