(Ratanakkiri): Deputy Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, Mr. Lon Sopheap, presented the report that in the first half of 2020, the Northeast Provincial Drug Control Committee has implemented a total of 39 drug offenses. In 29 cases, a total of 106 Cambodian and Vietnamese stakeholders were also arrested.
This statement was made during a meeting to disseminate the results of the first half of the drug control and the implementation direction for the second half of 2020 at the Ratanakkiri Provincial Hall on August 26, 2020 under the chairmanship of General Mak Chito Deputy Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, representing General Santin Bandith Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner.
The provincial governor said that out of 29 cases, 23 cases of trafficking and 6 cases of use were arrested and 106 suspects were arrested, including 15 women, 89 of whom were Cambodian nationals, 11 of whom were female. 17 Vietnamese nationals, 4 females.
Comparing the same period in 2019 and 2020, it was found that the number of crimes of drug trafficking, distribution and use increased by 4 cases equal to 2019, equal to 16% and repression activities increased 14 times more than 2019, equal to 56%.
General Mak Chito praised and appreciated the results of the Provincial Committee, which achieved its results with a high sense of responsibility and received congratulations, support and strong participation from the people.
