(Kampong Thom): Almost every day, Mr. Hak Mong Huot, Governor of Taing Kork District, Kampong Thom Province, always takes the time to visit his local people to see the living conditions as well as to know the needs and additional requests of the people. Citizens are the cause of the people's warmth and happiness.
Along with the activities in the villages, the district governor always brings a small handkerchief to distribute to the people, and if there are people who are affected or have a poor life, he always can afford to support the people. People with disabilities, the elderly, orphans or families with deceased members often receive more or less support from him.
Seeing the activities of the Governor of Hak Mong Huot District become more and more active, a series of local and foreign philanthropists have donated materials and funds to the victims through the respectable District Governor. Love this picture.
On the other hand, most of the activities of Mr. Hak Mong Huot's visit to the people also included the district police inspector and the police officer, the commander and the military police officer, the youth working group, the local aid team, as well as the monks, the chief priest of the pagoda. Preah Mongkul Silavan Lim Vuthy, King of the Honorary Council of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Preah Khet Nureak, Preah Anukon of Taing Kork District, often attended.
Tang Kork residents often observe that no matter how busy they are with administrative work or other work, when they know that there are victims in their locality, Mr. Hak Mong Huot always leads the team to the back of the house. Regardless of the time of day or night.
In fact, on the morning of August 26, 2020, the district governor accompanied by Moni Silvong Ton Pisey, Chief Inspector of Wat Kuho Nokor, as well as Sangkari Nimon to visit and distribute gifts to the grandparents. There are 38 poor elderly people in Pong commune, Tang Kork district.
