(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Cults and Religions has issued guidelines on the organization of the Kan Ben and Pchum Ben festivals and strengthened social security measures to reduce the risk of the spread of Kovid 19 in pagodas throughout Cambodia.
* First: Organize the pagoda in an orderly, hygienic, good environment, put up flags, banners, slogans, slogans and set up public bins.
* Second, cooperate with the competent authorities at the local level to organize security forces for the people who come to perform meritorious deeds at all pagodas.
* Third: Prepare and distribute alms appropriately, avoid some waste and give to the Armed Forces to distribute alms to poor people, orphans and homeless children.
* Fourth: Monitor and inspect pagodas to implement the recommendations of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
* Fifth: Disseminate all educational messages produced by the Ministry of Health widely and regularly in the pagodas and disseminate to the Buddhist public to increase vigilance to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease in the community.
* Sixth: Arrange for a health check-up place before entering the courtyard of a pagoda, temple or hall. Have a thermometer, soap or alcohol to wash your hands regularly. Wear a mask, scarf, towel or cover your mouth when coughing or sneezing and keep a distance of at least one and a half meters from one person to another and follow the rules set by the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health.
