Mr. Chhim Phal Varun, Director of the Secretariat of the Supreme Advisory Council, said in a press conference after the meeting that the issue of the Cambodian-Vietnamese border in Tbong Khmum province was raised by the heads of delegations of some political parties. The arrests of Rong Chhun and Suong Sophorn in connection with the border issue are also mentioned.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized in response to the remarks made by the head of the delegation of the political party, a member of the Supreme Advisory Council, that the debate, the pain and the visit to the border was a good thing and not a bad thing. Illegal. But taking the border issue to provoke an event is not something that can be mentioned.
The border issue between Cambodia and Vietnam has resurfaced after Cambodia adopted a 1 / 25,000 scale map that has just been published. The 1 / 25,000 scale map is the map that defines the border demarcation between Cambodia and Vietnam, which is about 84% agreed.
Mr. Rong Chhun and Mr. Suong Sophorn arrived in Tbong Khmum province and met with some people. The villagers claim they have lost land in the border area. Based on the claims of the people, Mr. Rong Chhun and Mr. Suong Sophorn made statements and comments accusing the Royal Government of losing territory.
After issuing the statement and commenting, Mr. Rong Chhun and Mr. Suong Sophorn were arrested and charged with "inciting serious social unrest."
In this morning's meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also instructed Senior Minister Var Kimhong, Chairman of the Joint Border Affairs Committee, to go to the place where the people claimed the land was missing to find out the truth and end all doubts.
In addition, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced to open a forum to explain to people who have questions or want to know about this border issue.
In front of the members of the Supreme Advisory Council from 16 political parties who went to the polls in 2018 this morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also explained some of the difficulties in negotiating border affairs with neighboring countries. Side. In that, the provision in the Cambodian Constitution on border issues with neighboring countries is also a shortcoming of Cambodia. This is according to Mr. Chhim Phal Varun.
This special social assistance program was officially launched on June 24, 2020 under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to help address the livelihoods of poor and vulnerable families affected by Kovid. 19 Equitable cards include those who lose their jobs or their income, which puts them in poverty.
The second round of cash support program (August and September 2020) that starts on Tuesday, August 25, 2020 through the use of the Wing money transfer service will provide $ 30 million in cash from the national budget. To more than 2.6 million people for this August.
According to the Ministry of Economy, this amount increased from 26 million US dollars in July and 23 million US dollars in June due to the increase of poor households through the identification of about 60,000 households. Add.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 117 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to August 25, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 149,188 vehicles, including 110,589 motorcycles and 38,599 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 117 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for August 25, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 9 times, in which 1 person died, 13 people were injured (8 seriously injured).
The 80-year-old politician's sweet words of praise were uttered at a meeting of the Supreme Advisory Council at the Peace Palace this morning, August 25, 2020, to summarize the work of the fourth semester. The meeting was also attended by representatives of 16 non-governmental parties who are members of the Supreme Advisory Council.
During the meeting, Mr. Mam Sonando, who participated in anti-government demonstrations with Mr. Sam Rainsy and Mr. Kem Sokha in 2013 and 2014, had some comments, in which he praised Samdech Techo Hun Sen for his efforts to build the border line and build Long lasting peace that no leader can replace.
In the last term, Mr. Mam Sonando saw that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has achieved some success, especially on border work. He claimed that the previous generation of leaders since the former King Lon Nol and Pol Pot led the country is not as good as Samdech.
He added: "We know the history related to the leadership of former King Norodom Sihanouk to General Lon Nol to Pol Pot to this day, we see that Samdech is a great leader, we have peace and this peace is very strong. "For the benefit of the nation."
The Royal Government of Cambodia has strived to resolve border issues with neighboring countries peacefully in order to build a peaceful and prosperous border area with the expansion of mutual trade relations. About 84 percent of the Cambodia-Vietnam border demarcation has been completed so far, with both sides committed to continuing to demarcate the remaining border.
With this achievement of the border post, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc, Prime Minister of Vietnam, on October 5, 2019, signed an agreement to recognize the two countries' border posts, which achieved 84%. The signing of the border post of the two countries is another new historical event for Cambodia and Vietnam.
Separately, on August 1, 2020, Cambodia and Vietnam also held a ceremony to hand over and receive a 125,000 scale land border map, which is a modern digital map that is easy to see the border line.
However, recently, Mr. Rong Chhun and Mr. Suong Sophorn went to incite and inspire people to protest the re-establishment of the border post in Tbong Khmum province. They were both arrested and remanded in custody on charges of "inciting serious social security unrest" and inciting Suong Sophorn to incite chaos and incitement. Insecurity to society as well.
For Mam Sonando, the border issue between Cambodia and Vietnam can only be resolved peacefully, not violently. He believes that if there is violence on the border, those who are in danger are the people living along the border. Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works Announces Restrictions on Issuance of Letters for Domestic Road Transport Vehicles
(Preah Vihear): The Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province has issued a notification on the restriction of the issuance of letters to vehicles for road transport business in the country. This is according to the announcement that Fresh News received on August 25, 2020.
* First, for vehicles transporting goods and passengers that do not have the mark or the mark is not in accordance with the set technical standards, it requires the vehicle owner or legal representative to take the vehicle to prepare and seal. Mark correctly according to the set standards (please attach the appendix of Prakas No. 038 PRK with).
* Second: In case the vehicle owner does not follow the above instructions to close the designated mark, the vehicle is not allowed to carry out the transport business.
The Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province sincerely hopes that all branch owners, freight forwarders or passengers who own vehicles will cooperate and implement this notice effectively from the date of signing. .
