The Capital-Provincial Secretariat of the 25th Provincial Election Organizes a Meeting with Stakeholders on the Provision of Invitations to the Finalists of the 2019 Voter List (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): As of August 24, 2020 The 25 Elections (CEC) held a meeting with the authorities of the Capital, Provinces and Municipalities, Districts and Khans on the issuance of invitations to the final voter list in 2019.
Mr. Som Soreida, Deputy Secretary General of the NEC, stated that the meeting was to promote the work and request the cooperation of local authorities to provide support to commune councils, village chiefs, political parties and non-governmental organizations. To implement the issuance of invitations by name and voter data contained in the invitations in the relevant communes / sangkats to reach all stakeholders.
He added that the purpose of issuing the invitation is to inform the people whose names are on the voter list as follows:
* Citizens whose names are on the last voter list in 2019 who have used an expired Khmer Nationality Identity Card (OAK) or identification documents used to register to vote (EE) in the previous voter registration must be checked. Verify and update the data in the voter list according to the new category during the review of the voter list and voter registration in 2020.
* Citizens whose names are on the last voter list in 2019 and who have used the new type of AK in the previous voter registration must verify their names and data in the voter list by voter invitation letter, if any. Inaccurate records must be corrected during the 2020 voter list review and registration.
According to the action plan, the invitation will be given from September 1 to 30, 2020. Commune / Sangkat councils and village chiefs, as well as stakeholders involved in the distribution of invitations to people in villages in the commune / sangkat. Minister Ouk Rabun Tells Australian Ambassador to Cambodia Strategic Rural Development Plan and Requests Further Support
The Minister expressed his warm welcome to the new Ambassador on his diplomatic mission in Cambodia and welcomed his full cooperation in contributing to the further development and deepening of bilateral ties.
At the same time, the Minister thanked the Australian Government for its participation and support for the development of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
It should be noted that the Australian Government has contributed significantly to the economic and social development of Cambodia through various official assistance in areas such as trade, agriculture, rural development, health infrastructure, and demining assistance.
The Minister informed about the Strategic Plan for Rural Development 2019-2023, focusing on strengthening institutions and capacity building of civil servants, improving the living conditions of rural communities, promoting rural economic activities and developing transportation infrastructure by improving roads. In rural areas, gradually from red gravel roads to DBST paved roads and concrete roads to vulnerable areas.
In response, the Ambassador expressed his pleasure at completing his diplomatic mission in Cambodia and praised the good cooperation between the two countries in all fields.
The Ambassador also mentioned the provision of assistance in the field of demining and will continue to contribute to Cambodia achieving its goal of becoming a mine-free country by 2025.
The Minister also asked the Australian Government to continue its support.
In response, the Ambassador praised the good cooperation between the two countries in all fields. Join the elimination of drugs for the future of our children! Nationwide drug crackdown for August 25: 26 cases cracked, 51 arrested
