Senior Minister Sun Chanthol urges joint officials to make Cambodia a logistics hub and a warehouse for neighboring countries
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, urged experts of the Ministry to participate in the opinion to turn Cambodia into a logistics center and a warehouse of neighboring countries, because Cambodia is in a geographical location. There is a favorable location in the region and a shipping port from Thailand-Cambodia-Vietnam and from Vietnam-Cambodia-Thailand.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol made this statement on August 25, 2020, when he chaired the first meeting of the working group to address the challenges at the Cambodia-Vietnam and Cambodia-Thailand border crossings. With the participation of ministry leaders and stakeholders at the Ministry of Public Works.
The meeting was held to review the 78 action plans prepared by the working group and to gather additional input to ensure that the action plan is comprehensive, effective, and serves the common good.
During the meeting, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol mentioned the project to build, expand and improve the quality and modernize the transport infrastructure of land, rail and waterways to promote and enhance the Cambodian logistics sector to be better and more competitive with Regional countries.
The senior minister said the ministry was working with the Thai side to temporarily allow trucks to pass through the Stung Bat-Ban Nong Ian border crossing to reduce traffic congestion at the Poipet international border crossing and was working with the Vietnamese side. To solve traffic congestion at the Bavet-Mok Bai border.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also commended the working group for the work and stakeholders who cooperated well in preparing this action plan and instructed the working group to take all the inputs from this meeting to revise the action plan. Improve and plan action plans for the short, medium and long term, especially the emergency action plan to be implemented later this year in collaboration with relevant institutions.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also instructed the working group on its second meeting to review these action plans in detail before submitting them to Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance. Decided. Chamkarmon District Governor Inspects COVID-19 Prevention Measures at Aeon Market
(Phnom Penh): Considering the safety and effectiveness of COVID-19 disease prevention measures for people who enter Aeon Mall Branch 1 at the call of the Royal Government on Tuesday afternoon, August 25, 2020, Chamkarmon District Administration led by Mr. Theng Sothol, Governor of Chamkar Mon District, inspected the measures to prevent and prevent Kovid-19 disease in Aeon Mall, located along Samdech Sothearos Blvd., Village 8, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
During the inspection, the team observed that the market was well managed in accordance with the rules of the Ministry of Health, with about 14 entrances and exits of the market, staffed with alcohol spray. Heat meter, heat scanner, computer system at all entrances.
At the same time, the Governor of Chamkar Mon District also advised the managers and supervisors to pay more attention to the staff in the market, especially the vendors in the market to be more careful about the rules that the market has put in place. Like alcohol, wash your hands before entering a store or grocery store.
The district governor urged market managers to tell customers or customers not to gather in large numbers to prevent the spread or spread of this new type of respiratory disease in Cambodia. The head of the Royal Government has announced a fight to prevent the spread of this disease for the safety of the people.
