This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen convened a meeting to review the work of the fourth half of the Supreme Advisory Council.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Tuesday morning, August 25, 2020, presided over the meeting to review the work of the fourth half of the Supreme Advisory Council.
According to the press release of the Supreme Advisory Council, in today's meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will express the interest and concept of the contribution of the Supreme Advisory Council for 24 months. Ago.
In this meeting, the heads of delegations of member political parties will be allowed to give constructive ideas on the context of the current social situation based on the discovery of clues and evidence through additional work missions with the challenge. Kovid 19 also.
Mr. Chhim Phal Varun, Director of the Secretariat of the Supreme Advisory Council, told Fresh News that in the fourth half of this year, the Supreme Advisory Council has been actively studying issues in society and the people. Submit to the Royal Government for review and find a solution.
It should be noted that the Supreme Advisory Council was established by Royal Decree dated September 6, 2018 at the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen after the 6th National Election. The Supreme Advisory Council is composed of 16 of the 20 political parties that participated in the 2018 national election.
The Supreme Advisory Council has the role of advising the Royal Government outside the parliamentary framework in order to improve work efficiency for the benefit of the people and the potential for social development.
Over the past three semesters, the Supreme Advisory Council has said that during its 16-month mission, it has visited more than 400 missions across 25 capitals and provinces and made reports accompanied by evidence on the issue. The collections were submitted to Samdech Techo Hun Sen in nearly 200 cases. In nearly 200 reports, the Supreme Advisory Council received 32 responses from Samdech Techo.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen, during the closing ceremony of the Supreme Advisory Council in early 2020, expressed his great satisfaction with the work of the Supreme Advisory Council. Samdech Techo said that the Supreme Advisory Council has done better than the opposition MPs in the previous term.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned that the Supreme Advisory Council has made a significant contribution to social reform and finding out the truth about social irregularities. Samdech Techo noted that without the Supreme Advisory Council, some reports would not have fallen into Samdech's hands.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen encouraged all members of the Supreme Advisory Council to continue their efforts to participate in improving society, eliminating corruption and inactivity.
