A large Chinese company is ready to invest in the agricultural sector in Cambodia by collecting fresh fruits, processing and exporting to China
(Phnom Penh): Another large Chinese company, Thien Thien, has announced plans to invest in Cambodia's agricultural sector, which will procure fresh fruits grown in Cambodia for processing, packaging and export. China.
Regarding this investment project, Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his full support, stating that this investment project is in line with the agricultural development plan of the Ministry of Agriculture of Cambodia to boost local agricultural production through agricultural modernization. Processing, packaging and export, all of which will boost the national economy.
In order for the project to be successful, Director-General Wang also sought advice and recommendations from Minister Veng Sakhon and officials related to the procurement market and procedures for exporting the above products to China.
In response, the Minister instructed the company to cooperate with the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, the General Department of Agriculture, the Department of International Cooperation and the Department of Agro-Industry to learn more about the potential of the above fruit trees and prepare a memorandum of understanding with the Ministry for the Ministry. Ability to facilitate contract farming with the community and, in particular, export procedures.
According to Veng Sakhon, the government of the People's Republic of China and the Chinese people have always provided excellent cooperation in all fields with Cambodia, especially in the field of agriculture. So far, the Chinese side has increased the volume of Cambodian rice imports to 500,000 tons and recently allowed Cambodia to export yellow bananas and fresh mangoes directly to China.
British researchers find incredible loss of ice on Earth
The study found that the planet lost 28 trillion tons of ice in just 23 years. This could cause sea levels to rise sharply, possibly to 1 meter by the end of the century. Rising sea levels mean that tens of millions of people living in lowland areas around the world will face the loss of their land due to floods.
Not only that, the massive loss of ice on Earth could also have other serious consequences, including damage to marine biodiversity in the Arctic and Antarctic, as well as a weakening of our planet's capacity. Pushing radioactive material from the sun back into space as well.
The cause of the melting of the glacier is nothing but global warming due to greenhouse gas emissions and booming industries, as well as deforestation and the destruction of the natural environment of humans. This planet.
