(Battambang): Based on the principles of in-depth reform in the field of post, telecommunication, information and communication technology, Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, has paid great attention to human resource development at both the national and sub-national levels.
In particular, in order to enable the sub-national level to carry out its work more effectively, under the initiative of the Minister, the Ministry of Post and Telecommunications has organized a workshop on capacity building at the Department of Posts and Telecommunications, which is the intended training course. :
The workshop was organized for post offices and telecommunications in 24 provinces across the country, divided into four regions, and each region was convened from the director level to offices from six provincial post and telecommunications departments.
The training process is conducted with the participation of teachers, leaders and civil servants who have skills and work experience related to each topic.
Training methods include: presentations, questions / answers, discussions, group exercises, sharing experiences, monitoring and understanding of participants' lessons, as well as taking feedback from participants on a daily basis.
The leaders of the Ministry, four Secretaries of State, approve the content of the lesson. The Secretary of State and the Under-Secretary of State for Regional Leaders will conduct quality inspections of the workshop and evaluate participants' participation on a daily basis.
The facilitator organizes the cost planning, selects the venue, conducts the workshop, invites the participants to attend and summarizes the daily report to the regional chairperson.
In fact, the first workshop was held in two areas from the morning of 10 to 14 August 2020 for 5 days in Battambang under the chairmanship of Mr. Kay Khun Heng, Secretary of State, Representative Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications in Opening-closing ceremony.
As well as leading the team to encourage the process of the workshop, which conducted training on 22 topics to provide a basis for solving real challenges to 53 participants (24 females) from the Provincial Department of Posts and Telecommunications. 6 in area 2 and 3 from 3 provincial post and telecommunication departments (outside area 2).
By completing the evaluation questionnaire in the process of the workshop in these two areas, almost all the participants expressed their satisfaction with the whole workshop process and requested to continue to organize such workshops more often to provide opportunities. All civil servants participated in the study to gain more understanding and help promote effective work performance.
Overall, the results obtained in this workshop are very important for the Ministry's leadership to know and re-establish the vision to train officials to be more high quality, professional, clear and key. To help solve challenges in performing work at the sub-national level.
In order to encourage the regular attendance of the trainees, the leaders and officials from the Provincial Department of Public Works in Area 2, Battambang City, the delegation also handed out certificates. Study to all 53 participants as a souvenir on the closing day of the workshop.
Please be informed that after the event is held in Zone 2, the workshop will continue as planned in Zone 1, Zone 3 and end in Zone 4.
