Spokesman for the General Commission: On August 23, another 886 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 115 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to August 23, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 147,118 vehicles, including 1090,064 motorcycles and 33,8054 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun said that for the past 115 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
