2 killed, 5 injured in car accident in Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): At least two people were killed instantly at the scene and five others were seriously injured in a car accident in Preah Vihear province on the evening of August 23, 2020.
Lieutenant Colonel Rith Souna, Tbeng Meanchey District Police Inspector, said that before the accident, the car was carrying eight family members from Preah Vihear province to Kulen district. Speeding overtook the car in front due to the high speed, took the steering wheel too much and fell on the road, causing it to overturn on its own, causing two deaths and five minor injuries.
Tbeng Meanchey District Inspector added that after the incident, the police arrived at the scene and contacted the ambulance of the Provincial Police to transport the injured to the Provincial Referral Hospital, while the body was handed over to the family. The festival is traditional and the car is towed to the district police station.
