Woman sues O'Smach International Immigration Police for kidnapping 400 baht in exchange for allowing two chickens to be raised
(Oddar Meanchey): An O'Smach International Immigration Police officer, Lieutenant Colonel Sean Vanna, was sued by a woman living in O'Smach Sangkat for extorting 400 baht in exchange for not catching two chickens. The head that the plaintiff bought from Thailand to raise as a family.
The plaintiff, 55-year-old Chhum Samnang, a resident of O'Smach commune, described this morning, August 23, 2020, that on August 20, 2020, she gave an acquaintance who was driving a truck. Ice from Thailand helped him buy two chickens to raise at home, because the Kovid-19 era did not know what to do, so he found it easier to raise animals at home.
The same woman said that when she arrived at the O'Smach international gate at 9 am on the same day, Lt. Gen. Sean Vannara did not allow the two chickens to be brought in.
The police officer even demanded 400 baht in exchange for not confiscating the two chickens. Due to his refusal, the person he sent to buy the chicken paid the police officer 400 baht as required.
Due to the actions of the immigration police officers at O'Smach International Port, the same woman decided to file a complaint to the General Department of Immigration today without fear. He said that the immigration police at Osmach International Port often abused the weak people, sometimes there were arguments about taking money from people to buy food from Thailand on motorbikes.
