Cambodia, Japan show stance on expanding economic, trade and investment cooperation (Video inside) Kovid 19 brought another high level of commitment between Cambodia and Japan to strengthen relations and cooperation in various fields between the two countries.
Motigito Shimitsu has become the first foreign minister and senior official of a friendly country to visit Cambodia in 2020. The Japanese diplomat's visit is considered one of the most valued as a strategic partner, as Cambodia and Japan are both struggling with the Kovid 19 crisis.
During his first visit as Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan, Mr. Motigito Shimitsu was warmly and warmly welcomed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon. Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on August 22, 2020 yesterday.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during his visit, Mr. Motigito Simitse congratulated the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the strong and progressive socio-economic progress of Cambodia. Successful transmission of Kovid-19 disease in Cambodia.
He also expressed his deep appreciation for the progress of bilateral relations and cooperation as a strategic partner, and agreed to further enhance this relationship and cooperation.
Economic recovery between Cambodia and Japan was also an important discussion in both the meeting between Motigito Simitsu and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as with Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon.
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, in order to further promote cooperation and economic activities between the two countries affected by Kovid-19, Cambodia and Japan have agreed to reopen in stages and gradually. Boundaries between Cambodia and Japan for travelers to work and do business with strict adherence to epidemic prevention measures.
The two sides will work with their respective authorities to start cross-border travel for more than 14 days of "gateway to accommodation" in early September 2020 and expedite talks on transit practices. Domains for stays shorter than 14 days "Port for business".
During his current visit to Cambodia, Motigito Simitsu also focused on strengthening economic, trade and investment cooperation.
In a press release on the results of the current visit of the Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia, it was emphasized that Japan and Cambodia have expressed a common desire to strengthen and expand cooperation in all fields, especially economic, trade and investment cooperation. Tourism, health, education and culture.
Japan has also expressed its willingness to support Cambodia's efforts to build the capacity of the agro-processing industry and the high-tech industry, and to expand cooperation in the preservation of ancient temples in Cambodia.
Cambodia also expressed its appreciation for the cultural and educational communication promotion activities of the Asia Foundation Liaison Office of the Japan Foundation in Phnom Penh and welcomed its continued presence in Cambodia.
In order to promote the growth of economic relations and cooperation, Cambodia and Japan also discussed the implementation process of major projects in Cambodia, including the development of Sihanoukville Port, the new container port in Sihanoukville and National Road 5, which will contribute To expand investment activities and increase trade volume between the two countries, while Cambodia is committed to further efforts to improve the business and investment environment even better.
In addition, Motigi reaffirmed Japan's commitment to continue to support the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to promote the democratic process, improve the lives of its people and develop Cambodia in all areas.
