The former president was the first black Democrat senator in U.S. history. He led this great country for two consecutive terms, the first term from 2009 to 2013 and the second term from 2013 to 2017 because of his good leadership ability. What are Obama's daily routines?
Obama spends between five and seven hours sleeping each night as he wakes up at seven in the morning. When he wakes up, he exercises for about 45 minutes, and he usually exercises six days a week.
Every evening, Obama meets with colleagues to complete his day-to-day work. His commendation is that if there is too much work in the country and it is complicated, Obama will always find a way to finish it and be willing to sacrifice some time and daily routines such as dinner with family, exercise and Other personal work.
