Germany, Britain and France issue joint statement "reject the resumption of US-imposed sanctions on Iran"! (Video inside) (London): Britain, France and Germany issued a joint statement on Thursday this week that they do not support the United States to continue to impose sanctions on Iran. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Friday morning, August 21, 2020.
The United Kingdom, France and the Federal Republic of Germany have reaffirmed their commitment to safeguarding international institutions that are fundamental to multilateralism and to uphold the powers of the United Nations Security Council (UNSC). Avoid any actions that could cause deep divisions within the Security Council.
The Iran nuclear deal was signed by Britain, China, France, Germany, Russia and the United States in July 2015. However, under Donald Trump, the United States withdrew from the agreement on May 8, 2018 and unilaterally imposed further sanctions on Tehran, despite opposition from the international community.
