(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Japan, Mr. Mito Gito Shimizu, praised the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, for putting in place effective measures to combat and control the spread of Kovid 19.
The Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan expressed this appreciation through his message to the people of Cambodia this morning, August 21, 2020.
As of 7 a.m. on August 21, 2020, Cambodia had identified a total of 273 cases of 19 Kovid 19 cases. There are a total of 259 healers nationwide and 14 in-patients. The rate of infection is assessed as a good situation for Cambodia compared to the momentum of the acute epidemic.
In a message to Cambodians before arriving in Cambodia on the evening of August 21, 2020, the Japanese diplomat also expressed interest in the status of Kovid 19. He said the disease was a challenge for the international community today. The Japanese diplomat also praised Cambodia for putting in place effective and effective measures to combat the disease.
"The international community is facing a global epidemic of 19 cases of Kovid," said Motiguito Simitsu. "I commend Cambodia for controlling this epidemic through the efforts of stakeholders under the leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen and the cooperation of the people."
In the private sector, Japanese companies are collaborating to provide educational apps and online learning programs, as well as Japanese NGOs are promoting measures to prevent infections as well as supporting children who are unable to attend school due to closure. School. At the same time, a number of Japanese doctors traveled to Cambodia to perform emergency surgery and medical treatment for Cambodians.
These measures on the 19 Kuwait measures have also strengthened relations between the two countries. To further strengthen this relationship, Japan will continue to hold talks with the Royal Government of Cambodia to reopen people-to-people exchanges in the business sector in a manner appropriate to preventing the re-emergence of the Kovid 19.
Mote Gito Shimizu also expressed his desire to promote solidarity towards economic recovery and development after the end of the 19 Kovid spread.
Please be informed that Mr. Motigito Shimitsu will arrive in Cambodia on the evening of August 21, 2020 to pay his first official visit to Cambodia as the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan for 3 days, starting from the 21st. Until August 23. During the visit, the Japanese diplomat will pay a courtesy call and discuss with Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the morning of August 22.
