Readers, please find out the general knowledge about 11 species of animals that have the longest life, including 1 species that has immortality as follows:
Greenland sharks, or gray sharks, can live up to 272 years, with some claiming a maximum lifespan of 392 years. However, the Greenland Shark is considered an endangered species due to a significant decrease in the number of sharks.
The Chiodak, a seaweed, has lived for more than 165 years. This species grows very fast immediately after birth, averaging 1 inch per year during the first four years.
This species lives between 170 and 250 years. The lamellae prachilla is unique among similar species because it grows slowly throughout life to over 6 feet in length.
Red Sea animals can live from 100 to 200 years. They are found only in the Pacific Ocean, especially along the west coast of North America and the northern coast of Japan, and they live in shallow water and some in rock formations.
The squid is a home decoration fish and is considered a freshwater fish with unusual properties. They have a life cycle of about 40 years, while the oldest squid live up to 200 years.
Kohok oysters are livestock that can live for 200 years, but their average life cycle is only 100 years.
Antarctic crows live at depths of about 325 to 6,500 feet and in extremely cold water. These species grow very slowly, while the processes in the body are also very slow, which makes them live longer.
