APSARA Authority repairs and restores the old drainage system on the west bridge of Angkor Wat
(Siem Reap): In order to save the structure of the bridge on the west side of Angkor Wat so that the rocks do not break easily due to flooding during the rainy season, the Water Management Department of APSARA Authority has repaired and restored the old drainage system on The bridge was reopened. The drainage system was designed by the French during the renovation of the bridge in the past, but did not leave a detailed technical plan.
Technicians claim that the main cause of the congestion is due to debris, plastic debris and sealed soil. Therefore, in order for the drainage system to work again, the technicians cleaned a total of seven drainage holes.
Ministry of Justice Spokesperson: NGO Statement Requesting Rong Chhun's Release has No Influence on Cambodian Courts as an Independent Institution
(Phnom Penh): Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Justice, Mr. Chin Malin, on August 19, 2020, stated that the statement of some NGOs demanding the release of Mr. Rong Chhun has no effect on the Cambodian court. As an independent institution.
Mr. Malin's remarks came after a number of NGOs issued a joint statement on August 18, 2020, demanding that the government release Rong Chhun and other illegal protesters. Authorities arrested.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Justice stated: "The judiciary is an independent body and no individual or international group can put pressure and order on the court. Issuing pressure statements and demanding that the court release the accused and drop the charges is not a legitimate means of protecting the accused and will not affect the court's decision. Independent institutions.
In addition, senior officials of the Ministry of Justice also presented some points of knowledge for young people about the law and the implementation of the right to freedom of assembly, protest and expression in response to the vague and baseless statements of a group of civil society organizations. That includes:
* The Constitution states that citizens have the right to freedom of assembly, expression and protest, but also states that the exercise of these rights shall be determined by law. Therefore, we need to look at the Constitution, not just one part, including the relevant laws, in order to know which actions are the exercise of rights and which are violations of the law that can lead to legal liability. One eventually.
* Expressing concerns about border issues is an exercise in the right to freedom of expression, but instead exaggerates and distorts false information about border issues with malicious intent, inciting unrest, and undermining national security. It is an exercise of rights, but a criminal offense for which the perpetrator is legally liable.
* The border issue is a sensitive and complex issue, and exaggeration and misrepresentation of this border issue could lead to serious harm to the nation, especially to national security and diplomatic relations with neighboring countries. Prevention and repression must be very strict to protect the peace of the nation.
* Boundary resolution should be done by experienced professionals, research and knowledge of border issues, rather than by unscrupulous activists and political traders.
On July 31, 2020, Mr. Rong Chhun was arrested in connection with the distortion of facts on the border issue, which is a clear crime, incitement to cause serious disturbance to social security under Article 495 of the Penal Code. Kingdom of Cambodia. He was remanded in custody pending further proceedings.
