ISO is the largest organization for the development and release of many international standards around the world. These standards are very important to apply to the management of the production, service and quality of each business.
As each company around the world adheres to the same common standards, the techniques of business management, production management, as well as the quality of products and services are all set to international standards. To date, ISO has released more than 22,000 standards, members from more than 160 countries, and a technical committee for the development of at least 800 standards.
Philippines bans import of poultry and eggs from Australia after H7N7 bird flu outbreak
The Philippines on Wednesday decided to temporarily ban the import of poultry and eggs from Australia after the H7N7 bird flu virus was found on a farm in Australia. Recently. This is according to the release by CNA on Wednesday afternoon, August 19, 2020.
Australia, which supplies less than 1 percent of the Philippines' bamboo imports, confirmed an outbreak of bird flu at a poultry farm in Victoria in late July.
In a statement issued Wednesday, the Philippine Ministry of Agriculture issued a temporary ban on the import of poultry and eggs from Australia.
However, Agriculture Minister William Dar emphasized that all exports from Australia with import permits before August 6 would be allowed to enter the country normally if the birds were caught. Sample before July 3 or 21 days before the outbreak.
