(Pursat): The criminal force of the Veal Veng District Police Inspectorate arrested a suspect after deliberately using violence to attempt to kill his father. The suspect was arrested on August 16, 2020 at the entrance to Boeung Romlech in Samlanh village, Krapeu Pi commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
Colonel Theang Veng, police inspector of Veal Veng district, said that the suspect involved in the case of beheading was Sakun Chandara, a 31-year-old Cambodian man. His father, Prohm Sakun, is a 67-year-old Cambodian man living in Samlanh village, Krapeu Pi commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
The father was slightly injured when the suspect cut his son with a knife.
Sources said that the suspect, Sakun Chandara, was arrested and interrogated by the police before the story broke that he had a warrant for his involvement in the murder of his brother-in-law in Siem Reap a year ago.
