Former Youth Volunteers Join the Army on September 25, 1986 to pay tribute to the late Mr. Heng Chung, Customs Officer of Preah Sihanouk Province
(Phnom Penh): A group of former youth volunteers enlisted in the army on September 25, 1986 to pay tribute to the late Mr. Un Phirum alias Heng Dong, Customs and Excise Officer of Customs Branch and Sihanoukville International Port Authority.
A group of former youth volunteers considers Un Phirum's death to be the loss of a great ally, the loss of a son, the loss of a brother, the loss of a husband and the loss of a beloved and respected father. Too late to find no.
Mr. Un Phirum passed away at the age of 53 on the night of Thursday, August 13, 2020 while working in Sihanoukville due to a heart attack.
After the high school exam in 1986, Un Phirum, alias Heng Dong, volunteered to join the army on September 25, 1986 in Phnom Penh and to train at the 50 E "Training School.
After six months of training, Un Phirum alias Heng Dong was sent by the Ministry of Defense to the F196 front.
Later, from 1987 to 1992, Ou Phirum alias Heng Dong was sent by the Ministry of Defense to study in Russia for five years as a tank commander.
