Samdech Techo Hun Sen Resolves Not to Postpone the Transfiguration of the Blue Hat Army After Receiving a Clear Transition Time from the United Nations
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has re-decided not to ask for a delay in the transfer of the Blue Hat Army after Samdech received a clear time to change, which makes it easier for Cambodia to prepare for the transact. Kovid's disease 19.
At the inauguration of the "Garden City" water park on August 16, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that he had asked the United Nations to delay the transfer of Cambodian Blue Hat forces to avoid Outbreaks of Kovid 19.
But on the morning of August 17, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced a new decision without asking for an extension. Samdech Techo stated, "After receiving the specific time of return and exchange of Cambodian Blue Hat troops organized by the United Nations. "This morning, I have decided not to postpone the return of the Cambodian Blue Hat Army and to send a replacement Blue Hat Army."
Samdech Techo stated that the organization of the United Nations has given this makes it easier for Cambodia to organize the Talisman. Samdech Techo added that the Cambodian Blue Hat troops who will be transferred back to Cambodia include: from Mali in September 2020, from South Sudan in October 2020, from Central Africa in November. 2020 and return from Lebanon in January 2021.
Taking this opportunity, Samdech Techo also called on officers, deputies and soldiers who are in the above four countries to prepare to return to Cambodia. Samdech Techo also asked the officers, deputies and soldiers who will be replaced to prepare to leave under the arrangement of the Ministry of National Defense and the United Nations.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized in his writings that he expressed Cambodia's strong position that although Cambodia was a poor country and was facing 19 more Kovit, the country where the Cambodian Blue Hat army had to go was under attack by 19 Kovit. The Cambodian government and its military have not relinquished their duty to participate in peacekeeping in countries under the auspices of the United Nations.
Samdech Techo further stated that this mission is for Cambodia to participate voluntarily and responsibly as a member of the United Nations.
