Speaking at the inauguration of "Garden City" water park by Tycoon Ly Yong Phat in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh this morning, August 16, 2020, Samdech Techo confirmed that on Friday in the Council of Ministers. Samdech has instructed Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, to contact the Secretary-General of the United Nations to delay the transfer of Blue Hat forces.
According to a report by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon yesterday, Cambodia's Permanent Representative to the United Nations met with the UN Under-Secretary-General for Peacekeeping Forces. Delaying the transfer of peacekeepers, as more than 400 troops may be transferred in the future, so the risk of importing 19 Kovid from abroad remains high.
Cambodia has a total of 678 peacekeepers carrying out humanitarian missions in four countries, including Mali, South Sudan, Central Africa and Lebanon. This was confirmed by Ms. Malinda, a spokeswoman for the Center for Peacekeeping Forces.
