(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on Sunday morning, August 16, 2020, visited and inaugurated “Garden City” water park of Tycoon Ly Yong Phat in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
"Garden City" is the first large water park in Cambodia to be built in the development area of Tycoon Ly Yong Phat, a satellite development area northeast of Phnom Penh. According to the company report, "Garden City" water park has a total investment of more than 44 million US dollars.
The water park was built on an area of more than 8 hectares, starting construction on May 28, 2018 and completed in July 2020.
Garden City Water Park has 38 modern and high quality entertainment equipment imported from the United States and the European Union. These toys are designed for people of all ages, including children, teenagers, teenagers and the elderly.
In addition to the swimming pool, there is also a restaurant in the park that serves Khmer, French and Khmer food.
Phnom Penh, after the liberation from the genocidal regime on January 7, 1979, was named the Ghost City. After the liberation of the capital, which was left from the ashes of the war, very few people came to live.
But now, more than 40 years after the liberation, Phnom Penh has become a center of economy, culture, tourism and living. Phnom Penh, which used to be under the dark veil, has been transformed into a high-rise residential and commercial building and many entertainment areas.
Under the shadow of peace, Phnom Penh has developed and grown strongly and is also ranked as a modern capital in the region. Currently, the area of Phnom Penh has been expanded from more than 300 square kilometers from the past to nearly 700 kilometers today.
The presence of "Garden City" water park is another achievement of new development for Phnom Penh under the shadow of peace. The presence of "Garden City" water park creates a place of entertainment, brings happiness for the people of Phnom Penh, in particular, and for people from all over the world in general.
In addition, the presence of "Garden City" water park is also a contribution to attract tourists to visit in Cambodia.
Please note that in the development area of Tycoon Ly Yong Phat, Prey Treng land from the past, now has become a satellite city of Phnom Penh. In addition to the new water park, the area also has a large zoo called Safari Zoo, a hotel, a golf course and a large national stadium under construction.
