(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, on the afternoon of August 15, 2020, led a working group to inspect the results of the construction of the river bank in Pong Lech village, Pong commune, Koh Sotin district, Kampong Cham province.
According to the administration of Kampong Cham Provincial Hall, the river area in the above commune village always suffers from landslides every year due to floods. However, after the inspection of Mr. Un Chanda, the Governor of Kampong Cham Province, he initiated the idea of building concrete blocks to prevent further landslides.
The same source continued that as a result, after the provincial governor led the professional officers to inspect the e-mail, the construction of this river bank has so far been 80% completed.
At the same time, the provincial governor advised to continue to plant flowers as an ornamental garden along the river bank in order for people to use this area as a recreation area to be able to come and exercise here as well.
