The handing over ceremony was attended by Mr. Chan Lumphat, Deputy Chairman of the Disaster Management Committee, on behalf of Senior Minister Kun Kim, Chairman of the Disaster Management Committee, and Ms. Chak Heng, Deputy Governor, on behalf of Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province. Peng Trida, Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Ros Heng, District Governor and other relevant officials.
Mr. Peng Trida said that despite the continuous rain in Preah Vihear province, the rainfall distribution was not equal in all communes. This August. These factors affect and damage a small number of seedlings and irrigated fields caused by slow, unseasonal rainfall.
According to the report, the National Committee for Disaster Management, in collaboration with the Preah Vihear Provincial Administration and the Department of Agriculture, Department of Water Resources, district authorities and relevant offices, conducted a field assessment of the effects of drought on two communes. There are 2 villages in Tasou commune and 3 villages in Saang commune. The rice seed offered now is 1,000 baht, equivalent to 25,000 kilograms.
On this occasion, Mr. Chan Lumphat and Ms. Chak Heng urged our farmers who received rice seeds now to sow and transplant in time, it rained enough. Mr. Hun Manet's Aid Team Brings Donation Materials and Planting 600 Luxury Saplings at Wat Tapov, Svay Rieng Province
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Hun Manet's team brought construction materials including 10 tons of cement, 10,000 bricks and 4 million Riels as a gift from Mr. Hun Manet and Mrs. to donate to Wat Tapov in Bavet Sangkat. Bavet, Svay Rieng province, under construction.
In addition to the above donations, the team also distributed school supplies and shoes to 55 students and provided to nearly 100 people, each receiving a white cloth, a scarf and 10,000 Riels in the morning. Saturday, August 15, 2020.
Mr. Sanh Sokhon, Chief of Bavet Sangkat and listened to the order of thanks of the Chief Inspector of Wat Tapov. Greetings from Mr. HUN Manet and Ms. and expressed a strong interest in the achievements at Wat Tapov has improved a lot, especially in the last 4 years.
Wat Ta Pov in the past, or if you look at the picture in 2014, is present only the gate of a small pagoda, no hall, the field is a field and only a few palm trees. But now, under the influence of peace, the temple has seen the achievements of the synagogue, the construction of many religious buildings, and the construction of more churches.
According to historical documents, Wat Ta Pov was built a long time ago but was abandoned in 1945 for unknown reasons. Mr. Messithon said that although there is no record of the reason for the abandonment of Wat Tapov at that time, we can still conclude that it is definitely due to the war. Because 1941-1945 was the time of World War II and Cambodia was controlled by Japan.
He said that according to documents, the period 1945-1946 was the most difficult time that the whole of Indochina was overthrown and Cambodia suffered severe destruction, some villages, houses, schools and pagodas were destroyed and abandoned.
He said that our country had peace and development during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum era for more than 10 years and also disintegrated into a series of internal wars until falling into the genocidal war in 1975-1979. Since 1998 or more than 22 years, Cambodia has lived in peace under the shadow of peace, and this precious peace that this generation and the next generation must continue to participate in protecting and maintaining.
Comfrel, a non-governmental organization that monitors the implementation of democracy and human rights in Cambodia, conducted a survey on Facebook on the arrest of Rong Chhun.
During the seven days, 13,600 people cast their ballots. Among the voters who support that "the arrest of Rong Chhun is right, does not violate the law and human rights" to more than 10,000 people, equal to 79 percent, while voters support that "the arrest of Rong Chhun is a violation of the law and Rights "have only nearly 3,000 people, equivalent to about 21 percent.
Comfrel, a foreign-funded organization, has been noted for its anti-government and anti-government activities. Despite their actions, the organization has always boasted of its neutrality and impartiality.
Through the cover-up of this survey, it is another proof of the impartiality of the organization in its activities.
Rong Chhun was arrested on July 31 and charged with "inciting serious social security unrest" under Article 495 of the Kingdom of Cambodia and was detained. At Prey Sar Prison temporarily.
According to the survey, the vast majority of Cambodians support the Royal Government of Cambodia's actions against Rong Chhun's malicious intent to attempt to cause unrest and instability in Cambodian society. The Cambodian people still love and value peace and social stability, which are the indispensable prerequisites for the development of the nation, building the economy, society and the Cambodian nation to be more prosperous.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, during the inauguration of the "Garden City" water park of Tycoon Ly Yong Phat on August 16, 2020, demanded that Comfrel, a foreign radio station broadcast in Khmer, and civil society organizations work on rights. People need to publish the results of this survey.
