Do not make the relatives of the victims shed tears because of your driving! 4 killed, 10 injured in road accidents nationwide on August 15
(Phnom Penh): According to the report of the General Commission of the National Police, on August 15, 2020, there were 9 traffic accidents across the country, resulting in 4 deaths and 10 minor injuries.
The same source confirmed that the causes of traffic accidents include: speeding, disrespecting rights, not taking the right, competing and turning accidents.
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 107 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to August 15, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 140,700 vehicles, including 104,324 motorcycles and 36,376 vehicles of all types.
Please note that for August 15, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 9 times, including 4 deaths, 10 injuries (9 serious injuries).
