Wing donates materials to children living at the Cambodian Gospel Church Child Care Center in Kampong Speu
About 60 children living in centers in Chbar Morn district will benefit from Wing's support for child care centers that provide free education, food and shelter.
Wing staff traveled to Kampong Speu to meet with students and give some personal gifts to the children there. The children received 17 laptops, sports equipment, school supplies and a tree planting ceremony.
"I would like to thank Wing Specialized Bank and its Wing staff for their generous contributions and for their long journey to meet with us," said Hussein Say Sunny, Director of the Cambodian Gospel Church Child Care Center. With the kids here. The grant comes at a time when children here are unable to attend school due to fear of Kovid 19. "Through these aids, children will be able to continue their education in their dormitories."
Manura Chan, CEO of Wing Specialized Bank, said: “Children are the bamboo shoots of Cambodia, so we must support them to get an appropriate education at an age that requires strong development for them to become A solid pillar for the country. "As Wing employees, we have benefited from a strong foundation of good education, and it is time for us to share these experiences with the next generation."
Hor Bunthe, Deputy General Manager of Wing Specialized Bank, said: “In addition to providing study materials, I am pleased that the Wing team has taken the time to exchange personal experiences with children at FGACCCC. "I hope our gestures will motivate them to do more study for the benefit of their families and communities."
