(Kampong Thom): Two trucks that always evade the scales were cracked down by the Kampong Thom Provincial Gendarmerie on August 15, 2020 in Veang village, Tang Krasang commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province.
Mr. Say Veasna, Deputy Prosecutor of Kampong Thom Provincial Court, led the Provincial Gendarmerie to intercept two vehicles carrying overweight sand and license plates to evade the scales under his direct command. Sin Virak, Prosecutor of the Kampong Thom Provincial Court.
Authorities said the ambush came after information related to scales in Prasat commune, Santuk district, along National Road 6, in collusion with the owner of a 30- to 40-a-night sand truck. Trucks from Stung Trang district, Kampong Cham province, cross the scales, pay 150,000 riel per car and head to Siem Reap to be parked at the new airport.
Mr. Say Veasna confirmed that the two vehicles were brought back to the weighbridge and sent to the Provincial Gendarmerie Headquarters for legal action.
