Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin Meets Vietnamese National Assembly President
(Phnom Penh) - After arriving in Hanoi on the afternoon of August 15, 2020, National Assembly President Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, paid a courtesy call on National Assembly President Nguyen Thi Kim Ngin at the National Assembly building. After laying a wreath at the funeral of Le Kha Phieu, former General Secretary of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam.
During the meeting, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin expressed his deepest condolences on the death of Le Kha Phieu, the tragic loss of an important leader of the Communist Party of Vietnam and the Vietnamese people. Great for the nation.
Samdech Heng Samrin emphasized that the Cambodian People's Party, the leaders of the legislature, the executive, as well as the people of Cambodia and Samdech himself would like to extend our deepest condolences to the President of the National Assembly and the people of Vietnam, as well as the families of the bodies.
The President of the National Assembly would like to dedicate the body of Mr. Le Kha Phieu to his death.
Ms. Nguyen Thi Kim Ngin expressed her deep gratitude to the National Assembly President and the delegation for paying a working visit to Vietnam and taking the opportunity to pay their respects to the late Mr. Le Kha Phieu.
The National Assembly President Nguyen Tan Dung confirmed that the government will officially pay tribute to Le Ca Phieu at three different locations: Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh City and Le Kha Phieu's hometown.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin and Mrs. Nguyen Thi Kim Ngin expressed their congratulations on the friendship and solidarity of the two countries.
The National Assembly President praised Vietnam for successfully hosting the ASEAN Summit via video, despite the global crisis of the 19-year-old Kovid.
At the same time, Samdech strongly hopes that the 41st ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly, hosted by the Vietnamese National Assembly, hosted by video in early September, will continue to be successful. The National Assembly of Cambodia is always ready to cooperate and support the General Assembly to be successful.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin once again thanked Vietnam for providing US $ 25 million for the construction of the National Assembly building. Samdech said that so far, professional officials of the two countries are working on the procedure, although a little complicated, but the construction committee has already completed the procedure to select a construction company and will sign a contract with the company to be used. That budget is extremely transparent.
The President of the National Assembly said that in the new turn of the Kovid 19 epidemic, regional and global issues have changed. Kovid 19 has had a devastating effect on the economy, investment, tourism and well-being, especially as it has claimed the lives of many people around the world. The fight against Kovid 19 is a global problem. In the past, Cambodia and Vietnam have worked closely together to respond to the fight against Kovid 19.
In the afternoon of the same day, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin led a high-level delegation of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia to return home safely by special flight.
Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia calls on parents to protect their children from dengue fever
(Phnom Penh): Dengue fever usually occurs between May and October, so the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia has once again called on parents and guardians to work together to protect their children and family members from dengue fever by introducing preventive measures. 6 important protections.
* The 6 measures include: 1: Wear close clothing 2: Do not go to places where there is a forest 3: Use mosquito repellent, mosquito repellent or mosquito incense 4: Use mosquito nets if you rest where possible There are many mosquitoes. 5: Windows and doors should be closed to prevent mosquitoes from entering your place.
