(Banteay Meanchey): Nearly 100 kilograms of drugs were burned during the International Day Against Drug Abuse on August 15, 2020 on the outskirts of Serei Sophorn.
The ceremony was also attended by leaders of the Ministry of Justice, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Governor of Svay Rieng, General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, General Mak Chito. Deputy National Police Commissioner, President of the Court and Prosecutor of the three Provincial Courts, representatives of the four provincial administrations, as well as government officials, the Armed Forces and many people.
Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, reported that the International Day Against Drugs, which weighed 93 kilograms today, was collected from four provinces:
* First: Banteay Meanchey province has drugs weighing 23 kg * Second: Oddar Meanchey province has drugs weighing 9 kg * Third: Siem Reap province has drugs weighing 58 kg * Fourth: Kampong Thom province has drugs weighing 6 kg The total number of grams of drugs examined was 93 kilograms.
