(Tbong Khmum): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, distributed 65 tons of rice seeds to 1,004 farmers in Tbong Khmum District, Tbong Khmum Province for further cultivation after their rice suffered. Damaged by a drought last July.
The rice seed distribution ceremony was held on the morning of August 15, 2020 with the participation of Mr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, leaders of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and relevant officials and local authorities. Many more.
According to the report, the prolonged drought last July caused about 575 hectares of rice fields, equivalent to 1,004 families in 13 villages in Anhcheum commune, to be completely damaged.
During the rice seed distribution ceremony, Senior Minister Kun Kim conveyed the greetings of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to the people.
The Senior Minister also informed the people of the regret of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit who were affected by the drought. The Senior Minister said that Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit have always monitored the impact of the people on natural phenomena, especially the drought in the past.
At the same time, the two Samdechs also reminded the National Committee for Disaster Management to distribute rice seeds immediately to farmers to continue planting after the rain and have enough water for rehabilitation.
