According to the police report, before the incident, the victim walked into Samrong Market to shop, while one of the four suspects came behind the victim's back and said that the money was lost immediately. Another party member whispered to the victim that he had collected a lot of money, do not tell them and asked the victim to go out of the market to share the money.
The suspect then took the victim out of the market on a motorcycle to stop at the first drain on the rubber road west of Trapeang Sno and asked the victim to remove a gold necklace weighing 5 g, a gold ring weighing 2. 5 grams and 38,500 riel in a blue bag and put in a basket, then the suspect gave the lead in the cloth bag to the victim and rode away on a motorcycle.
At the same time, the victim was driving a motorcycle to chase after him. At that time, one of the suspects drove a motorcycle to block the road. The victim saw the uncomfortable situation and remembered that he had cheated. .
After receiving the information, the Samrong City Police Intervention Force launched an operation to detain two suspects, namely: Bun Pith, a 33-year-old female resident of Chi Khmol Commune, Kirivong District, Takeo Province, and Sar Sam Oeun, a 43-year-old male. Chhnang lives in Svay Chrum village, Ou Dambang 2 commune, Sangke district, Battambang province, while the other two escaped.
