In a written statement, the Turkish Foreign Ministry said on Friday that "the history and conscience of the people of the region will not be forgotten and the hypocritical behavior of the UAE will not be forgiven." "It seeks to show that it has sacrificed for Palestine, while in fact the UAE has been betraying the Palestinian cause for its own little benefit."
According to the agreement, Israel will suspend its occupation of the Palestinian territories in the West Bank and will now focus its efforts on expanding ties with other countries in the Arab and Muslim worlds. The agreement makes the United Arab Emirates the first Gulf Arab state and the third Arab nation after Egypt and Jordan to have relations with Israel.
Addressing the Plenary Session of the Council of Ministers on August 14, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that although the world remains in a state of uncertainty about Kovid 19, Cambodia must be vigilant. Clarity and ownership of work are two main priorities:
Second, maintaining good macroeconomic stability, preventing inflation and rising market prices.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also urged the relevant ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations to implement five tasks:
Task 1: Continue to fight Kovid 19 to prevent the spread of the disease in the community and to continue to implement and take strict health measures in places where tourists visit, especially during the upcoming holidays to maintain well-being. Of the people. The Ministry of Health must work to establish 19 laboratory tests for Kovid virus in addition to the laboratories in Phnom Penh in three other major provinces: Sihanoukville, Siem Reap and Battambang.
Task 2: Continue to maintain security, public order and ensure traffic safety to protect the safety and life of the people.
Task 3: Continue to implement the cash support program for the poor and vulnerable people due to the effects of Kovid-19 for another two months.
Task 5: To allow the reopening of general education institutions and vocational training schools, which must be divided into stages and must adhere to the health rules. For general education institutions and vocational training schools that will be allowed to reopen, there must be proper disinfection according to the technical specifications, especially the school building that used to be used as a center.
The Royal Government also thanked and appreciated the high capacity and responsibility of the team of doctors and health officials of Cambodia who have worked hard to contribute to improving the quality of the local health sector to grow proudly while the need for services. Local health care is now on the rise, replacing people seeking medical treatment abroad during the Kovid 19 crisis.
The Royal Government would also like to thank all Ministries, Sub-National Administrative Institutions, the Armed Forces, civil servants at all levels, the private sector and the people of the country for their hard work and active participation with the Royal Government in maintaining peace, political stability and stability. Macroeconomics, as well as participating in the fight against and prevention of the spread of Kovid-19 in the past in Cambodia.
