Siem Reap Red Cross Branch Campaigns to Promote and Strengthen Traffic Safety for the Public and Road Passengers
(Siem Reap): The Cambodian Red Cross Branch of Siem Reap Province, in cooperation with the Provincial Police Commissioner, Siem Reap Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports and the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, on August 14, 2020, organized a campaign to promote and strengthen traffic safety for the holidays. The Royal Government allows holidays instead of Khmer New Year.
The campaign was conducted in the presence of Ms. Teang Eng Tea Seiha, Vice Chairwoman of the Siem Reap Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, who led the branch staff and Red Cross youth to facilitate traffic at some traffic lights in Siem Reap by distributing traffic safety leaflets, leaflets. Prevent dengue fever and chickenpox for the people and some street travelers in Siem Reap.
Ms. Teang Eng Tea Seiha, on behalf of Mr. Tea Seiha, Chairman of the Branch Committee, said that in order to contribute to reducing the rate of traffic accidents to death, injury and disability, the Provincial Red Cross Branch has carried out many activities such as improving traffic safety on the road. Disseminate in public places, especially in the community, and Red Cross volunteers and youth educate how to wear safety goggles properly, obey traffic signs, turn off reflectors and so on.
Today's campaign aims to remind all road users of all means of transportation to be extra careful when traveling, especially during the Khmer New Year holidays. On the other hand, the Siem Reap Provincial Administration has organized the "Siem Reap Holiday" program from 17 to 21 August 2020.
Ms. Teang Eng Tea Seiha also reminded all people not to be neglected about Kovid 19, which is a common global challenge now and it is important to participate in high responsibility together. Step 1: Do not forget to bring a mask or scarf with you always, Second: Do not forget to bring gel or alcohol to wash your hands and Third: Do not forget to keep a safe distance to prevent the spread of Kovid-19.
