Preah Vihear Provincial Authority Delivers Donations from the Royal Government of Cambodia to 600 Veterans and Poor Families
(Preah Vihear): Food items, a precious gift from the Royal Government of Cambodia, were handed over by the Preah Vihear Provincial Authority to the Cambodian Veterans Association of Preah Vihear Province for distribution to the families of 600 veterans and poor families.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Ko Subunsoeut, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province, representing Mr. Prak Sovann, Provincial Governor and Honorary President of the Provincial Cambodian Veterans Association, with the participation of the Director of Departments around the province on the afternoon of August 14, 2020. At Preah Vihear Provincial Military Operations Area Headquarters.
Mr. Kor Subunsoeut said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister, has always taken care of the families of Cambodian veterans, the families of the army, as well as the families of people with special needs. During the period when Kovid 19 was spreading around the world and during this flood season.
On behalf of Mr. Prak Sovann, Mr. Ko Subunsoeut praised and thanked the Cambodian Veterans Association of Preah Vihear Province for its efforts to find veterans in the villages, communes and districts and helped our veterans' families on time, such as construction. Home delivery as well as bringing other gifts to distribute.
At the same time, the Deputy Governor also urged the families of veterans and our people to work hard to increase the cultivation of various mixed crops to improve family life even better.
