(Koh Kong): With the support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Koh Kong Province has received new achievements of 230 kV transmission line and substation infrastructure.
Mr. Keo Rattanak added that the new transmission line and substation are within the framework of cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the French Republic through the French Development Agency, which has granted concessional loans to Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) to increase the scope of transmission of electricity. By quality, stability and sustainability.
The project has been overseen by EDC engineers since the beginning of 2014, with the assistance of EDF International Technical Advisor, and is being built by major Chinese companies, including ZTT for 115 kV transmission lines and 230 kV and TBEA for substations 115 kV and 230 kV.
At the same time, the new high-voltage transmission line can provide up to 600 megawatts of power, which can further expand the development of our country's coastal corridor along National Road 48, which will help accelerate national economic growth.
