MOSCOW (Reuters) - Iranian oil under Washington's target has been seized and transferred to four other ships for transport to the United States, but Iran has denied the allegations. Immediately. This was released by Sputnik on Friday evening, August 14, 2020.
Sputnik made the report based on Reuters, which published the news after receiving a source from a US official on condition of anonymity. A U.S. judge has ordered the seizure of four Iranian oil tankers carrying oil to Venezuela in July after receiving a complaint from U.S. prosecutors. Not a ship or a ship.
The owners of the four ships acknowledged the Iranian oil transfer, but the Iranian ambassador to Caracas claimed that the Iranian tanker to Venezuela had not recently been seized by the United States. Of the Western press.
