(Phnom Penh): Mr. Youk Ngoy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, said that so far, technology is more and more modern, so we have to keep up with technology, if not keep up with technology, it is really difficult to compete with countries in The region and the world, because they have already taken a step forward in this field of technology.
Mr. Youk Ngoy said this on the morning of August 14, 2020 at the National University of Education on the occasion that he presided over the announcement of the three winning teams in Cambodia, which will go to compete with many other youth groups. From other countries later this month to reach the finals in China to win the 2020 Alibaba Awards.
Mr. Youk Ngoy added that the three groups of young people who will compete in the e-commerce talent of Alibaba 2020 at the end of this month through this competition program is very important for Cambodia and it reflects the technological up-to-date policy. Of the Royal Government of Cambodia as well.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Education further stated that, in fact, in the 19th Kovid phase, if we do not have modern technology, we can not learn online and have to wait for the Kovid 19 to calm down before we can continue to study like this. If we are not good at technology, we are wasting almost a year.
