(Phnom Penh): With the growth of Cambodia's rice exports to international markets in recent times, which will be able to achieve the goal of the Royal Government to export 1 million tons of rice in the future. Sustainability is the main spirit of the plan that the Cambodian Rice Federation has been pursuing.
The 22 farming communities located in Kampong Cham, Kampong Thom and Siem Reap, with a total of 1,516 families, have benefited from the sustainable rice production and supply market from today's contract farming. At the same time, these 22 communities have a production capacity of 5,536 tons of rice on an area of 2,303 hectares.
It should be noted that on July 10, 2020, Battambang Province also held the signing of agricultural production contracts according to the contract between 8 communities on the supply and purchase of 18,000 tons of rice by the end of August 2020. There will be contracts for another 50 communities on more than 10,000 tons of sustainable rice with agricultural communities from Preah Vihear, Kampot, Kampong Chhnang, Takeo and Mondulkiri, which will take place in Phnom Penh.
It is highly appreciated in the interest of Mr. Prem Ratha to open the program on today's agricultural production contract signing ceremony, which the Deputy Governor is really proud of on behalf of rice farmers in Kampong Thom and two other provinces, Siem Reap. And Kampong Cham, which have the opportunity to enter into agricultural production contracts with Amru Rice, which will be a mutual benefit, a guarantee for both the company and the community.
Mr. Oknha, President of the Federation, also encouraged the farming community to become a community and successful farmers, to be transformed from ordinary farmers to entrepreneurs who can manage and gain 1-market, 2-technical support from partner organizations And 3- Appropriate budget or loan from the bank.
The commitment of the 22 farming communities to supply sustainable rice to Amruray through contract agricultural production is reflected in the demonstration of production processes and results, thorough and comprehensive rice quality control.
In fact, a representative of the Samaki Sustainable Agriculture Community in my village, located in Trapeang Russey commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province, Ms. Siv Vandy, the deputy head of this farming community, said at the ceremony that the signing of her community's agricultural contract with Amru Rice has been cooperating since 2018.
Her community has 64 SRP rice producers on 155 hectares of land and yields 388 tons. Since the signing of the agricultural contract, the lives of the community members have started to improve.
Police crack down on illegal cigarette production site in Po Sen Chey district, arrested 18 foreigners, sent to court today for legal action
(Phnom Penh): Police launched an operation to crack down on the theft of illegal cigarettes and the forgery of an illegal brand in Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The operation was carried out under the direction of General Miech Sophanna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Chairman of the Committee on Combating Counterfeit Products (PRC) and led by Lt. Gen. Tan Sokvichea under the coordination of Mr. Say. Nora, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
As a result, the specialized force found counterfeit raw materials, production of large-scale machines and cigarettes, ready to export a total of 25 tons, and arrested 18 foreign suspects (15 Chinese and 3 Vietnamese) with a Chinese mastermind.
On the morning of August 14, 2020, the Anti-Counterfeit Products Committee prepared a case file and sent the 18 foreigners to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to continue the proceedings.
