Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and General Neth Savoeun decide to transfer duties and discipline a group of police officers in Prey Veng province (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, has decided to resign. Transfer duties and warn a group of police officers involved in the recent misconduct of the National Police in the operation to crack down on drug cases that have been criticized on social media.
According to the decision of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and General Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner General decided as follows:
* First: Facilitate the duties of Brigadier General Thong Vandy from Deputy Commissioner for Prey Veng Provincial Anti-Drug Planning to Deputy Commissioner without receiving any plan and receiving the first warning.
* Second: Apply discipline under the image of the first warning to Colonel Pov Chivoan, Director of the Prey Veng Provincial Anti-Drug Office, the reason for the violation of discipline of the National Police Force.
* Third: Remove the position of Lieutenant Colonel Touch Theara from the Deputy Director of the Anti-Drug Bureau to become an officer and move up to the rank of Lieutenant Colonel (Officer 2) for violating the discipline of the National Police Force and the police officer. This must appear at the staff office at Prey Veng Provincial Police every working hour until a new decision.
* Fourth: Remove the rank of Lieutenant Colonel Sibo from the Research and Investigation Officer of the Anti-Drug Bureau to be an officer of the National Police Force for disciplinary reasons and to appear at the staff office at Prey Veng Provincial Police every working hour. Until a new decision is made
* Fifth: Discipline should be applied to 3 more police officers of the Anti-Drug Office of Prey Veng Provincial Police under the guise of downgrading the ranks as follows: Lieutenant-Colonel Heng Chanratana to the rank of Lieutenant-Colonel. Lieutenant Siek Chanthoeun, an officer to the rank of lieutenant colonel, and Lieutenant Colonel Yun Daraphos as an officer to the rank of lieutenant colonel for reasons of breach of discipline of the National Police Force.
Following the decision of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and General Dr. Neth Savoeun on the afternoon of August 14, 2020, Lt. Gen. Sok Monorom, Deputy Director of the Personnel Department, representing the General Commissioner of the National Police, strengthened the working procedures for officers. Police of Prey Veng Provincial Police.
On July 20, 2020, at 20:30, the specialized force of Prey Veng Provincial Police cracked down on drug trafficking in front of the gate of Rong Damrey pagoda in Village 6, Sangkat Kampong Leav, Prey Veng City.
During the operation, the police arrested the suspects, Thai Samad, 26, and Hoeun Rath, 28. The suspects claimed that Prey Veng provincial anti-drug police officers pulled out a pistol from their waists, hit them on the head and summoned their accomplices to the police station, tortured them and extorted another 4,000,000 riel. In exchange for his release.
