Cambodian workers kill at a handicraft shop in Korea, Cambodian ambassador expresses regret and calls on Cambodian workers to love each other and preserve the honor of the Cambodian nation
(Phnom Penh): A Cambodian worker died in the factory while working because another Cambodian worker who worked with him was assassinated. The murder case was a tragic and shocking affair that deeply saddened the Cambodian embassy in South Korea.
The same massacre between Cambodian workers took place on August 10, 2020 at a handicraft factory in Namyangju, Gyeonggi-do Province. The victim, 30-year-old Su Oun, was born in Andong Thmor commune, Prey Nob district, Sihanoukville province.
According to people familiar with the victim, the victim has been working in Korea for two terms and will have only a few months left to complete his term. The victim is known to be meek, kind-hearted, rarely has problems with others, and strives to be loved by his boss, until each time he visits the district, he has to issue more letters. Also.
According to reports, the victim also had a wife who went to work in South Korea and gave birth just eight months ago.
The story goes that the murderer's hatred of the victim, who was loved by his boss more than himself, and that he had been teased about this when he had been killed. Drinking program together.
According to reports, the suspect in the murder has been arrested by South Korean authorities and is being questioned and prosecuted.
Cambodian Ambassador to South Korea Long Dimanche told Fresh News that after receiving the information, the embassy visited and coordinated the issue and issued a permit for the cremation of the victims. This Friday, August 14th.
The ambassador said the victim's items would be brought back to Cambodia by his wife next Monday. The ambassador also said that because the accident was not a work accident, the victim did not receive any compensation from the employer. However, due to the compassionate feelings of the boss, the boss paid for the festival and paid for his wife's travel expenses to bring the items back to his hometown.
Mr. Long Dimanche said that the murder of Cambodian workers in South Korea has happened in the past, but at various drinking places, but never happened in the workplace. According to Long Dimanche, the murder case has caused a great deal of controversy in the Korean community.
Representing the Cambodian people in South Korea, Long Dimanche also expressed deep regret over the murder. He said that the murder case also affected the dignity of Cambodian workers, which the Royal Government of Cambodia has always tried to maintain to ensure jobs in South Korea for Cambodian workers.
The ambassador also called on Cambodian workers in South Korea not to quarrel to the point of killing each other. If you are upset that the boss loves you more than you do, as in the case above, you must try to strengthen your ability to work hard and build a better life without choosing to kill each other, destroy their lives, destroy their own future and destroy the honor of the Khmer nation. .
