(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, said that as of July last year, Kovid 19 disease affected 3,000 tourist destinations and affected more than 50,000 employees in Cambodia.
Mr. Thong Khon said this on August 13, 2020 at a press conference after meeting with the National Assembly Committee on Education, Youth, Cult, Religious Affairs, Culture and Tourism (7th Committee) to discuss measures to address tourism. In the context of Kovid 19 and beyond Kovid 19, as well as examining the possibility of increasing tourism activities in Cambodia.
"As of July 10, more than 3,000 locations have been affected and more than 50,000 employees have been affected, but the government is still struggling with its operators," he said. The private sector and the employers as well as the government have put in place a number of measures to help operators as well as employees affected.
The Ministry of Tourism has assigned a special working group led by the Permanent Secretary of State to have five sub-committees to carry out the work of the main sub-committees, including: First, to pay attention to the request of the business base, and second, to review the request of the employer. And third, consider training at this stage.
Mr. Thong Khon said that the Royal Government has so far launched the fifth round of measures, including addressing more than 30,000 affected employers in the tourism sector by providing a $ 40 subsidy. Each person for 2 months and this 5th round provides 2 more months.
At the same time, for the private sector, business operators who own restaurants, the Royal Government has provided from the first round, the first is to exempt the business tax (which usually has to declare tax, but the state pays the tax instead) and the second is not to allow traders to pay contributions for No, but at this stage, the employees still receive the UWSA from the Royal Government.
Mr. Thong Khon said that it is the responsibility of the Ministry of Tourism for all tourism licenses to apply for a license, but does not require a license fee. For guides, even if they do not receive a $ 40 allowance, the Royal Government guides license is free.
"So the ordinary guide license is $ 50, if the special guide license is up to $ 100, but we do not take the license." This is an additional confirmation of the Minister of Tourism.
Mr. Hun Many, Chairman of the National Assembly's Seventh Committee, said that the commission also requested and urged the Ministry of Tourism to continue its activities, especially in promoting tourism, focusing on building the confidence of tourists, both domestic and international.
He also encouraged the Ministry to continue to work closely with the international community, especially ASEAN countries, to promote intra-ASEAN tourism movement at an appropriate stage where currents and flows of regional tourism can flow. Reworkable.
Mr. Hun Many stated: "At this stage, increasing the reliable and safe tourism environment from Kovid 19 and ensuring the standard of care and protection is important. "Promote the tourism industry to function normally, as well as contribute to the growth of the national economy."
Please be informed that the Seventh Commission will continue to cooperate in monitoring and discussing, as well as supporting both the spirit and strength of the Ministry's implementation of measures and measures for tourism in the context of Kovid 19 and beyond Kovid 19, as well as continue to examine the possibility of increasing activities. Tourism in Cambodia.
