Please read the press release below: Singapore Port Authority launches strict measures to control "ammonium nitrate"
MPA authorities told CNA that ships carrying the chemical ammonium nitrate to the port of Singapore must notify the port authorities of their cargo before arrival and that they will be able to load the cargo only if approved. In addition, the MPA will carry out inspections of ships to ensure that all policies are followed.
The decision to tighten controls by Singapore authorities came after an ammonium nitrate explosion at the port of Beirut, Lebanon, last week killed at least 170 people and injured six others. More than 500 people and more than 300,000 have lost their homes.
