National Council for the Khmer Language seeks approval in writing Latin letters, names of provinces and locations
(Phnom Penh): The National Council for the Khmer Language has organized a roundtable discussion on "Experiences and Issues of Principles in the Use of Latin Letters for Pronouns in Khmer Anonymous" in order to seek consensus in writing Latin letters on provincial names and Public places.
This roundtable discussion was chaired by Dr. Hean Sokhom, President of the National Council for the Khmer Language, this morning, August 13, 2020 at the Royal Academy of Cambodia, with the participation of speakers from relevant ministries, the Ministry of Education, the Ministry of Planning and the Ministry. Organize land, urban planning and construction, including a large number of research officers and students.
Dr. Hean Sokhom pointed out that in the era of globalization, the use of the Latin alphabet for writing Khmer public names was necessary. In everyday life, the use of Latin letters is also essential in the registration of passports. On the other hand, the need to write the name of the province, district, commune, village, street, place, temple, park in Latin letters is also necessary.
