Former brother-in-law beats brother-in-law, beheaded, bleeds 4 stitches in Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Sen Chey, the perpetrator was arrested by the police
(Phnom Penh): A case of violence occurred in Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Sen Chey, next to the Choam Chao 1 Administrative Police Station.
This incident happened on the afternoon of August 12, 2020 in Sangkat Choam Chao 1, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The victim is Kry Sokny, male, 35 years old, living in New World Borey, Trapeang Thleung Village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, while the perpetrator is Nhim Chhin Leang, male, 31 years old.
According to the victim, he and his wife lived in disarray, leading to a legal divorce. The court ordered his two sons and daughters to live with his wife, paying a monthly allowance, but his 8-year-old son refused to live with his wife and did not take good care of his children. Chief.
He said his son had been living with him for three months. On the afternoon of August 12, 2020, while he was at home, the authorities summoned him to settle with his ex-wife and brother-in-law at the commune hall to discuss the issue of children, while on August 13, 2020, he and The wife has to go to court to file a lawsuit to change her boss.
According to the victim, when he arrived at the commune hall, his brother-in-law, who was the instigator, beat him from behind with a hard object in his hand, causing his head to bleed in the commune hall, where many officials were watching. .
After the incident, the victim filed a complaint at the Chaom Chao 1 police station, requesting the authorities to find justice and deal with the perpetrators according to law.
The perpetrator, who is a brother-in-law, was arrested and sent to the police inspector of Po Sen Chey district to continue the procedure.
