Who is the first generation of Westerners in Cambodia? There is no one but the extremist opposition group led by prisoner Sam Rainsy.
The opposition, on the other hand, is its own chess player, and it has disintegrated, partisan, family-oriented, scattered, and fled to every corner, causing serious trouble for the boss. To make matters worse, the group's leaders have been facing countless lawsuits both at home and abroad, all of which are clear crimes that the West clearly understands, even at home. Their law is not favorable.
In a state of internal division, exhaustion, discouragement, and in such an old age, the boss is very desperate to see his first-generation nephew as a kind of child who feeds and is useless. Therefore.
Such a deteriorating situation does not improve, even if it continues to be supported, will result in nothing but time and wasted resources.
That is why the European Union decided to abandon its first generation of nephews, but only on August 12, 2020, and finally start to cultivate a new generation of nephews, according to Western theories that have been. Practiced since the 20th century, "open for development can not only be demolished and rebuilt for development."
What are the reasons for the EU to stop supporting its first generation?
Third: After the CNRP was dissolved by the Supreme Court, Sam Rainsy did not show the ability to unite to defend his politics, but instead took the opportunity to build his own forces, betrayed Kem Sokha, which caused the party supporters to dissolve. After that, the breakup got worse and worse.
Fourth, both before and after the arrest of Kem Sokha and after the dissolution of the CNRP, Sam Rainsy chose the wrong strategy by fleeing to a foreign country and relying entirely on the West. This act is like peeling off the face of its boss to make it clearer that the opposition is a foreign pawn.
Fifth, in order to maintain the geopolitical balance in Southeast Asia and to be able to maintain the benefits of its partnership with ASEAN, the EU has no choice but to abandon its first-generation subordinates and return to work with the government. Prime Minister Hun Sen.
Continuing to provide assistance, as well as the decision to reduce the EBA by 20%, is an important part of EU policy to demonstrate its commitment to continue working with the Cambodian government and is a sign of the abandonment of the first generation. "Because the EBA is the end of the lives of the opposition, the pawn of the West," said Prime Minister Hun Sen.
Therefore, the EU decision to cut 20% is a "cold-blooded murder" to the political life of Sam Rainsy and his allies.
As evidence, lately, neither the European Union nor the United States has raised the issue of Sam Rainsy with the Cambodian government, let alone questioned it. And to put it bluntly, Sam Rainsy is a card that has been completely discarded, while Kem Sokha is a small card that is being used as a psychological warfare to show the new generation of opposition groups that "just serve them." "They are still protecting and supporting."
First: "Politics through conspiracy and serving foreign ambitions to destroy the nation itself is a non-native politics that the first generation of opposition groups have suffered the most bitter defeat because the principles of national sovereignty cannot be compromised."
Second: "Being an opponent of the ruling party led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen is absolutely impossible to use foreign influence to threaten, impose conditions or put pressure on, and if you dare to follow the same old path, it is true. "Will inevitably get the same results as the first generation opposition."
