(Phnom Penh): Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, on August 12, 2020, allowed 24 students who received scholarships to study in Japan to pay a courtesy call and receive some advice before they left. Study.
During the meeting, Dr. M. Chhun Lim shared his personal experience of studying and working abroad, such as France, the Soviet Union, the United States and other countries around the world. Used to live and study for 2 years in Japan.
Mr. Kitti Nitikosal Bandith shared about the process of building the rule of law based on the strong foundation of the Constitution that the Kingdom of Cambodia is striving for and achieving peace, stability and national development. At the same time, Mr. Kitti Nitikosalbandit also shared his experiences about the culture and way of life in Japanese society so that all the winners would understand and be ready to live.
At the same time, Dr. M. Chhun Lim instructed the 24 winners to study hard according to their skills, overcome all obstacles to acquire knowledge and experience to help build the institution they are working for and help build the country. The nation must respect the rules and regulations of the school and the laws and customs of Japan.
Mr. Im Chhun Lim also instructed them to work hard to maintain the honor of the nation and national sovereignty by understanding the laws and good traditions of the nation and help promote what is beneficial to the nation.
Dr. Kittinit Kosal Bandith considered all these winners to play the role not only as students but also as ambassadors representing the country, so they must know how to protect the honor and national interest and build good relations with all students. Country of study there.
Dr. M. Chhun Lim, the Honorary Legal Officer, wished all 24 winners good health and safe flight. He also reminded all the winners to take care of their health and avoid the COVID19 infection that is spreading around the world at this time.
