(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health presented a leaflet explaining the obligations to be made during the 14-day isolation period.
The 10 obligations that you set yourself apart include:
2: Monitor the symptoms of the disease * Take the temperature daily, twice a day, morning and evening * If the temperature exceeds 37.5 degrees Celsius or any symptoms such as cough, sore throat, difficulty breathing, must provide information to the health center to Consultation.
3. Separate from family members * Live in a separate room with adequate ventilation and use a separate room or toilet from the family. Other members and families must live in a separate room * Eat separate meals from family members * Wear a mask when family members are nearby in the same room or at least 2 meters apart. Reduce meeting with family members and use of shared space.
4: Use separate items from family members: * Plates, spoons, glasses, towels or shawls, beds, mats, pillows, pillows, blankets, clothes and other personal items * Wash items with clean water and soap well * Wash clothes, rugs, towels or Cover with a mild soap and pat dry.
7: Eat only well-cooked food * Food should be cooked well * Eat foods rich in fish, meat, vegetables, fruits, reduce salt and sweetness to help strengthen the immune system.
8: Maintain a normal mood and good hygiene in the living room * Exercise and do other activities as usual, such as reading books, watching news, entertainment programs on the radio or television, using the Internet, phone ..... * Clean your own living room, bathroom and appliances. Others such as beds, desks, cabinets, door handles, etc. Every day.
9: End the practice of Chattalysak * Allow to end if you have properly followed the measures of living separately at home every 14 days and during that time you have no symptoms.
10: Contact in case of need and urgency * If you need consultation or medical assistance, please contact the health center staff or doctors assigned to monitor health and contact you regularly or call the Ministry of Health's hotline 115 by Free. Telecom Regulator of Cambodia Issues Guidance on Measures to Enforce Telecommunications Law on Telecom Operators
