(Phnom Penh): The Governor of the Board of Governors of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, warned that if in any district, there is a burglary of entertainment clubs and karaoke with a lot of guests and the competent forces of the Phnom Penh Municipal Commission to crack down. Obviously, the district governor will have problems with the Ministry of Interior and the Royal Government.
Mr. Khuong Sreng made this remark on the afternoon of August 12, 2020 at a meeting on measures to prevent the spread of COVID-19 at entertainment clubs and karaoke in Phnom Penh at Phnom Penh Capital Hall. Participation from 14 district authorities and other relevant departments.
He said that the entertainment club and karaoke, which is converted into a restaurant, the district authorities must check whether the rules of the Ministry of Health, such as washing hands with alcohol and soap and water, wearing a mask and keeping away from each other. In connection with this issue, Samdech Techo Prime Minister has already said that on behalf of the authorities, the competent forces related to Kovid-19, we should not be too brave and not too afraid to lose control.
Regarding the transformation from a karaoke club into a restaurant, Mr. Khuong Sreng also urged all district authorities to check whether the rules of the Ministry of Health have been properly followed. For example, have a thermometer, have alcohol, wash your hands, set the table properly.
At the same time, the Capital Governor also instructed the governors of all districts to cooperate with the Department of Health and Markets to spray and disinfect the market in a rotating manner.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that for the supermarket, there must be security guards to open the door, there must be a thermometer, and there must be alcohol to wash hands. In state markets, the president of the market must also follow the rules of the Ministry of Health.
He also stressed that the issue of Covid-19 is not a matter for the Ministry of Health alone, but for all of us to work together to prevent the spread of the disease. The district authority shall monitor the location of the police station and the residence of the people who are in charge of the police station and report to the Phnom Penh Capital Administration on a regular basis.
"We can forget Kovid 19, but Kovid 19 does not forget all of us, but we dare to be careless and at risk," he said, especially in the markets must be cleaned and sprayed regularly to prevent To spread in our community by taking responsibility from all of us, our community and the high attention of local authorities.
Kandal provincial official warns of legal action if any ice-making enterprises and handicrafts are found to be substandard
(Kandal): Mr. Huot Vantho, Director of the Department of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation of Kandal Province, warned against taking legal action against the owners of enterprises and handicrafts producing ice cream and sanitary ware throughout the province if it is found to be in violation of hygiene standards.
Such a warning by Mr. Huot Vantho was made on August 12, 2020 in the meeting to promote the "Quality of hygiene for business owners and handicrafts, ice and sanitation" in Kandal province, with the participation of professional officials. And more than 20 owners of sanitary ice handicraft enterprises.
Mr. Huot Vantho stated that the main purpose of this outreach meeting was to disseminate to the owners of all ice and ice handicraft enterprises to ensure that the products are made in accordance with the standards of hygiene and safety. Consumers.
On that occasion, the director of the department also advised and encouraged all owners of ice handicraft enterprises to have regular inspections on their production lines, especially to implement the S5 principle: clean, orderly, clean, standard and stable to Improve product quality, reduce costs, make products faster and safer.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health has produced a leaflet to explain to the Cambodian people to protect themselves from the transmission of Kovid 19 while traveling, especially on the holiday of Khmer New Year from the 17th. August 21, 2020
Here are some measures to prevent transmission of Kovid 19 while traveling:
* First: Avoid traveling or pausing if you have a fever and cough.
* Second: If you have a fever, cough and difficulty breathing, seek medical attention immediately and tell your doctor about your travel history.
* Third: If you start to get sick while traveling, tell the flight attendant and seek medical attention as soon as possible and tell your doctor about your travel history.
* 6: If you wear a mask, be sure to cover the mouth and nose, but avoid touching the outer mask while wearing and removing.
9th: Avoid close contact with people with acute respiratory diseases such as fever, cough, sneezing or cold.
