GMAC has developed this guide for the benefit of members and international buyers who will be affected by this EU decision. This guideline is designed to provide clarity on the tariff line on products that lose EBA benefits and the tariff line on products that continue to benefit from duty-free and quota-free imports for the EU market.
European Commission Decision of 12 February 2020 excludes benefits for a total of 40 tariff lines (1 line for sugar, 5 lines for travel products, 25 lines for garments and 25 lines Tax line on footwear products 9) at 4 and 6 digits, effective from August 12, 2020. These 40 tax lines are in Table 1.
The remaining six-digit tariff lines still receive duty-free and quota-free benefits under the same EBA program for exports from Cambodia. Those lines are in Table 2.
