The entry into force comes six months after the EU issued its decision to partially cut the EBA on 12 February 2020. According to the Royal Government, the partial exclusion of the EBA is worth about $ 100 million.
In response to the decision to partially cut off Europe's EBA, the Royal Government of Cambodia, with its Ministry of Economy and Finance in charge, has developed a strategic policy to counteract hundreds of millions of dollars since early 2019. Increased with 19 cases of Kovid. And considering the EBA and Kovid 19, the government is preparing a budget of up to more than $ 1 billion to cope with the crisis.
Meas Sok Sen San confirmed that the removal of parts of the EBA does not mean a loss to the European market. Europe is still Cambodia's market, just a few items that used to be tax-exempt.
He said the removal of the EBA was just a tariff increase of about 20 percent of Cambodia's exports to Europe, which resulted in some factories shifting production lines to duty-free areas and others. Still able to process exports.
On 12 February 2020, the European Commission (EU) issued a decision to cut parts of the EBA on the grounds that Cambodia undermines respect for human rights, political rights and democracy, and calls on Cambodia to improve all aspects. This. It is estimated that more than 100 million US dollars will be deducted from 40 parts of Cambodia's preferential treatment.
