"We see e-commerce as a new destination for doing business and we want to be a part of it from the beginning," he said. We would like to thank MasterCard for partnering with this project and we are confident that through this collaboration we will be able to bring a wide range of modern lifestyle options to our customers. ”
"People and businesses in Cambodia are increasingly focusing on the latest digital products, such as virtual cards, debit cards and MasterCard," Wong said. "Phillip Bank MasterCard Debit Card is the bank's first step into the field of electronic card payments and is also the first step in MasterCard's partnership with Phillip Bank."
Sweet bamboo shoots and materials to support the production of sweet bamboo shoots were handed over to the forest community in Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): In order to improve the livelihood of community forestry in Preah Vihear province, the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Preah Vihear Province has donated sweet bamboo seeds and materials to support the production of sweet bamboo shoots to three forest communities in Preah Vihear province. In the provinces, there are Krasaing forest community, Chep Lech forest community and Samaki Trapeang Tontum forest community.
The handover ceremony was held on August 10, 2020 in the presence of Mr. Peng Trida, Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, with the participation of Forestry Administration District, ASPIRE Program Advisors in collaboration with the Office of Agriculture, Natural Resources and Environment of Chhep District. As well as many other communities.
Mr. Peng Trida said that in 2020, the Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries (ASPIRE) will provide bamboo shoots, sweet grapes and production support materials to the community forestry. Growing sweet bamboo shoots, each community received a pond, 700 sweet bamboo shoots, a wheelchair, a water pump and a scale.
The director of the provincial agriculture department said that in addition to forest by-products such as mushrooms, vines and other natural resources, the community will also benefit from this sweet bamboo vine in the future. He called on people to participate in the cultivation and maintenance of this sweet bamboo vine, as instructed by professional officials.
