But they later admitted that what they were saying was wrong. Hong Sochua, a former senator from the Sam Rainsy Party, in 2017 wrote a letter apologizing to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for his slanderous allegations in the border case.
In the letter of apology, Hong Sochua stated, "I regret that Samdech's policy was wrong in the process of erecting border posts, such as using incorrect documents in border issues, leading to confusion in public opinion on the basis." Past policies and practices of the Royal Government. "From today on, I will be careful not to let this happen again."
In the letter, Hong Sochua also highlighted Samdech Techo Hun Sen's efforts to achieve national unity, national unity to protect Cambodia's territorial integrity and maintain good relations with neighboring countries. Hong Sochua called on Samdech Techo's efforts to make it easier to build a prosperous homeland.
In addition to Hong Sochua, Oum Sam An, a former CNRP lawmaker, in August 2018 also wrote a letter of apology to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for the mistake of falsifying the border issue. In the letter of apology, Oum Sam An admitted that he spoke without considering the border issue between Cambodia and Vietnam, which led to serious damage to security and social order.
Through the letter of apology, Oum Sam An even promised not to take any action on the border issue between Cambodia and Vietnam without consideration. Oum Sam An also promised to abide by the Constitution and other laws to participate in protecting the peace that Samdech Techo Hun Sen worked hard to build to survive to develop the country.
Not only Hong Sochua and Oum Sam An, even Sam Rainsy, who incited the border issue and fled the district, once apologized to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for falsifying the border issue.
