(Mondulkiri): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission, presided over the opening ceremony of the Consultative Workshop on the Draft Master Plan for Tourism Development in Mondulkiri Province on August 10, 2020. This is to ensure that the tourism sector in the province can attract more tourists to contribute to supporting socio-economic growth and job creation.
The workshop was held at Pich Da Restaurant, Sen Monorom City, with the participation of Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Mondulkiri Province, Vice Chairman and members of the Inter-Ministerial Commission, Mayors, District Governors, Commune Chiefs, Commune Chiefs, Private Sector Units, National and International Organizations.
Minister Thong Khon and the Governor of Mondulkiri Province, representatives of relevant institutions and departments in this workshop, paid attention to the key points such as: Defining the vision for the development of tourism in Mondulkiri, zoning. ) For tourism development, strategic orientation, key priorities and institutional mechanisms to implement the master plan, etc.
At the same time, Minister Thong Khon also commented on the draft master plan for tourism development in Mondulkiri, including:
* First, the development of tourism in Mondulkiri must adhere to the approach of sustainable development and responsibility "Development, service, conservation and conservation support development" for the benefit of the economy, society and people. The base contributes to the preservation, protection and conservation of natural resources and cultural heritage, especially the preservation of the original identity of Mondulkiri province.
* Second, development must respond to the vision of national development in 2020-2035 and the years to come, based on the current situation and the commitment of the Royal Government.
* Third: Determining the scope of investment-development activities in the five wildlife sanctuaries (Phnom Prech Nam, Lear, Lumphat, Keo Seima and Sre Pok) and the Busra Cultural and Ecotourism Corridor, encouraging the development of Ecotourism and ecotourism activities, in conjunction with indigenous cultural tourism, in particular, should be encouraged to strengthen the tourism community in a good and effective manner.
* Fourth: Provincial authorities at all levels and expertise must strictly and strictly implement the orders of the head of the Royal Government to prevent encroachment on state land, forest land as private property.
* Fifth: Register the main tourist resorts in the province as soon as possible to ensure the sustainability and efficiency of the use and development of these areas.
