General knowledge: Who made the war fail under Russia?
(World): Some emperors and warlords have always wanted to take control of Russian territory and led the army to invade many times, but the king and his leaders did not get much victory over the Russian army. Only turning back, failing, carrying shame, running through the pages of history, taking only life.
* Emperor Napoleon Bonaparte of the French Empire
In 1812, French Emperor Napoleon raised 600,000 troops from Vienna, Austria, to invade the Russian Empire, then ruled by Alexander the Great. In front of Napoleon's army, the Russian army retreated and refused to fight at all, which made Napoleon's army more and more advancing and advancing to the walled city of Moscow, the capital of Russia.
After conquering Mongolia from the Great Wall, Russian troops continued to invade eastern Asia, near Machu Picchu in present-day northeastern China. On arrival there, the Russian army clashed with the army of Japanese Emperor Mujihito and fought for a year from 1904-1905.
This battle caused Russia to lose to Japan, while Japan also gained a reputation as the only Asian power that successfully defeated the ambitions of European powers.
In 1941, Adolf Hitler ordered 3 million German troops to invade the Soviet Union. In that battle, Hitler's Nazi army killed millions of Soviet soldiers and civilians, much to the surprise of Soviet leader Joseph Stalin.
Stalin also dispelled the Soviet Red Army against Hitler until victory and pushed the Nazi army back from Soviet territory, where the battle with the Nazis was called Stalin Grad. .
Despite this victory over the German army, the Soviet Union itself lost many millions of troops and civilians. "An estimated 14 million civilians have been killed, while Germany has lost more than 5 million troops."
In modern times, Russia has been able to continue to live with a prosperous world and become a communist ideological power, daring to compete with the United States, causing the world to be in turmoil for many years. .
The Socialist Republic also lost its influence in 1991, but to this day, the federation remains a powerful nation on the international stage. Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Inspects Meteorological Area in Batheay District
