(Svay Rieng): Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, on August 10, 2020, told officers, deputies and soldiers to absolutely protect the peace and legitimate government that emerged from the election and fight together. Kovid 19 of the second wave, starting with regular hygiene.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Men Vibol presiding over the opening ceremony of the training course on pedestrian tactics, technical education, psychology and martial arts at the Svay Rieng Military Operation Area Command on August 10, 2020.
On that occasion, the Provincial Governor also sent a message of greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to all officers, deputies and soldiers in the Svay Rieng Military Area.
The Provincial Governor expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the Svay Rieng Military Operations Area for all officers, deputies and soldiers who have actively participated in social work and relief work in the event of a disaster. Natural disasters, various social ventures, and in maintaining security, safety, and public order in the province, especially in the process of the third-mandate provincial / municipal council elections in 2019.
He stated that this is the third training course organized today, the first of which is the training course on martial arts training on November 1, 2016 and the second training course on defense skills. Boundary on November 6, 2017 and the third time today.
He stressed that as an army, it is necessary to have clear skills in all areas, including tactics, education, psychology, martial arts, how to use weapons, both heavy and light, driving vehicles or military equipment (tanks or armored vehicles) and the use of maps. Original. And these skills do not just happen, they come from practice, training and practice.
He said that as Samdech Techo Prime Minister often said, it is better to sweat on the training ground than to bleed and lose your life on the battlefield.
At the same time, Mr. Men Vibol also instructed the officers, deputies, soldiers and trainees on some important tasks as follows:
* 1: Must absolutely protect the peace and legitimate government that emerges from the election.
* 2: Must maintain absolute loyalty to the motherland and promote a sense of patriotism, strictly respect all roles and responsibilities of the army in strengthening national defense, defense, independence, peace, border protection and territorial integrity. On this basis, must always be ready to implement and achieve all the orders of the Royal Government of the Ministry of National Defense and the Commander-in-Chief.
* 3: To participate in maintaining and strengthening peace, political stability, security, and public order both within the geographical framework of the province and throughout the country.
* 4: To maintain good internal unity, especially the ranks of officers and commanders must adhere to the code of ethics and discipline consistently.
* 5: In addition to this training, all our soldiers must strive to train, learn and strengthen their professional skills on a regular basis, as well as to develop a sense of responsibility in the management and maintenance of equipment, weapons and equipment. Other to use well in the direction and take care of properly.
National Association of Capital-Provincial Council Holds a Meeting of Capacity Development Committee to Review Training Strategies for Capital-Provincial Council Members
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pa Socheatvong, President of the National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils, on August 10, 2020, chaired the first meeting of the Capacity Development Committee, which organized the purpose of discussing strategies and action plans to build council capacity. Capital, provinces throughout the country.
The Capacity Development Committee was established in 2017 for the purpose of advising and assisting in technical work related to the capacity development of Capital-Provincial Council members.
Currently, there are 11 capacity development committees, with one chairman, Ms. Mom Krasal, a member of the Phnom Penh Municipal Council, and two vice chairmen, Ms. Prak Puthy, a member of the Svay Rieng Provincial Council, and Mr. Em Det, a member of the Tbong Khmum Provincial Council.
The National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils was established in 2013 as a legal entity representing the Capital and Provincial Councils in order to enhance the status, develop the capacity and protect the legitimate interests of the Capital-Provincial Council.
