(Phnom Penh): In daily life, there is always communication and communication with each other, which is under different images, such as: normal communication in daily life Assisting in the exchange of goods or doing business. Under the picture of this relationship, we can see that the parties have established these relationships through oral contracts or through written contracts.
It should also be noted that a written contract is stronger than an oral contract in the sense that in the event of a dispute (dispute), a written contract can be used by the parties as evidence against the parties or Third parties or before the law.
If we look at the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia 2007, Article 5 is a collection of important contracts, and one of the most economically viable contracts is the "company contract".
What is a company contract and how is a company contract formed and dissolved?
Therefore, for this week, Fresh News' Legal Awareness Program in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation would like to raise the topic of "Company Contract" to explain and share to all citizens as follows:
Please note that the above topic we would like to focus on the company contract as stated in the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia 2007 only.
A company contract can be formed based on the spirit of Article 700 of the Civil Code, which shows the establishment of a company contract as follows:
1. A company is a company formed by the promise that each party invests its own assets and operates in a collaborative manner. That is, a company contract can be created only with the consent of the parties can be created as a company contract.
2. The assets that each party must invest in a company contract, in addition to assets, can be used as a subject of labor. This means that the investment assets in the company contract are not necessarily the property of the parties, the labor force can also be the subject of the investment.
3. In the event that the parties have taken the money as the subject of the asset investment, if there is a delay in payment, in addition to having to pay the interest of the delay, also shall pay for the damage caused by the delay to the company. Also. This provision reflects the liability of the parties for their delays in paying on time.
In addition to the formation of a contract or the formation of a company, there may also be liquidation based on the non-performance of the parties.
In summary, a company contract is a type of contract that is highly economical and has a positive effect on society, and in order for this contract to be strong, the parties should make a written contract, especially for this contract to be valid unless it is established. By consensus, the ability to express one's will by complying with the provisions set out in the 2007 Civil Code.
