According to Tin Pheakdey, before the incident, his wife, Neang Sotheary, rode a black Honda C125 Series 2020 with license plate number Svay Rieng 1O-2042 to her mother's house to buy a net. Fish located in Preah Tonle village, Sangkhor commune, Svay Rieng city.
While he was measuring the net, an unidentified man pulled out a pistol and shot his 18-year-old sister, Sophea, who was a shopkeeper, and shouted at her and took her away on a motorbike.
Suddenly, the sister shouted that the thieves surprised the people and chased after her, but could not because the car was hidden in front of her. After the incident, the victim went to file a complaint to the police to help find the suspect.
Regarding this case, Mr. Ken Rithy, Police Inspector of Svay Rieng City, said that there was indeed this case, but it was not a robbery. Opportunity approached, but another woman stood next to the motorcycle, the suspect took something and threatened and fled.
Currently, the police are conducting a search to find the suspect and take legal action.
