King sends condolences on death of former General Secretary of the Communist Party of Vietnam
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, His Majesty the King of Cambodia, has sent a message of condolence to the Government and people of Vietnam on the death of Kha Phieu, former General. Secretary of the Communist Party of Vietnam.
In 1991, at the 7th Party Congress, he was elected a member of the Party Central Committee. In June 1994, at the Third Central Committee (7th term), he was elected to the Secretariat until January 1994, he was elected a member of the Politburo, and in April 1996 he was appointed Permanent Secretary.
In 1996, at the 8th General Assembly, Secretary Phieu was re-elected as a member of the Party Central Committee, a member of the Standing Committee of the Politburo and a permanent member of the Politburo.
On December 26, 1997, at the Fourth Session (8th term), he was elected Secretary General of the Party Central Committee and held this position until April 2001.
