Asia Foundation Launches US Embassy Access Program for Empowerment and Leadership for Alumni
(Phnom Penh): With the support of the US Embassy in Cambodia, on August 7, 2020, the Asia Foundation announced the launch of the "Alumni Capacity Building and Leadership Program" for Alumni. From the Access program of the US Embassy 90 people.
The program lasts for 5 months in order to help improve soft skills, personal development and other important skills to successfully find a career in the job market in Cambodia.
Melanie Lynnberg, Director of the Asia Foundation, said the program focuses on learning and applying soft skills in formal work contexts to help alumni strengthen their careers.
She added that one of the other purposes of the program is to teach students how to prepare for job interviews in English, a skill that is overlooked but important for many jobs.
The capacity building and leadership program will be conducted online, combining group discussions, joint project implementation, and five-month personal learning.
Through joint projects, students participating in the program will have the opportunity to practice social work in their communities. These will contribute to giving them a hands-on experience, as well as boosting confidence in finding a way to higher education and career development. The program will showcase a variety of careers through online meetings with successful professionals from institutions, organizations, companies and governments.
"According to the National Employment Agency, soft skills such as communication, customer service, teamwork and innovation are common challenges," said Aaron Swedjes, spokesman for the US Embassy. Cambodians encounter it when they look for work.
This capacity building and leadership program will facilitate the necessary learning and leadership opportunities for the new generation of young leaders who are knowledgeable for Cambodia.
