APSARA Authority is renovating the Bay Kaek temple west of Angkor Wat into a new resort
(Siem Reap): The Apsara Authority has been improving the beauty around Bay K'aek Temple, located west of Angkor Wat, into a space museum, a new recreation area for tourists because in the past the temple was not well known. And most tourists pass by.
Today, the temple is in a dilapidated condition, leaving only the foundation and remains of the temple structure, material, scars, pedestals, bodhisattvas, sages, bodhisattvas, Bayon style and diamond pillars, which experts believe was built in the 12th century. In the Bayon style.
On the occasion of inspecting the excavation site of Bay Kaek Temple on August 3, Mr. Hang Pov, Director General of APSARA Authority, together with relevant experts, decided to raise the value of Bay Kaek Temple to become a space museum to attract tourists and preserve the building. Temple out of risk.
The team will plant trees, plant grass, restore ponds, show the history of the temple and the results from the excavation, prepare this site to attract tourists to visit, relax and organize various ceremonies.
