(Banteay Meanchey): On the night of August 6-7, 2020, a heavy downpour caused some areas of Svay Chek district, Banteay Meanchey province to be flooded due to heavy rains. In fact, nearly 40 houses of disabled soldiers at the 317 Techo Phnom Chhat Disabled Soldiers Development Center were flooded due to rain, as well as some other areas.
According to the disabled soldier there, at around 9 pm on August 6, heavy rain until 2 o'clock on August 7 left his house in the development center. 317 Techo Phnom Chhat disabled soldiers and nearly 40 houses of disabled soldiers were flooded.
Lt. Col. Sok Sreng, deputy director of the 317 Techo Phnom Chhat Disabled Soldiers Development Center, also said that the rain had flooded about 40 of the nearly 400 disabled soldiers' homes.
The flooded water flowed from the upper part to the 5th road, flooding the soldier's house above, with a small drain.
Mr. Loeung Sopheak, Governor of Svay Chek District, said that on the night of the 6th, rain fell all over Svay Chek District in 8 communes, including at the 317 Techo Phnom Chhat Disabled Veterans Development Center, about 40 houses were flooded. It has also gradually shed.
At the same time, for crops, people are not threatened by the effects of floods.
The district governor also urged people to be careful when the sky is raining, please be careful of natural phenomena such as thunder, lightning and wind that often occur.
Mr. Loeung Sopheak added that the district authorities have prepared the necessary materials such as medicine, worms, food to help people in case of need during the flood.
