(Phnom Penh): The leading technology thermometer by measuring the temperature through the scanner on the face and body, easy, fast and safe for general users of Yuropavision Company handed over to the Ministry of Health on the afternoon of the 6th. August 2020.
The handover ceremony was held at the Ministry of Health under the chairmanship of Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, and was also attended by Mr. Daniel Nellly, Founder and CEO of Europa Vision.
On that occasion, Dr. O Vandin mentioned the strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia has been implemented to prevent the transmission of 19 Kovid virus to the community.
At the same time, Mr. Daniel Nielly is committed to contributing to the prevention of Kovid 19 in Cambodia, especially his technology company is also helping businesses and the Royal Government of Cambodia apply the latest technology to easily measure the body temperature through the lens. That can capture people from a distance of 6 meters.
He said the camera could easily and accurately capture 100 people per minute and would sound an alarm if the person was found to have an abnormal temperature. In addition, the Khmer language is integrated into the system of this machine, which makes it easy for users.
Li said that Europa Vision has now started implementing solutions for large banks, international schools, corporations, hotels, restaurants and entertainment businesses.
This machine will provide easy access, is completely portable and requires little maintenance. This device will provide security, reduce the cost of using manpower, especially reduce the transmission and maintain individual gaps.
At the same time, Dr. O Vandin said that this is a victory over the invisible enemy, especially as it contributes to the security in the community.
