Tbong Khmum Water Treatment Plant to Transfer Management Under Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority to Expand Water Supply
(Tbong Khmum): On the morning of August 7, 2020, the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation transferred the management of Tbong Khmum Water Treatment Plant to the management of Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, which took place at the Provincial Water Treatment Plant. Tbong Khmum on the artificial river, Tbong Khmum provincial town.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Kim Touch, Secretary of State, Representative of the Senior Minister, Dr. Cham Prasidh, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, Mr. Sim Sitha, Advisor to the Ministry and Director General of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority, and Mr. Peang Narith, Deputy Governor of Tbong Khmum Province.
Mr. Ping Vutha, Director of Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, said that after Tbong Khmum was separated from Kampong Cham, the provincial water treatment plant was completed in late December 2017 and will start testing in February 2018. Until September 2018, it has been decided to supply clean water to provincial halls, departments, units around the province, provincial branches of the Red Cross and a total of 800 houses for government officials.
He said that from May 2019 until now, the department has connected 320 clocks and supplied about 96,043 cubic meters of clean water.
On that occasion, Mr. Sim Sitha expressed his pleasure that the Ministry has given confidence to the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority to provide the ability to continue to expand the scope of the water system in Tbong Khmum.
He presented the goal of a series of steps to expand the network and supply of clean water by 2023 to about 5,000 families in six communes in Tbong Khmum district of the provincial capital at a cost of about $ 2 million.
Mr. Kim Touch praised and appreciated all the leaders and officials of Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation who have worked hard in the past on clean water production, networking and water supply. All institutions and government officials around the province.
On that occasion, the Secretary of State instructed the leaders and officials of all departments need to have close internal unity, continue to cooperate well with the administration of provincial halls, departments, units and authorities around the province, have a transparent account together. Work effectively to absorb the sympathy of the people.
Please be informed that this transfer of management aims to achieve the 6th goal of the Royal Government of Cambodia's goal of achieving sustainability on clean water and sanitation, which determines that "People living in cities and towns across the country will have access to 100% clean water supply in 2025 "by the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has enough human resources and capital to achieve the target plan.
