Minister of Agriculture and Governor of Pursat Province Distribute Fruit Seedlings to 200 Families for Integrated Agriculture
(Pursat): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, this morning, August 7, 2020, met with the people and brought fruit seedlings (Khmer coconut). Russey, Svay, Trabek and Sdao) chicken breeds and chicken feed distributed to 200 families for the implementation of mixed farming system.
This project is implemented in collaboration with the International Institute for Rural Rehabilitation (IIRR), a local executive partner of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Pursat and Kampong Chhnang Provinces, and the Center for Development and Environment of the University of Bern, Switzerland. The SUCRA project aims to:
First, increase resilience to climate change for vulnerable smallholder farmers by encouraging them to implement good examples of integrated farming systems; Second, to improve food security and nutrition; Revenue and strengthen ecosystem function 4: Raise awareness of the risks of climate change and how to achieve sustainable resilience.
The project is implemented in 23 target villages in Pursat and Kampong Chhnang provinces, with a total of 1,500 families directly benefiting from the project. For Pursat province, there are 11 target villages in Phsut Rong commune and Talor commune, Talo Sen Chey district, and a total of 750 target farmers.
Mr. Mao Thunin was very interested and highly appreciated the results of the project implementation as reported by the Rector. He also briefed on the potential of his local agricultural sector, which has made remarkable progress despite the overall economic situation being plagued by Kovid-19.
Minister Veng Sakhon gave the people strong hope and confidence that under the wise and prudent leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, "no one can be left without food."
Regarding technical work and how to make the project sustainable, the Minister advised the project manager, project implementation officer, local authority and farmers to continue to cooperate better in disseminating, training and applying techniques on breeding and hatching methods. Mix food and care for animals and crops, and moreover, and join in maintaining peace for peace and development (thank you for peace).
