Senior Minister Osman Hassan tells all Islamic associations and organizations to step up their activities responsibly
The meeting was held on the morning of August 7, 2020 at the Office of the Council of Ministers to focus on encouraging and encouraging all (Islamic) associations and organizations to increase their activities and humanitarian activities. It has been making it more effective to join the Royal Government in the development of the community and society as a whole.
The meeting also examined some gaps to ensure that all achievements serve the society as a whole with transparency, fairness, truth and justice in accordance with the Law on Associations and Organizations in force and in line with the development direction of The Royal Government will also abide by the rules of Islam.
At the same time, the Senior Minister also reminded the representatives of all Islamic associations and organizations to increase their activities with high responsibility and good cooperation with the relevant components, including the authorities, the Imam at all levels and ministries and institutions. As a staff for the Royal Government and in accordance with the Constitution of Cambodia on Associations and Organizations.
At the same time, Mr. Prak Sam Oeun, Director General of the General Department of Administration, Ministry of Interior, gave a presentation on the content of the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations. According to the law, this law came into force in August 2015, which took almost 20 years to process, with nine chapters and 39 articles.
He urged all NGOs, both domestic and foreign, to strictly abide by the Law on Associations and Organizations, especially to carry out their humanitarian activities in a transparent, neutral, non-partisan manner, especially to report activities and Annual financial sources every end of February to the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Mr. Prak Sam Oeun appealed to the Association of Inactive Organizations to delete their names at the Ministry of Interior, but before deleting, any issues must be cleared to show their transparency and cleanliness. In particular, in the case of associations, organizations that do not have a proper registration must also hurry to register properly.
