Mr. Ponh Sachchak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, said that Banteay Meanchey province has received a project to build an irrigation system, which is a project of the Republic of Korea through the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to build an irrigation system to reduce floods and supply water. For people to use and grow crops.
Mr. Ou Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, said that at the beginning of 2020, Banteay Meanchey Province, with the prolonged drought, some districts and cities affected rice and damaged more than 7,000 hectares, the provincial administration and specialized departments are paying attention. Will find a solution for farmers who are facing the problem of no water to pump rice.
On behalf of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Administration, Mr. Ou Rathrey thanked the Korean project owner who planned to help the irrigation system in Banteay Meanchey to reduce the flood and to supply water to the people to use, grow crops and provide livelihoods to the people.
