A former demining expert in Svay Rieng province, who is seriously ill and has financial problems, is looking for a philanthropist to support him.
(Svay Rieng): A 62-year-old woman named Kong Saroeun, a resident of O'Kam village, Sambour commune, Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province, is considered a hero of the demining unit of Svay Rieng province. In bed, Phok Sam Ol, 70, has high blood pressure and diabetes and is being treated at Svay Teap District Referral Hospital in the emergency room.
Ms. Kong Saroeun described that after the liberation on January 7, 1979, she volunteered to work in the demining unit of Svay Rieng province and cleared all kinds of mines, cleared the conflict and collected unexploded ordnance every day without a day off. Demining for 13 years until 1992, when the government disbanded the demining unit.
In particular, in 2004, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, built a house through Mrs. Sangkhab Dr. Men Sam An. The sign is gone, when it rains, thunderstorms, the wind does not dare to stay on the house, wait to come to the hut outside the house.
She has a husband, three children, two daughters, not well educated, living in poverty, only 30 meters by 40 meters of residential land, no farmland, so life is difficult. Currently, all three children are married and the first child has a husband to live in Kampong Cham province.
The second daughter is married and lives with her husband in O'Kam village, but lives in poverty in a factory. The son has a wife and lives in Sambour commune, Svay Teap district, but is poor. The wife works in a factory during the day and the husband works in a factory at night. Day adopted an 11-year-old grandson named Tim Kakada, a fourth grader.
