Q: How does the CJP plan to move forward in promoting journalism ethics?
Mr. Huy Vannak: Professional ethics is the most important core value for journalists. Unethical knowledge is a loss of respect and destruction of society. Knowledge without a cause is missing the national soul. The mission and cause for which we created the CUCC is to contribute to the strengthening of professional ethical capacity and the quality of outreach. Subsequently, we set up a training course with 200 participants at a time. We are now focusing on three major tasks.
