The meeting took place on August 6, 2020 at the Ministry of Health, with the participation of representatives of the United Nations and the World Health Organization.
According to the spokesperson and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, Dr. O Vandin, "This is an important meeting to explain to the embassies in Cambodia to be aware of the health measures that have been put in place. "Recently, in facilitating diplomats, especially in working together to prevent the spread of smallpox 19 to the community."
Ms. O Vandin said that the introduction of revised health measures applied to diplomats and partner organizations within the UN cluster holding diplomatic A and B official visas to further facilitate Better to travel to Cambodia.
However, a number of other health measures are still in place, arriving in Cambodia immediately, despite the fact that 72 negative Kovid 19 certificates have been issued, all tests are required, with the exception of one, except for diplomats and partner organizations. A special place for both testing and accommodation waiting for test results.
(Kampong Chhnang): The Cambodian Red Cross, with Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia, Kong Prathap as the Honorary President and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen as the President, always cares and seeks to help. Relieve the suffering of the people.
In fact, on August 6, 2020, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen sent Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross to visit and provide humanitarian aid to alleviate the hardships in the situation of Kovid-19. To the most vulnerable 367 families (50 Khmer-Muslim families) living in Rolea Bier and Kampong Tralach districts, Kampong Chhnang province.
