National Committee for Disaster Management Holds a Workshop on Disaster Risk Reduction
(Phnom Penh): The National Committee for Disaster Management and the United Nations Development Program (UNDP) on August 6, 2020, held a workshop on data reporting for the SANDI Framework for Risk Reduction Monitoring Indicators. Disaster 2015-2030.
The workshop was held at the Cambodiana Hotel and was chaired by Mr. Lam Heng Huot, Deputy Chairman and Secretary-General of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management.
Participants in this workshop were representatives of relevant ministries / institutions, including: Ministry of Health, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, Ministry of Rural Development, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Representatives of Departments Relevant provinces and provincial disaster management committees.
The CamDi database has been made public by the National Committee for Disaster Management (NCDC) and the data is open to relevant ministries, agencies, planners and researchers. Free to use.
The CamDi database provides data and information for development planning, assisting them in their management decisions to mitigate the impact of disasters by raising awareness.
Mr. Lam Heng Huot thanked the representatives of relevant ministries and institutions for their participation and cooperation in the past and encouraged the whole workshop to review and discuss the input of the study results. Evaluate the need to develop this Camdi system better. The workshop ended with an atmosphere of close cooperation and solidarity.
