Ministry of Labor launches first online training system for TVET under the auspices of the Swiss agency SDC
(Phnom Penh): The Swiss Agency for Development and Cooperation (SDC) has contracted with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to support a project to establish a remote or online training system for technical and vocational education and training institutions (TVET). A new tool to help young Cambodians during the spread of Kovid-19 and the future.
Mr. Pech Sophoan told reporters that this is another new development project of the Swiss SDC, which will run for 10 months from August 2020 to May 2021.
Mr. Pech Sophoan expressed the expectation that within 10 months, both sides would achieve a remote or online training system for TVET, claiming that although Cambodia has passed the Kovid stage, the implementation Through this distance training mechanism continues.
The Permanent Secretary of State said that this distance training mechanism includes enrollment, learning and teaching, as well as the management and distribution of teaching materials to trainees, which makes it easier for them to acquire knowledge. High skills, although some of them live far away from the countryside.
This new mechanism differs from the previous training in that in the past, if the trainees did not listen or were not clear at any point, it would not be easy for the teacher to re-teach, but this online learning Will produce a video clip for teaching and distribute to all participants so that even if they do not see or not clear where they can watch the video clip many times.
