General knowledge! It will be 115 years before the world knows exactly who made the first phone
(World): From 1889 to 2004, the world was confused for 115 years about the person who invented the first mobile phone, while this important device in everyday life was first developed from 1854, not in 1874.
In 1871, Antonio applied for a patent for the Telephony at the U.S. Intellectual Property Office, but he owed $ 10 more to complete the "full" patent service, and he owed it first. Only "temporary" intellectual property.
Unfortunately, Antonio also fell ill when a ship's steam tank exploded while en route to Staten Island. Because he did not speak much English in the United States and needed money for physical therapy, he could not afford to pay $ 10 to complete his first device patent protection.
While the litigation was still unresolved, Antonio died before his death, and Alexander became the victor in 1889 and was named the world's first maker of mobile devices. .
It was not until 2004 that some US lawmakers sought justice for Antonio and achieved what they set out to do. Since then, the world has known for sure that it was Antonio Messi who invented the first telephone in 1854. Two road cleaning vehicles and more than 20,000 masks donated by the people of Yunnan Province, China to be handed over to Siem Reap Provincial Administration
