The crackdown took place at 1:15 pm on August 6, 2020, under the direction of Dr. Kun Nhim, General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, and under the direct command of the Director of the Department of Crime Prevention and Suppression. .
It should be noted that the owner of the car, Mao Vannak, alias Sokea, has been smuggling duty-free cars in the past, often using high-tech tricks to confuse the authorities, however, he could not escape the mobile customs authorities in Area 6.
This highly skilled trader hired skilled drivers to drive at speeds of 150 to 160 km / h in rainy and dark skies, regardless of the danger to others.
According to the confession of the owner and the driver, he smuggled 17 to more than 20 cars from Vietnam per month, using the National Police license plate to equip every car during the import activity.
Please note that the name Mao Vannak used to be a mobile customs officer in Area 1 seized a duty-free car that this name had already been smuggled in the past.
According to the confessions of the traders, the smuggler of another duty-free car was named Bun Thoeun, who was cracked down on by the customs authorities and is still being hunted.
Currently, the vehicle is stored at the mobile customs location in Ponhea Krek, Tbong Khmum province to record customs violations according to procedures. Senior Agriculture Official: Pailin lentils, durian, fragrant coconut and radish are considered as priority crops for the Chinese market (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ngin Chhay, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, stated the four priority crops that the Royal Government has identified as priority goods for further negotiations and exports to China. From the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement signed and officially launched.
Mr. Ngin Chhay made the statement at a press conference on "Measures to promote agricultural products to the world market" on the morning of August 6, 2020, organized by the Government Spokesperson's Unit.
"I also hope that after we negotiate free trade with China and other crops will grow, both production and processing and exports of Pailin will be put in the crop," he said. "Preference is given to durian, fragrant coconut, and saliva, as a priority for the Chinese market."
Currently, Cambodia's agricultural products that can be exported to China include: rice, cassava slices, cashew nuts, bananas and mangoes.
Mr. Ngin Chhay also stated that organic vegetables are also a commodity that the Royal Government is paying attention to promote exports by targeting the market.
At the same time, the senior official of the Ministry of Agriculture also mentioned the agricultural products that will be targeted for export, which include organic rice, red rice, cassava, while Cambodia's fresh bananas are very popular in China.
According to the report of the Ministry of Agriculture, in the first seven months of 2020, Cambodia exported 2,689,685 tons of agricultural products to international markets.
Cambodia's agricultural markets include China, Thailand, Vietnam, India, Europe, Japan, Russia, Australia and more.
Cambodia is building a project to develop the Dountry Dam by digging a tunnel in Rukkiri district, Battambang province, which can irrigate nearly 40,000 hectares of agricultural land.
(Battambang): After inspecting the Sala Ta On Dam Development Project in Battambang City, on August 6, 2020, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, continued to visit Daun Try Dam Development Project. Located in Rukkiri district, Battambang province.
According to the Ministry of Water Resources, the main infrastructure of the Dontry Dam Development Project that has been implemented includes:
During his visit to the project, the Minister stated, "The Dontri Dam Development Project is a historic new irrigation system for Cambodia, which is a large dam that requires the use of new methods never implemented in Cambodia In the past, such as: digging tunnels in the mountains, digging rocks in unfavorable geological conditions and methods to strengthen the bottom of the dam.
The minister added that the project not only provides water to increase agricultural production in both the rainy season and the dry season, but also contributes to the supply of clean water and reduce flooding in some areas in the lower reaches. In addition, the Dountry Dam will be able to partially supply water for irrigation to downstream projects such as the Po Kanal Sub-project and the Reamkun sub-project through the Dountry River.
At the same time, the Minister instructed all working groups to take care of their health and adhere to hygiene in accordance with the rules and declarations of the Ministry of Health for the spread of Kovid-19 disease. National Center for Drug Addiction Services in Sihanoukville Launches, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan Says It Will Be a Multidisciplinary Human Resource Training Center for the Cambodian Market
(Preah Sihanouk): Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, President of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, affirmed that the National Center for Voluntary and Community-Based Medical Services in Preah Sihanouk Province will be a multi-skilled human resource training center to serve To the job market in Cambodia in the future.
General Chuon Sovann, Deputy Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Chairman of the National Center Construction Committee, reported on the progress of the construction of the center with the infrastructure of the original water treatment plant.
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan added: "This national center will be a center that provides training, production of multi-skilled human resources to serve the labor market in Cambodia and asked the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to provide agricultural technical equipment for Training in agricultural skills at this national center.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan requested all relevant ministries and institutions to work together to launch the National Center for Voluntary and Community-Based Medical Services in Sihanoukville in November 2020 to reduce Congestion prevents the spread of Kovid-19 disease at temporary centers.
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan said that with the construction of this National Center by the Royal Government of Thailand, we will put this National Center into operation at the same time as the 70th anniversary of the friendship and solidarity between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Kingdom of Thailand.
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan thanked friendly countries for providing construction assistance and commended the relevant ministries' center building committees for jointly building infrastructure achievements in the center and encouraging the deputy prime minister to provide support to the construction team. Workers working on construction at the National Center as well. Director of Fisheries Administration tells people to raise fish, do not be afraid of no place to sell (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, recently encouraged farmers to increase the raising of fish or frogs for food and trade to earn a living.
After receiving this instruction, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries through the Fisheries Administration, which is in charge of this work, has been trying to disseminate and guide the people about some skills and techniques, especially some target provinces set out in the Northeast.
Along with the promotion of raising fish and frogs, there are also concerns that people raise a lot and can not find a place to sell.
Responding to this concern, Mr. Eng Chea San, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Fisheries Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, told people not to worry about prices and markets, because the Ministry has already considered this issue, what is important The people themselves have to work hard to raise fish or frogs to get a good yield.
At a press conference on agricultural markets organized by the Royal Government Spokesperson on August 6, 2020, Mr. Eng Chea San emphasized that "at harvest, prices will not fall, the Ministry has taken action. According to the technique, that is, to divide the time.
He said, for example, that for each target province, the Ministry will arrange for the people to raise one by one, that is, not all at once, so when the harvest will be done one after another. He also acknowledged that if the ministry does not allocate time, it is clear that once harvested, prices will fall.
The Royal Government delegate in charge of the Fisheries Administration noted that in recent years, the aquaculture sector in Cambodia has increased by about 20 percent. Production in 2019 collected 307,400 tons, supplied the domestic market and exported to some neighboring countries.
Mr. Eng Chea San also claimed that along with the strong revival of fish and frog farming, the Fisheries Administration also has measures to prevent imports from neighboring countries. Preventing imports from neighboring countries is part of ensuring that local prices do not fall during the harvest, which could affect people's interests.
During his visit to the Center for Research and Development of Fish Breeding and Conversation with Farmers in Peam Ro District, Prey Veng Province, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, appealed to the workers in the garment and tourism sector who lost their livelihood. Jobs turn to fish farming and the government will provide capital.
Military detains young man after digging roof of mobile phone repair shop in Poipet
(Banteay Meanchey): The military police force of Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province, searched and arrested a man after digging the roof of a mobile phone repair shop and stealing a lot of mobile phones and spare parts.
The victim, Snguon Piseth, a 27-year-old man living in the night market, Palilei 1 Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Mr. Nuon Ninaro said that the suspects and exhibits were sent by the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie to the Provincial Gendarmerie Headquarters for further action.
The suspect confessed in front of the military that he actually dug the roof of a mobile phone repair shop and took the phone and accessories. Based on the confession, including the exhibits, the Provincial Armed Forces, the Bureau of Criminal Investigation sent the suspects and exhibits to the provincial court for legal proceedings.
Sala Ta On Dam Development Project in Battambang Province Can Supply 15,000 Hectares of Water for Irrigation, Minister of Water Resources Inspects 70% of Construction Site
(Battambang): Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, inspected the development project of Sala Ta On Dam located in Battambang City, Battambang Province on Thursday morning. August 06, 2020 Accompanied by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State and Technical Officers of the Ministry together with the Board of Governors of Battambang Province, Director of Battambang Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology.
The Sala Ta On Dam Development Project is a concession financing project of the Republic of Korea. Construction of the project began in January 2019 and is scheduled for completion in June 2021.
As of today, the work has achieved about 70% of the total workload of the project. After the construction is completed, the Sala Ta On Dam development project will be able to supply water for irrigation on 11,000 hectares of wet paddy land and 4,000 hectares of dry paddy land.
(Phnom Penh): At a time when Cambodia, as well as the rest of the world is facing the Kovid-19 crisis, there are 61 Technical and Vocational Education and Training Institutions (TVETs) across the country trying to overcome the obstacles posed by the crisis. Transformed into an online distance training system, consistently implemented by the Ministry of Health.
This was confirmed by Mr. Pich Sophoan, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training during the appointment and transfer ceremony of the Director of the Institute of Agricultural Industrial Technology on the morning of August 6, 2020 at the meeting room of the Institute of Agricultural Industrial Technology, including Mr. Chin Tara. Appointed Director of the New Industrial Technical Institute, replacing Mr. Moan Sam Oeun, who has been assigned a new task.
On that occasion, Mr. Pich Sophoan said that the Ministry of Labor has urged all institutions to organize training remotely (Online) to keep up with technology and develop themselves up to date. As of July, a total of 61 technical and vocational education and training institutions have been trained, including 34 public institutions, 17 private institutions and 10 associations.
He stressed that in the current situation, Cambodia as well as the whole world is really struggling to achieve the plan set out due to the severe impact of Kovid-19, which is a global concern.
He added that despite the above problems, the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister has not slowed down its reform and development work. Instead, consider the circumstances of this crisis as an opportunity to push for more proactive reforms in response to the crisis and to sharpen the competitiveness of the national economy in order to promote the fundamental diversification of sustainable growth for a period of time. Long too.
