Former Deputy Director General of Atomic Capital Financial Institution CCHR in the case of embezzlement of more than $ 8 million was released on bail by the Court of Appeal
(Phnom Penh): After the Investigative Chamber of the Court of Appeal decided to release one of the three defendants in the case of embezzlement of more than $ 8 million of the financial institution of the Capital Petroleum Securities Co., Ltd. was released this morning. On August 6, 2020, the victim expressed his concern and urged the Attorney General of the Prosecutor General of the Court of Appeal to review and appeal the decision.
The plaintiff's insistence is due to the fact that the plaintiff believes that the decision to release the accused Ouk Kiriratanak may further harm the interests of the victim, as the defendant may evade liability. In addition, the accused may have the opportunity to destroy evidence and threaten witnesses as he is being sued in up to three other cases at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
Please be informed that the decision to release the accused Ouk Kiriratanak, male, 34 years old, former Deputy Director General of Atomic Capital Financial Institution CCHR, was temporarily released on bail by the Investigative Chamber of the Court of Appeal. The investigating judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court has already rejected the defendant's bail application.
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng Sar, instructed the specialized departments to introduce or eliminate all illegal gas stations in Phnom Penh in order to reduce the risk of accidents of the people by any means.
In the meeting of Phnom Penh Capital Council this morning, August 6, 2020, the Governor of Phnom Penh advised the relevant departments to cooperate with the 14 Khan authorities to inspect gas stations to understand the legal aspects, technical equipment, standards and Protective equipment to ensure that the business does not disturb or endanger the people and the environment.
