Senior Minister Sun Chanthol vows to build strong roads, not to damage the face after damaging the face or to inject a thin layer of thick film
(Banteay Meanchey): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, presented the position and principles of the Ministry in building a strong road that can be used for a long time, that is, not to damage the face after damage or injection. Thin, thick, thick, thick, thin.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol's strong statement on the quality of such roads was made on the occasion that he led a delegation to meet with civil servants, workers of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Banteay Meanchey Province with the participation of the President. Provincial Council, Provincial Governor and leaders, civil servants, staff and workers of the Department of Public Works and Transport, about 100 people.
Speaking at the event, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol highlighted the importance of the construction project to expand and improve the quality of major national roads in Cambodia and the main infrastructure projects, including: 1st, 2nd and 3rd ring roads. Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway Phnom Penh-Bavet Expressway, Stung Trang Bridge, Kratie Bridge, Sihanoukville Multi-Purpose Port and Deep Sea Port.
The senior minister added that this principle must be strictly implemented through the use of intensive inspection mechanisms and the establishment of special inspection teams to monitor the construction of construction companies and technical consultants.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol spoke about the benefits of using automated systems to provide public services to the people effectively, quickly, transparently, reduce informal costs, as well as to bring public services closer to the people, such as: Chheak Mobile and establish driver's license exchange and renewal centers at both Aeon Mall and Chip Mong.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also encouraged all leaders and civil servants of the Department of Public Works and Transport to strengthen internal solidarity, cooperate with departments around the province and listen to the instructions of the provincial administration to further strengthen this sector. Another level.
The Senior Minister expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the leaders and civil servants of the Department of Public Works and Transport for their hard work in serving the public with a high level of concern and for making this sector possible. To make significant progress as well.
