(Kandal): Mr. Ou Chheang, Governor of Kien Svay District, Kandal Province, warned to take legal action and immediately stop the illegal activities of a group of people, dragging dozens of people to seize their land in Banteay Dek commune. Which can lead to unrest at the grassroots level.
Speaking to Fresh News in Kandal province on the evening of August 5, 2020, the governor of Kien Svay district confirmed that a group of people had incited people to encroach on other people's land in Banteay Dek commune and that it was illegal. So please stop immediately because it leads to unrest.
Due to this problem, the district governor recently held a public forum to explain to the people to understand the procedures and geography of the land in this area, especially focusing on personal ownership, the landowners have had the correct title deed since 2017. He said, however, that the people accused the district governor of conspiring with wealthy merchants and increasing their activities without fear of the law.
The district governor said that if he received a complaint from the landowner on this case, he would deal with the procedure.
Meanwhile, residents who have land titles in the area told Fresh News that they were very worried because the land was bought from the landowners at full price and had a certificate from the special authorities. There is also a valid title deed. If those people continue this kind of activity, it will be like robbing alive.
