(Phnom Penh): The Standing Committee of the National Assembly on the morning of August 6, 2020 held a meeting to review the request for approval of three draft laws proposed by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The meeting was held at the National Assembly Palace under the chairmanship of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Krey Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, with the participation of representatives of the 10 committees of the National Assembly.
The three draft laws that are on the agenda of the National Assembly for review in today's meeting include: 1. The draft law on the management, use and management of state property. 2. The draft law on the management of commercial gambling. Action 3: Draft Law on the Approval of the Treaty on Legal Aid in the Criminal Field between Cambodia and South Korea.
After reviewing these three agendas, the National Assembly Standing Committee under the decision of the President of the National Assembly, who chairs the meeting, will distribute these draft laws to the relevant specialized committees of the National Assembly for review and study before submitting them to Agenda for the plenary session of the National Assembly.
