General knowledge: Plato scholar is the founder of the first philosophy university in Europe
* Biography of Plato:
Plato's life before the founding of the University:
Fortunately, a rich man bought him freedom and sent him back to Athens. Arrived in Athens in 387 BC, Plato established the first philosophical university in Europe. He worked there for about 20 years.
Plato University:
Around 387 BC, when Plato was 40 years old, he returned to Athens and founded the University of Philosophy outside the city, which housed a group of about 10 Greeks named Acedmus. . While working at the university in the middle of the field, Plato taught many students from all over the Greek world (including about 10 other students from other countries).
* Plato's famous philosophy:
Plato's view claims that the world is made up of two elements: the world of vision and matter. The world of philosophy does not refer to the structure of ideas, but to the real world that expresses reality. Physicalism, on the other hand, has no truth in its evolution.
Plato showed that "no matter is immutable, loses its state, only change does not change", meaning that only the worldview is real and unchanging, while matter is ambiguous. There is no truth, it does not respond to its physical condition all the time.
