(Phnom Penh): Ms. Koy Pisey, Deputy Director of the Permanent Secretariat of the National Authority for Border Affairs, on August 5, 2020, expressed her deep regret for the rebels who slandered and polluted society beyond reality on border issues. Cambodia-Vietnam.
Ms. Koy Pisey's remarks came after opposition groups painted the Royal Government of Cambodia to cut off land to Vietnam by accepting a land border map with a scale of 1/25,000.
Ms. Koy Pisey said: "The great achievements of the nation and our loyalty to the motherland have been slandered by the rebels beyond thinking. For the sake of gain, they throw away all the virtues, trample on the honest, deceive the weak with poison. "Their evil deeds, this land may not recognize them."
On August 1, 2020, Cambodia and Vietnam held a handover ceremony to receive a 125,000 scale land border map, a modern digital map.
The handover ceremony took place at the Mok Bai International Border Crossing in Tay Ninh province, Vietnam, where the Cambodian delegation was led by Mr. Var Kimhong, Senior Minister in charge of Border Affairs and Chairman of the Joint Boundary Commission and erected border posts. Cambodia and the Vietnamese delegation led by Mr. Le Hui Trung, Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs and Chairman of the Joint Commission on Boundaries and Land Boundaries of Vietnam.
Ms. Koy Pisey stated that the map of the Cambodia-Vietnam border sign on the scale of 1/25,000 fully showed the results of the demarcation and demarcation of the border, which is about 84% achieved by both countries.
She added that this map is a modern digital map 4.0 that clearly shows the boundary line, border posts, as well as the actual geographical situation on the ground, easy to use, unlike the 1 / 100,000 scale carbon map with only the border line. And nothing more specific.
Please note that Cambodia-Vietnam has a land border with a length of 1,270 kilometers. On October 5, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Nguyen Suon Phuc, Prime Minister of Vietnam, signed an agreement to recognize the two countries' border posts, which reached 84%.
The signing of the border post of the two countries is another new historical event for Cambodia and Vietnam. Separately, the remaining border issues, both sides also continue to resolve to resolve and complete the border demarcation of the border.
