The technical team is planting poles and repairing the medium voltage (MV) line to connect the electricity to the customers for re-use before 20:30 tonight. China expresses displeasure over UN leak over North Korea
The Chinese government on Tuesday (New York time) expressed outrage and concern over the leak of a draft secret report of the United Nations (UN) on North Korea. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Wednesday evening, August 5, 2020.
A spokesman for China's Permanent Mission to the United Nations said: "The report for mid-2020, drafted by experts of the 1718 Security Council Committee, has leaked to the media and caused the media to conclude. I'm not sure what to do. "China expresses its deep dissatisfaction and concern over this issue."
"Similar incidents have taken place in the past, and some member states, including China, have also expressed concern," the spokesman said. "Therefore, China urges the UN to pay more attention to this issue and avoid future document leaks."
