Spokesman for the General Commission: On August 5, another 1,337 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 97 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to August 5, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 129,560 vehicles, including 96,050 motorcycles and 33,510 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet offense, sign offense, no license plate, overtaking, no license plate and drunkenness. In particular, the offenses for cars are mostly speeding, overcrowding, no belts, offenses, no license plates, overweight, no driver's license, use the phone and so on.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 97 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for August 5, 2020, traffic accidents throughout Cambodia also occurred 6 times, in which 1 person died, 9 people were injured (05 people were seriously injured).
Senior Minister Kun Kim Instructs to Accelerate Procedures for Providing Social Land Concessions in Samaki Meanchey District to Veterans
(Kampong Chhnang): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, accompanied by Mr. Thun Thoeun, President of the Provincial Veterans Association, inspected the location of social land concessions for the Armed Forces and their families located in Kraing Lvea Village, Kraing Lvea Commune. Samaki Meanchey District, Kampong Chhnang Province.
During his visit on August 5, 2020, Senior Minister Kun Kim instructed the Cambodian Veterans Association of Kampong Chhnang Province to cooperate with relevant institutions to expedite the procedure to hand over land to veterans who really lack land in Kampong Chhnang Province.
In order to expedite the management and settlement of land provided by the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Senior Minister Kun Kim recommended to the provincial association leaders to appoint a committee with all relevant departments as members, led by a deputy provincial governor. To manage the demarcation.
In addition, Senior Minister Kun Kim advised to update the solution to solve the problem based on the principle of win-win and to pave the road to hand over the lot to the members of the association who do not have real land and houses.
According to the report of Mr. Thun Thoeun, President of the Provincial Veterans Association, in the first half of 2020, the Association has settled the payment of death allowances to the families of 42 veterans' bodies equal to 168 million Riels and built a house for Samdech Techo Hun Sen donated 2 houses to poor veterans and handed over 9 houses that were built and given to members to live in.
According to Mr. Thun Thoeun, so far, veterans from all over the province have received 266 houses donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Association, including 44 stone houses. Separately, 43 families who are homeless and have unsuitable houses have to be dealt with by the association. In addition, there are 153 homeless families who are preparing social land concessions for them.
