Police crack down on more than 10 tons of illegal cosmetics in Boeung Keng Kang
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Economic Crimes Department, in cooperation with the Boeung Keng Kang District Police Inspectorate, on the afternoon of August 4, 2020, raided a place for storing and distributing illegal and infringing cosmetics in Group 24 Village. 03 Sangkat Toul Svay Prey I, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh.
According to the police, with the permission of Mr. MOT Dara, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and with the approval of the owner of the location, the specialized force inspected the above location in front of the joint police in connection with the suspected case. Import, distribution and distribution of cosmetic products infringing on intellectual property and various types of illegal products.
Police inspected the location of house 12B and found 1,040 cases of soap, equivalent to 11,112 kilograms, 3,500 kilograms of toothbrushes and 480 kilograms of cosmetics.
After inspecting, the police found that some products were counterfeit, counterfeit, the source of production and did not have the correct identification number, so the joint authorities decided to temporarily confiscate them by placing them in the ground floor room and the attic floor of the house No. 12B, Street 328, Sangkat Toul Svay Prey I, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh.
As for the other exhibits, which are undocumented goods from the Ministry of Health, therefore, the joint authority decided to detain and temporarily confiscate them, handing them over to the owner of the location to manage not to lose or distort the original shape for further research and pending a decision from the institution. Court.
In addition, the joint authorities confiscated 2 bottles or 2 pieces per sample for inspection. Separately, the owner of the location, Moeun Sok Sitha, was invited to clarify at the Department of Economic Crimes to continue the procedure.
