According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 96 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 49, from May 1 to August 4, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 128,223 vehicles, including 94,989 motorcycles and 33,234 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet offense, offense, no license plate and drunkenness. In particular, the offenses for cars are mostly speeding, overcrowding, no belts, offenses, no license plates, overweight, using mobile phones and so on.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 96 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for August 4, 2020, traffic accidents throughout the country also occurred 7 times, in which 5 people died, 8 people were injured (4 seriously injured). During the 96 days, a total of 744 traffic accidents, including 401 deaths, 1,154 injuries (679 serious injuries).
