* First: Judges, prosecutors, as well as all court officials must adhere to the five noble approaches of Samdech Techo Prime Minister: "Mirror, bathe, scrub, treat and operate" as a principle in performing the functions and duties of As well as in leading the tribunal unit.
* Second: Judges, prosecutors, as well as all court officials must adhere to their strictness in applying the law properly in order to provide an impartial trial to ensure fairness to the people in particular. Abstinence from the four virtues: will, will, guilt, delusion, and delusion, as all judges and prosecutors have sworn in before taking office.
* Third: Judges, prosecutors, as well as all court officials must participate in promoting the honor, dignity and prestige of the judiciary by strictly adhering to the discipline and professional ethics of judges and prosecutors during their work. In daily life.
Adherence to its professional ethics is an important contribution to the promotion of the honor and dignity of the judiciary itself, and it is an indispensable contribution to strengthening public trust in the judiciary.
* Fourth: Judges, prosecutors, as well as all court officials must participate with a high will and a sense of responsibility in the implementation of the campaign to resolve the congestion in the Capital-Provincial Courts, launched by the Ministry of Justice yesterday. May 18th, by implementing correctly and strictly according to the "fast, accurate, fair and non-corrupt" approach.
* Fifth: Judges, prosecutors as well as all court officials must pay attention to the performance of work by strengthening internal unity and strengthening good cooperation with relevant authorities and institutions to ensure the proper functioning of the judiciary as well Effective service of justice to the people.
