Parents should be extremely careful! A 3-year-old girl was electrocuted to death after taking an ax and breaking a power line in Khsach Kandal district
This incident happened in Prey Thom village, Sanlong commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province at 9 am on August 4, 2020.
The victim was a 3-year-old girl named Panha Srey La who lived with her parents in the commune where the incident took place. Prior to the incident, the girl's father went to work as usual, while the girl stayed at home with her mother. At the time of the incident, the girl's mother went out to buy food, leaving the girl alone.
When the mother disappeared, the daughter pulled out the light plug left on the bed, fell to the ground, and played with the ax. Caused a break and also tried to interfere, was shocked to death alone at the scene.
When the mother returned and found the child lying on the ground, she was taken to a nearby hospital. But doctors said Panha Sreila was dead.
Immediately after receiving the information, police officers and local authorities came down to examine the body and sent the girl's body to the family for a traditional ceremony at home. Takeo Provincial Police Chief Leads Forces to Strengthen Cross-Border Management and Inspection to Prevent the Outbreak of Kovid 19
(Takeo): On the morning of August 4, 2020, Major General Sok Samnang, Takeo Provincial Police Commissioner, visited and disseminated the announcement of the Ministry of Interior to the 603rd Border Guard Police Force. Strengthen the management and control of border crossings to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia to all 603 Border Police officers.
On that occasion, the General Commissioner also donated 4 tons of rice and 100 boxes of noodles to Border Police Force No. 603 as a precious gift from General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General at the meeting hall of the Defense Police Battalion. Land border No. 603.
It should be noted that on July 31, 2020, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, issued an official letter to the Provincial Governor and Chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command bordering Vietnam. Cross-border access control to prevent the spread of Vid 19 in Cambodia.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng confirmed that there has been an outbreak of 19 cases of cholera in some parts of Vietnam and that Vietnamese authorities have been taking steps to close access to the area. Also. In this spirit, in order to cooperate in the prevention of the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia, Samdech would like to advise the provincial governor and chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command to pay attention to the following work:
* Continue to promote education, guidance and dissemination to the public and local people, especially people living in border areas to increase vigilance in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 virus. Individuals and local communities in Cambodia. Veterans Association is studying the possibility of providing safe vegetable cultivation to veterans.
(Kandal): Officials of the Cambodian Veterans Association see vegetable growing as a new mechanism to contribute to supporting and improving the lives of Cambodian veterans. The association has also been looking for ways to support and encourage veterans' vegetable cultivation.
On August 4, 2020, Major General Kim Sopharun, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian Veterans Association, and Mr. Kim Rithy, Deputy Governor of Kandal Province, inspected the management of organic vegetable production in the safe green vegetable farming community in the commune. Teuk Vil, Saang District, Kandal Province.
The purpose of this visit is to find out about the work on this work to study the feasibility of a project to help improve the lives of veterans who are members of the association.
The community leader gave a presentation on the history of the community, the management of the services and the achievements of the community over the past three years.
Mr. Phay Pros, a model farmer, has shown interest and success in family life since he switched from growing vegetables using chemicals to growing natural green vegetables as instructed and studied with the Kandal Provincial Department of Agriculture.
The model farmer pointed out that now his income has increased by harvesting six times a year, and this natural green vegetable has a high market demand, with buyers to collect on the spot.
After listening to the presentation and learning about the safe green vegetable farming community, the Deputy Governor and Major General Kim Sopharun and his entourage inspected the natural green vegetable garden.
Major General Kim Sopharun praised the chemical-free vegetable cultivation techniques of the people in Saang district. He said he was studying the possibility to share the experience and knowledge of growing chemical-free vegetables to veterans and find ways to support their cultivation. Mr. Huy Vannak expressed his interest in the battle of public opinion (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): In the morning of August 4, 2020, Mr. Huy Vannak, President of the Federation of Cambodian Journalists, spoke at a press conference to evaluate the activities of the press conference on the work progress in 2019 and the work direction for 2020 of the Ministry, Institutions and Capital-Provincial Administration on the morning of August 4, 2020. Express interest in connection with the battle of public opinion.
In expressing his interest, Mr. Huy Vannak advised that as a journalist, you must be good at asking questions and learn to find important questions to ask important people or speakers. He gave an idea of who the speaker is today. What is the problem behind it? And research to find out what to ask.
Mr. Huy Vannak also encouraged journalists to participate in disseminating what is a national achievement and participate in building with patience, understanding and mutual complement. Agricultural authorities and officials launch a campaign to vaccinate cattle to prevent infectious diseases
(Kampong Cham): Kampong Cham Provincial Authority led by Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Un Chanda this morning, August 4, 2020, launched a campaign to vaccinate cattle to prevent various infectious diseases in Doung village, Tong Rong commune, Prey Chhor district.
Kampong Cham Provincial Governor said that every year in August, agricultural officials always carry out vaccination of cattle on the backs of people's houses before the floods, because when there is a flood, cattle are easy. There will be three diseases: dehydration, foot-and-mouth disease and pneumonia.
The provincial governor continued that although in modern times, some farmers have access to machinery, but there are still many farmers who are using cattle to engage in agricultural work, that is, cattle are really productive. Great benefits to farmers.
He said that the provincial authorities, especially the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, have set out an annual plan to vaccinate animals in all areas in Kampong Cham to prevent cattle from dying from the disease. To cause serious losses to farmers.
According to the provincial governor, the agricultural sector in Cambodia, even before or after the outbreak of Kovid 19, is still important for more than 60% of the population engaged in agriculture, especially expecting Cattle are the driving force, he said, and that is why the authorities have taken care to protect the health of cattle as the main point, because those animals can help a lot to lead people to have a better life.
The provincial governor pointed out that through the experience of rice cultivation in the past year, seeing that in some areas, farmers can grow rice up to three times a year because they have enough water sources to improve their livelihoods. He is rich because his rice yield is an average of 6 tons per hectare.
He added that in some areas, the rice was damaged by the drought and also had no water source, with rice farmers relying entirely on rain. Therefore, the provincial authorities plan in 2022 and divert road development to Irrigation development to provide farmers with sufficient water sources to grow crops in the agricultural sector.
