(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Justice is working to legalize and protect a Cambodian woman who was sentenced to death by a Vietnamese court by trying to escape the death penalty.
This is the assertion of Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, on August 4, 2020, on the occasion of presiding over the International Day against Drug Abuse on June 26 and burning drugs and other artifacts in Svay Rieng province.
Mr. Keut Rith said that "the Ministry of Justice strives to check and legally protect the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to comply with the bilateral agreement to avoid the death penalty." This is the additional confirmation of the Minister of Justice.
According to the Vietnamese VNA, during the conclusion of the hearing on July 31, 2020, the Tay Ninh Provincial Court sentenced a Cambodian woman, Mech Srey Neang, to death for drug trafficking from Cambodia to Vietnam. This woman was born in 1993 and lives in Phnom Penh.
Based on the confiscated evidence, Mech Srey Neang smuggled five packages of methamphetamine weighing 4,943 grams. Police arrested the woman at Mokbai International Airport in Tay Ninh province on December 2, 2019.
In this case, Koy Kuong, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, did not dare to detail the intervention of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Vietnam because he said it was an internal matter. However, he confirmed that Cambodia is paying close attention to the Cambodian prisoners.
A senior official of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated: "Currently, according to the information from the Consulate General (Cambodia) in Ho Chi Minh City, the person has filed an appeal, so we can file a complaint at any time during the 15-day procedure." "So the court proceedings continue, not just at the provincial court."
Mr. Koy Kuong also revealed that in connection with this work, Cambodia is trying to find a solution, and because Cambodia and Vietnam have an agreement on the transfer of prisoners, Cambodia also plans to request Mech Neang to return to trial in Cambodia.
