France finally decides to ratify extradition treaty with Hong Kong (Video inside) (Paris): The French government on Monday announced the cancellation of ratification of extradition treaty with Hong Kong after Beijing Introduce new security laws on this former British colony. This is according to the release by CNA on Tuesday morning, August 4, 2020.
"Given the latest developments, France will not proceed with the ratification of the extradition agreement signed on May 4, 2017," the French Foreign Ministry said in a statement. "Between France and Hong Kong." The ministry added that such a decision was due to the new national security law, which would also affect its citizens and businesses.
In addition to France, New Zealand, Canada, Britain, Australia and Germany have already suspended extradition treaties with Hong Kong since the new security law was introduced in June.
