84-year-old grandmother receives justice from Samdech Techo Hun Sen in more than 13 years of land dispute with her children
For many years, Ms. Nhel tried to call her son and son-in-law to mediate the land dispute, but to no avail. Until she asked the village, commune, district authorities to help solve for many more years, but still did not get results. On the other hand, on August 23, 2019, the son and daughter-in-law sued the grandmother and eldest son, Ros Ruon, at the Kandal Provincial Police for "illegal possession of real estate."
After appearing in court, Ms. Im Nhel and her eldest son, Ros Ruon, were allowed to return home because there was not enough evidence. Suddenly, on October 7, 2019, Ms. Im Nhel and her eldest son were summoned by the Kandal Provincial Prosecutor to comment on the case of "violence against the rightful occupants of real estate". It is the exact opposite of what happened to her.
Unable to bear the pain anymore, on July 22, 2020, Ms. Em Nhel decided to apply to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to help find justice for her. Because the previous settlement was ineffective for the 84-year-old who was abused by his son and daughter-in-law.
On the evening of Friday, July 31, 2020, Mr. Duong Dara took the time to meet Ms. Im Nhel and her son and son-in-law at the above land dispute. The son did not agree to anyone to mediate and confirmed that he would not give her land, but could only give her $ 3,000. The mother did not know whether to take it or not. Due to the inability to talk to each other, Mr. Duong Dara invited his son and daughter-in-law to come and talk at the Peace Palace to find a solution.
The grandmother's son agreed to let his wife come and settle the dispute without his presence. If the wife agrees, he agrees.
The money will be used by the grandmother to pay tribute to her husband and son, who sacrificed their lives while serving in the military, as well as to receive a portion of the land above her inheritance. .
Today's mediation for an entire morning was a success that everyone accepted with satisfaction. Mr. Duong Dara stated that if the mediation method can not be compatible, only follow the law to find the right and the wrong, which will take a lot of resources and time, and it is not certain that one party will win alone because The trial is based on all the evidence she has in her hand.
After giving a thumbs up to end the dispute based on the principle of victory over Samdech Techo, local authorities and cadastral officers will go to the site to measure the land for their son and son-in-law to issue a legal title from now on. Go.
Mrs. Im Nhel was very happy and she expressed her deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for giving her the mercy she received at the last minute of her life at the age of 84. Years.
Mr. Duong Dara also expressed his deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Prime Minister for always giving love, compassion and mercy to people of all castes. Because the well-being of the people is the personal well-being of both Samdechs. Mr. Duong Dara wished Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit the best health, longevity and a warm shade for the people all over the country.
At the same time, Mr. Duong Dara also thanked the Governor of Kandal Province, the President of the Provincial Court, the Provincial Police Commissioner, the Prosecutor, the Governor of Khsach Kandal District, the District Cadastral Director and all relevant authorities for their good cooperation. The solution for the people by following the win-win principle of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to succeed together.
Mr. Duong Dara also thanked the volunteer lawyer and Samdech Techo's lawyer who always help to solve the problem for the people regardless of time or profit. He also called on all officials to work together to build good deeds, share love and smiles, and respect people everywhere without discrimination.
