(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of August 3, 2020, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration issued a directive to the 14 Khan administrations under Phnom Penh to take legal action against rallies held without prior written notice. Holds the Phnom Penh Capital Administration. This is according to the instructions received by Fresh News.
The directive comes after the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration observed that in recent days there have been rallies demanding the release of Rong Chhun in connection with the criminal case in front of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. Informed the competent authorities.
In this regard, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has made the following recommendations:
* All rallies must be notified in writing to the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration in accordance with the Law on Peaceful Demonstration and in accordance with the guidelines for the prevention of the spread of Kovid virus - 19.
All rallies without the prior written notice to the Phnom Penh Capital Administration shall be considered illegal and the competent authority shall take action in accordance with the law in force.
* Receiving this instruction, the Director of Administration of Phnom Penh Capital Hall, the Governor of the 14 District Governors, the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, the Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie and all stakeholders must implement with a sense of responsibility and high efficiency.
