SCG strengthens business strategy to win the battle against Kovid-19
(Thailand): SCG has strengthened its business strategy to overcome the battle against Kovid-19 by focusing on agility, agility and sustainable business management in the chemical business sector, leading to growth. Profit in SCG's business results for the second quarter of 2020.
SCG will continue to focus on maintaining long-term business stability, along with the development of aggregate and innovative solutions to meet the needs of the "new normal" era, using digital mechanisms to drive online purchases and boost the packaging business. More in the ASEAN market.
The company's unaudited business results for the second quarter of 2020 recorded a total sales revenue of 12,285 billion riels (US $ 3,006 million), down 12% from the same period last year. Last year, mainly due to lower prices of chemical products, and revenue in this quarter was down 9% compared to the previous quarter due to the decline in all core businesses. .
Profit for the second quarter of 2020 reached 1.201 billion riels (US $ 294 million), an increase of 33% compared to the same period last year, and this increase was due to better performance. Within SCG's three core business units, driven by cost-effectiveness and business sustainability.
Compared to the previous quarter, profits in the second quarter of 2020 increased by 35% due to better results in the company's chemical business. SCG's sales revenue for the first half of 2020 decreased by 9% compared to the same period last year, reaching only 26,012 billion Riels (US $ 6,381 million) due to Declining prices of chemical products.
Profit for the first half of 2020 is down 13% compared to the same period last year, reaching only 2.109 billion riel (US $ 517 million), which is the reason for this profit decline Caused by a decline in profits from the chemical products business during the first quarter of 2020.
