According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, for 93 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to August 1, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 126,113 vehicles, including 93,454 motorcycles and 32,659 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorbikes are mostly without helmets, offenses, without license plates and using mobile phones. In particular, the offenses for cars are mostly speeding, overcrowding, no belts, offenses, no license plates, overweight, using mobile phones and so on.
