(Prey Veng): 38 Vietnamese nationals trying to cross the border to return home through the Koh Roka border checkpoint were detained by Cambodian authorities for 14 days at Koh Roka Secondary School, Peam Chor District, Prey Veng Province on the morning of August 1. This year 2020.
The reason for detaining these Vietnamese is to be a transgender person because they have crossed the border back to their country and are banned.
On July 31, 2020, many Vietnamese families traveled in eight smach boats to cross the border from Cambodia to Vietnam through the Kham Samnor border crossing in Kandal province, according to the Koh Rokar border checkpoint. . Later, they were not allowed to enter by the Vietnamese gate officials, so they turned back, crossing the border through Koh Roka, Prey Veng province.
According to the source, they traveled from three different provinces along the Tonle Sap Lake: five families in Siem Reap, one family in Pursat and one family in Battambang. There were 38 Vietnamese, including 14 adults (7 females) and 24 children (8 females).
At present, the Vietnamese nationals are being allowed to leave Cambodia by professional officers as well as provide food for 14 days in the compound of Koh Roka Secondary School, Peam Chor District, Prey Veng Province.
