Vital Continues to Donate 10 Tons of Rice to Angkor Hospital for Children in 2020
(Siem Reap): Vital Drinking Water Company continues to donate 10 tons of rice per year for 2020 to Angkor Hospital for Children on July 30, 2020.
This is the second year that Vital has donated 10 tonnes of rice to hospitals after the company signed a three-year rice subsidy agreement in 2019, said Chun Heang Thao Sithy, Vital's Chief Commercial Officer. .
"Vital always pays attention to humanitarian activities and our team is well aware of the values of Angkor Hospital for Children, which actively works to save the lives of hundreds of Cambodian children every day," he said.
Mr. Tep Navy, Executive Director of Angkor Hospital for Children, praised Vital, a national model company that always pays attention to humanitarian programs and thanked the company for supporting Angkor Hospital for Children by sponsoring 10 rice. Tons per year. This participation has encouraged the hospital and its team to be more motivated to provide better services for the examination and treatment of Cambodian children while the hospital is in need of this assistance.
