Minister of Justice officially announces the inauguration of Kratie Provincial Court President
(Kratie): Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, on the afternoon of July 31, 2020, presided over the inauguration ceremony of the new President of Kratie Provincial Court.
The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Hoeur Siyem, Chairman of Kratie Provincial Council, Mr. Vathorn, Governor of Kratie Province, members of the Supreme Council of the Magistracy, leaders of the Ministry of Justice, judges, prosecutors, court officials and other government officials.
Mr. Top Chhun Heng, former Deputy Chief of Siem Reap Provincial Court, has been appointed as the new President of Kratie Provincial Court by Royal Decree No. NS / RKOT / 0720/767, dated July 18, 2020, replacing Ms. In Manit. Appointed to the position of Judge of the Court of Appeal of Preah Sihanouk.
Speaking at the ceremony, the Minister instructed Mr. Top Chhun Heng, the new President of Kratie Provincial Court, as well as Mr. Keo Socheat, Prosecutor of Kratie Provincial Court, all court officials and civil servants of Kratie Provincial Court to adhere. The following work methods:
First, judges, prosecutors, as well as all court officials must adhere to the five noble approaches of Samdech Techo Prime Minister: "Mirror, bathe, scrub, treat and operate" as a principle in performing their functions and duties. As well as leading the tribunal unit.
Second, judges, prosecutors, as well as all court officials must adhere to their commitment to the proper application of the law in order to provide an impartial trial to ensure fairness to the people, especially Abstinence from the four virtues is will, guilt, prejudice and delusion, as all judges and prosecutors have sworn in before taking office.
Fourth: Judges, prosecutors, as well as all court officials must participate with a high will and a sense of responsibility in the implementation of the campaign to resolve the congestion in the Capital-Provincial Courts, launched by the Ministry of Justice on This past May 18, by implementing correctly and strictly according to the "fast, accurate, fair and non-corrupt" approach.
Fifth, judges, prosecutors, as well as all court officials and civil servants must pay attention to their work by strengthening internal unity and strengthening good cooperation with relevant authorities and institutions to ensure the proper functioning of the judiciary. As well as the effectiveness of providing justice to the people.
