Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State and spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, said in a press release on the morning of August 1, 2020 that as of July 31, 2020, there were 1,020 cases of chickenpox. In that case, 562 women, or 55 percent. More than 80% of the cases occurred in four provinces: Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Preah Vihear and Kampong Cham.
According to the Secretary of State, there are currently 12 cases of cholera in Siem Reap, Banteay Meanchey, Preah Vihear, Kampong Cham, Oddar Meanchey, Tbong Khmum, Takeo, Kampot, Sihanoukville, Pursat, Stung Treng and Pailin.
Ms. O Vandin quoted Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, as saying that the prevention and control of CHIK is the same as dengue fever, based on the prevention of mosquito bites. By eliminating the water droplets that are the breeding grounds for mosquitoes.
She emphasized that in order to protect the health of chickens from mosquito bites more effectively, the Minister of Health recommended and advised all citizens and local authorities at all levels to increase. Participation and movement to reduce and prevent mosquito breeding through the implementation of the following measures:
* Measure 1: Parents, guardians of all children, including local authorities, must actively participate in getting rid of water worms in places where water is left unused, such as car tires, motorcycles, bottle caps, coconut shells, rice bowls, soup cans, coffee cans, buried or burned. Or demolish or store in a way to prevent waterlogging.
* Measure 2: Adhere to the habit of living clean, clean house, light in and out, store items, clothes, under the house in order to eliminate the forest around the house to reduce the mosquitoes to cling to us. That can easily bite us. During the day it is necessary to wear long-sleeved clothes, sleep under a mosquito net regularly day and night and not to sit near dark places.
* Measure 3: In case of high fever symptoms, immediately take the patient to the state examination and treatment (public service) such as the nearest health center and hospital, do not try to treat patients with high fever. Immediately by yourself or delay treatment in a private service that does not have the ability to dengue at all.
Measure 4: All 25 Capital-Provincial Health Departments must manage the provision of services and clinics in the hospital well and refer patients to other hospitals in case of overcrowding. Ability to stay in any hospital without delay in accessing examination and treatment services.
Measure 5: All 25 Capital-Provincial Health Departments, in collaboration with all relevant parties and development partner organizations within their jurisdiction, review and introduce measures and promote the dissemination of health education messages to prevent epidemics. Outbreaks appear to be exacerbated during pregnancy and in children.
(Hong Kong): Police in Hong Kong have just issued a formal arrest warrant for a total of six activists on suspicion of inciting to threaten national security in violation of security laws. The new nation was just adopted last month. This is according to the release by CGTN on Friday night, July 31, 2020.
They are now under arrest by Hong Kong police on suspicion of separatism and collaborating with foreigners or outside forces to pose a threat to national security, as these acts are strictly prohibited under the new national security law. .
Meanwhile, four Hong Kong students have just been arrested under the new national security law on charges of inciting incitement to national insecurity.
On July 30, 2020, Li Kwai-wah, a police officer from the New National Security Force, said that according to some sources and investigations, the four students had just been announced online. Society to form an organization demanding support for the Hong Kong independence movement but was disbanded by police under a new national security law passed by Beijing.
The new national security law, which was introduced in Hong Kong a month ago, aims to prevent separatism, subversion, terrorism and conspiracy with foreign forces to provoke internal unrest in Hong Kong. Li Kwai-wah added that phones and related documents had been confiscated by police and that all those arrested were students.
