The following is the announcement of the Ministry of Labor: The Director General of Taxation explains the procedure to taxpayers who pay the wrong tax and want to correct it!
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the General Department of Taxation on July 31, 2020 prepared an important article explaining the procedures that taxpayers are responsible for paying taxes to meet the requirements.
The following is the text of an explanation prepared by a senior official of the General Department of Taxation:
Currently, the current tax payment is made through three options: tax payment at the tax unit that governs the enterprise, tax payment at the commercial bank, which is a partner that has signed a memorandum of understanding with the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and Pay taxes online of the General Department of Taxation.
You may have encountered cases of paying the wrong taxes, such as paying the wrong taxes, paying the wrong type of tax, technical errors of tax officials or bank officials.
When you have submitted the receipt to the tax return with the tax officer, but found that the tax amount is wrong, so you need to follow the following points:
* If you pay the tax online E-payment: 1: Apply with the printed receipt online stating the subject and reason to the General Department of Taxation 2: Follow up the application until it is completed 3: Follow the instructions in the letter issued by the General Department of Taxation 4: Then attach the correct receipt to submit the declaration according to the procedure.
The Ministry of Planning found that the son of the commune chief of Roleang Kreul in Kampong Speu province was really poor and had to receive an equity card
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Planning on July 31, 2020, said that the son of the commune chief of Roleang Kreul in Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province is really poor.
The Ministry of Planning's claim came after the news was published and mentioned that the commune chief put his relatives as poor families. Due to such false information, the above commune chief decided to withdraw the equity card from his son named Noy Chamnan.
According to the meeting with the commune council and inspect the house, the family said that the family is very poor and destitute, the head of the family is a widow and has a mental illness, has a son, a car accident, broken leg and broken arm. Became disabled, had orphans in her care, and her past life depended on her daughter working in a factory, but due to the Kovid 19 problem, her daughter lost her job.
According to the results of the actual inspection and the coordination and explanation of the identification procedure for the poor family, the commune councilors understood and agreed to return the equity card to the family.
