Wing Supports National Bank of Cambodia and Ministry of Women's Affairs to Increase Women's Access to Finance
(Phnom Penh): While some women are facing limited access to financial services and financial literacy, Wing Specialized Bank has joined the National Bank of Cambodia and the Ministry of Women's Affairs to boost the number of women accessing finance. Official in Cambodia.
With the participation of 38 staff members from departments around Siem Reap, including the Department of Education, the Department of Women's Affairs and the Department of Commerce and the Women's Development Center, this training aims to promote the use of official financial services and the use of the system. Digital for financial services and to promote outreach aimed at helping local women businesses and businesses.
Ms. Chea Serey said: “Recently, although the financial sector has grown significantly, a large number of women still face challenges in accessing financial services, especially when the knowledge of financial management in business. There is still a limit. ”
Therefore, the National Bank of Cambodia has partnered with the Ministry of Women's Affairs and other stakeholders to promote women's access to official financial services and to use them responsibly and objectively.
"The more women can access financial financing, the more they will be able to contribute to the social, economic, family and community development of their country," she said.
Ms. Chhay Kanha, Senior Product Marketing Manager of Wing Specialized Bank and Coordinator of the training, said that supporting women in the financial sector and encouraging them to become women entrepreneurs is an effective goal. One that can enable women to become national economic developers as well as effective family economies.
When women have jobs and decent incomes, they will have better rights to make decisions, both nationally and sub-nationally, as well as influence society and message groups.
In addition to supporting the National Bank of Cambodia in promoting the increase in the number of women receiving official financial assistance in Cambodia, Wing Specialized Bank has in the past supported the Ministry of Education's "Financial Literacy" program on March 8 with the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the Ministry of Women's Affairs. Collaborate with many other institutions to improve women's financial literacy and promote women's development in the field of financial technology.
Aiming to promote women in the financial sector and women entrepreneurs, Wing Specialized Bank has nearly 8,000 WING agents nationwide, of which 80% are women.
Women are playing an important role in providing financial services everywhere in Cambodia. In addition, female Wing agents are playing an important role in boosting the financial environment in Cambodia and supporting the national economy and families.
