(Phnom Penh): General Chuon Sovann, Deputy Director of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, stated, "You must remember that your family and community can not grow if you continue to use drugs."
This confirmation by General Chuon Sovann was made on the occasion that the General was invited to represent Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, this morning, July 31, 2020, led a working group to visit and Bring food donations to drug victims at the "My Opportunity Center".
General Chuon Sovann stated: "You must remember that your family and community can not grow if you continue to use drugs! "Do not forget that if you leave the drug treatment and rehabilitation center and still do not relapse, still use drugs after the repatriation, so in case of non-relapse, this is not a case of injury."
On that occasion, the General also called on young people affected by drugs in drug treatment and rehabilitation centers across the country to take their opportunities to try to change their lives because the children Everyone is very young, so do not despair of their lives.
General Chuon Sovann continued, "Therefore, the information that some young people who received treatment and drug treatment from the center have relapsed or re-addicted drugs is not true." In this case, young people who have suffered from drugs must be in control of themselves, please do not rush to use drugs as before to improve their lives to shine again.
General Chuon Sovann also reminded the young people who received all the rehabilitation services that you are the pillar of the nation to continue in the future, so please stop it. All illegal activities, especially those related to drug use.
The senior official of the Drug Authority emphasized that all nieces and nephews should seize the opportunity that all of you are receiving drug treatment at all rehabilitation centers, especially to strive to implement all programs. Education, vocational training to turn into good children, good friends and good youth is a great benefit for the family and the whole Cambodian society.
Ms. Mom Chandani said that in the 5th anti-illegal drug campaign in the first half of 2020, "My Opportunity Center" received 2,043 drug victims, including 109 women to receive. Get medical treatment and rehabilitation services.
