Cambodian Muslims in Cambodia Celebrate Raya Hajj with Smiles Under the Shadow of Peace in the Techo Age
(Phnom Penh): The precious smiles that appear on the faces of Cambodian Muslims across the country seem to show the excitement of celebrating the Raya Hajj festival in the Techo era under the shadow of peace, because the observance of the Kovid 19 measures has been implemented. Well done.
The Raya Hajj is one of the major Islamic festivals that Muslims around the world celebrate every year.
In fact, on July 31, 2020, Khmer Muslims organized this celebration with happy smiles under the shadow of peace, because there were no large gatherings in temples or shrines, but the Khmer Muslims are still satisfied because of the measures. Defending Kovid 19 It is important to obey the orders of the leadership.
Ms. Nut Yani and her family, a Cambodian Muslim living in Prek Tapov village, Sangkat Prek Pra, Khan Chbar Ampov, told Fresh News: "Avoid gatherings outside of your family."
The most important thing is Ms. "Thank you for the peace, thank you Samdech Techo Hun Sen, thank the Ministry of Health and all the relevant officials who worked hard day and night without any fatigue, while the results are really the best. Compared to other countries, Cambodia has no large-scale infections, no deaths, which is a great achievement of Samdech Techo Hun and all officials.
She and her family also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for bringing peace, security, prosperity, economic growth, and a more prosperous life while Cambodia was under Samdech Techo's leadership. To this day.
She and her family also called on all Cambodian Muslims to follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to work together to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 virus that has caused problems to the world.
The Cambodian Islamic Supreme Council, headed by Oknha Sos Komri, also issued a notice on the observance of Raya Hajj, while issuing guidelines to all Muslims to participate in the prevention of 19 Kovid virus. Instructed to worship on Raya Day in their respective homes as well.
The most notable thing is that during this festival, many Islamic associations distributed the beef to the Khmer Muslims in their respective communities, as this year there was a shortage of aid from 7,000 in 2019. Below 1,000 in 2020 due to the Kovid 19 virus.
It should be noted that all Muslims in Cambodia have always adhered to the principles of the leaders of the countries and leaders of the relevant institutions to participate in preventing the spread of Kovid 19 from spreading. That the Cambodian Muslims really follow the instructions of the leaders perfectly perfectly.
Drug effects! Man angry with father over drug smoking, angry house set on fire, lost nearly 20,000 dollars
(Banteay Meanchey): A man, due to drugs, came in just because his father told him to stop smoking drugs and went upstairs, suddenly exploded in anger, set fire to a house on the evening of July 30, 2020 in Phnom village Thom Thmey, O'Prasat Commune, Mongkul Borey District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Lt. Col. Bun Pheng, Deputy Commissioner for National Firearms, Explosives and Fire Management, said that the house that was demolished was made of 7 x 8 meters of wood, zinc and stone. The owner was Srem Wutty, 46 years old. Phnom Thom Thmei village, O'Prasat commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province, has 6 family members, 2 females.
According to the Deputy Commissioner, according to the owner of the house, the amount of damage to both the house and household items totaled $ 16,000. Search for arrests and punish them according to the law.
