Preah Sihanouk Provincial Authority Disseminates the Prevention and Suppression of Clearing and Burning Forests in Protected Areas
(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration, led by Mr. Mang Sineth, Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, disseminated measures to prevent and crack down on clearing, logging, forest fires, encroachment, occupation and sale. Purchase of forest land, flooded forest land, mangrove forest land and land in the protected area or forest cover area located in O Thmor area, bordering Prey Nob and Stung Hav districts.
This visit took place on July 30, 2020, with the participation of the Governor of Stung Hav District and a representative of the Forestry Administration.
Following the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, issued a directive to the governors of the five districts of Preah Sihanouk Province to immediately prevent all acts of deforestation and forest encroachment. Or buy or sell illegally.
1: Prevent and immediately suppress all activities of clearing, deforestation, burning of trees in protected areas, forest encroachment, encroachment on forest land, flooded forest land, mangrove forest land, purchase and certification of state land sale and purchase documents
2: Instruct local officials, especially villages and communes, to immediately stop all sale and purchase and confirmation of sale and purchase of state land. 3: In case of finding any person involved in illegal activities as mentioned above, Will build a case to send to court to deal with legal procedures.
It should also be noted that according to Article 97 of the Forestry Law, a person shall be sentenced to imprisonment from five (5) to ten (10) years and all exhibits shall be confiscated as state property to any person who has cleared the forest, cleared the forest. Occupy sterile forest land, pollute and destroy.
