With less than 100 days to go before the election, Donald Trump wants to postpone the election under the pretext of vote rigging.
WASHINGTON, Nov. 3 (Xinhua) - US President Donald Trump on Thursday raised the possibility of postponing the presidential election, which, according to the US Constitution, must take place on Tuesday, November 3, 2020. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, July 30, 2020.
With less than 100 days to go, the US presidential election will be held. As for the election date, the US president has no right to postpone it, as the US Constitution gives Congress the power to set election dates.
