(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, and Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State, Representative of Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, on July 30, 2020, announced the launch of "Message and Location Management System." "Population data on Kovid-19."
Mr. Chea Vandeth said that the message management system and location to receive information and data of the people about Kovid 19 is very important for the general public, as this system will automatically send voice messages to those who suspect It contains 19 Kovid to monitor their own health.
Mr. Chea Vandeth added that through the use of this system, the authorities can identify people suspected of having 19 cases of Kovid and obtain some information and data necessary to identify identifiable individuals. There is a high risk of contracting Kovid 19.
In addition, the Minister of Posts emphasized that this system will help avoid congestion on the existing 115 systems of the Ministry of Health. To allow us to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in a timely and effective manner.
At the same time, Minister Chea Vandeth also requested the working groups of the two ministries to continue to work together to improve and develop this system to be better and expand the scope even more. The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, with its Global Telecommunications Service Obligations Fund, will continue to fully support the development of comprehensive and comprehensive emergency services.
In addition, Mr. Chea Van Det said that the system was completed at a time when the world is facing the second wave of epidemics 19 and he strongly hopes that this system will help. Efforts by Ministry of Health officials, the front line staff of the Royal Government, to effectively prevent the second wave of the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
