Father of Architecture Vann Molyvann sells for $ 7 million
(Phnom Penh): If you travel along Mao Tse Toung Boulevard, you will surely see and admire one of the most unique villas compared to the houses as well as other nearby buildings accompanied by the art of architecture. Modern Khmer This mansion is the mansion of the father of architecture that Cambodians and foreigners alike know, Vann Molyvann.
For example, his famous mansion was built in the 1960s and still stands strong in the bustling town despite the new skyscrapers appearing around it.
Covering a total area of 924 square meters, this villa is divided into two floors, with 4 bedrooms and 5 bathrooms, which is spacious and designed to be light, airy and green nature, which creates a refreshing feeling together. For those who stay in it.
The location of the villa is easy to travel to places such as Toul Tompong Market, Aeon Mall, The Mall, schools, banks and many restaurants. More specifically, this villa is selling for only $ 7 million.
In line with the momentum of real estate in Cambodia, especially as Vann Molyvann's mansion is located in the center of the city, it clearly shows the potential of the location and the construction history for every client who wants to become the owner of this mansion. Whether you buy for living or for future investment.
It should also be noted that although Mr. Vann Molyvann has already passed away, his work continues to be appreciated by everyone, as those works are clearly left through public buildings. Famous such as the National Olympic Stadium, the Chaktomuk Conference Hall and the Independence Monument, these works have made the outside world know more about Cambodia.
The uniqueness of his work in the past is known as the combination of modern Khmer and ancient Khmer architecture combined to maintain the Khmer identity, but also compatible with modern, so-called architecture. Modern Khmer.
(Phnom Penh): Since the launch of the financing project to support small and medium enterprises, up to now, the loan of 30 million dollars has reached the owners of small and medium enterprises and the agricultural sector, in which SME Bank has released $ 20 million and the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank $ 10 million.
This is according to Mr. Ros Silva, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, speaking at the press conference of the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on the morning of July 30, 2020 under the theme "Process and Procedures of the Support Finance Project. Small and medium enterprises. The ceremony took place at the Council of Ministers.
As of July 28, 2020, the number of clients contacting and applying for loans has continued to increase to 430, totaling approximately US $ 42 million. . Most of these loan applications are for raising pigs, raising fish, raising chickens and ducks, raising cows, growing vegetables, fruits and processing agricultural products.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy also highlighted some of the challenges in promoting credit under the financing scheme, especially small and medium enterprises, most of which received loans from banks and microfinance institutions and used debt securities to secure debts with institutions. Those finances have already been proposed. Most of these small and medium enterprises lack assets to secure new debt.
In another case, some small and medium enterprises have not yet been registered or recognized by the competent authorities or other professional institutions. This is according to Mr. Ros Silva.
It should be informed that on February 24, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, launched a special financing program worth up to 50 million US dollars through the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture. In addition, 33 partner banks have contributed $ 50 million to the Royal Government, bringing SME Bank's capital to $ 100 million.
