(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, announced his support and affirmed that the Cambodian representative will participate in the 3rd China International Import and Export Fair to be held during November 2020 in Shanghai, China.
The purpose of the meeting was to disseminate important information about the 3rd China International Import and Export Fair, which will be held on November 5-10, 2020 in Shanghai, People's Republic of China. There will also be a presentation and interpretation of the policy of organizing the fair, opening up the market, expanding international cooperation and the many benefits of participating in the fair.
Addressing the meeting, Minister Pan Sosak spoke about the long-standing diplomatic relationship between Cambodia and China, which has strengthened bilateral ties year by year and has become an inseparable steel friendship. To work together to build progress, prosperity and mutual understanding.
The Minister praised the organization of the China International Import and Export Fair and stressed that this huge trade fair is very important for all participating countries, both public and private, with the opportunity to promote products, services and investment projects. And met directly in business negotiations with its new partners.
He also asked the Chinese side to support the development of emerging businesses, such as the digital economy, e-business and so on. And help Cambodia restructure its industry and raise the level of industrialization in line with the development of the global economy.
In response to the invitation from the Chinese side, the Minister informed the Chinese side that Cambodia is ready to participate in the 3rd China International Import and Export Fair from November 5 to 10, 2020 in Shanghai with the expectation that the situation The global Kovid-19 pandemic will be brought under control and flights will resume.
He added that the Ministry of Commerce was ready to set up a Cambodian pavilion and facilitate the private sector to participate in the event, as it had done twice in the past.
This large-scale global event has attracted the interest of many countries around the world to actively participate in trade exchanges, investments and share information and experiences with each other.
Cambodia has participated in this exhibition event twice, led by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission to organize and participate in the International and World Expo, the first in 2018 and the second. In 2019. In 2019, Cambodia was honored as a country of honor in this important exhibition as well.
General Neang Phat: Despite the difficult circumstances, Cambodia and China do not abandon each other in times of emergency
(Phnom Penh): General Neang Phat, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of National Defense, confirmed that despite the difficult circumstances, Cambodia and China are good friends and will not abandon each other in times of emergency.
This statement was made by General Neang Phat on July 29, 2020, during an interview with China's CCTV news agency at the Council of Ministers.
General Neang Phat said that in a show of concern for his Chinese friend, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid an urgent visit to the People's Republic of China as China was facing an outbreak of Kovid. 19. The general confirmed that these actions make it clear that "no matter how difficult the situation, good friends do not give up in an emergency."
Meanwhile, the General reminded that in the video conference between Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia, and Mr. Wei Fung He, Minister of Defense of China, reaffirmed the relationship of cooperation and support. Mutual cooperation between the two countries' Ministries of Defense to prevent the spread of Kovid-19, a common regional and global concern.
General Neang Phat recalled that through this steel friendship, the government and the Chinese People's Liberation Army provided a grant of medical equipment and sent a team of doctors to train Cambodian doctors in defense. Prevent and treat Kovid-19 in a timely and effective manner. In addition, it has sent anti-Kovid-19 equipment to Cambodia four times at a cost of millions of US dollars.
The Royal Government is preparing a draft law on (new) securities and a strategy for the development of the garment, footwear and bag industry in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has been preparing a draft law on state securities (new) and a draft strategy for the development of the garment, footwear and bag sector in Cambodia 2020-2025. This is according to a press release from the Ministry of Economy and Finance, obtained by Fresh News on July 30.
This "New State Securities Law" is the legal basis to allow the Royal Government of Cambodia to issue securities by determining the scope, decision on issuance, determining the size and format of the issuance of securities, determining the participants and Procedures for trading state securities as well as penalties.
This "new draft law" is comprehensive and highly responsive to the current context and changing trends of Cambodia's development through the establishment of a common framework for the management of issuance, trading and management of securities, and Defining specific objectives includes:
1: Responding to financing needs, especially for infrastructure development, 2: Strengthening cash flow management, 3: Development of the securities and finance sector, and 4: Supporting priority and other necessary projects.
2: Draft Development Strategy for Garment, Footwear and Bag Production of Cambodia 2020-2025:
The garment and footwear sector has played an important role in contributing to Cambodia's economic development by creating jobs, increasing people's incomes and reducing poverty. Although the garment, footwear and bag industries are constantly evolving based on their past competitive strengths, the sector still faces some challenges.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has considered the "Cambodia Garment and Footwear Development Strategy 2020-2025", an important roadmap, which sets out the vision of transforming the Cambodian footwear and footwear sector into an industry. Responsiveness, high value-added, supportive of diversification and competitiveness before the end of 2025, and that this sector can actively contribute to the socio-economic development of Cambodia.
This "strategy" aims to set the direction of common development, increase independence, strengthen the predictability and stability of the garment, footwear and bag industry in Cambodia to continue to promote the development of this sector in a sustainable and environmental manner. To achieve the goals and vision, the strategy has set goals:
1: Continue to strengthen human resources to increase productivity and create career paths for workers, 2: Continue to improve working conditions and well-being of workers, 3: Promote domestic and international investment by focusing on products Add value, 4: Attract investment in supporting industries and 5: Promote market diversification for the export of garments, shoes and bags.
This statement by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng was made on the occasion that Samdech presided over the opening ceremony of the 2nd National Consultative Workshop at the Leadership Level on the World Covenant on Safe, orderly and legal migration. GCM) on July 30, 2020 at the Ministry of Interior.
According to Kralahom, migrants who often face the risk of migration are job seekers or refugees from disaster areas, and according to research around the world, most migrants in The most difficult and vulnerable situations are those who are unskilled and leave the country illegally.
He added that migrants who venture out without the protection of the legal system are often exploited by those who exploit their destitute status by human trafficking, abuses, and the enslavement of the labor force. Old age, disability, loss of consciousness, loss of humanity or even loss of life.
In addition, Kralahom stated that the epidemic of Kovid-19 has exacerbated the migration problem and put the host countries at greater risk of negative fluctuations in the global and domestic economies. Encourage the operation of factories, enterprises and service sectors to be obstructed and subsequently suspended.
Kralahom added that while the target country has tightened and closed the country to prevent the spread of 19 smallpox, Cambodia has been rescuing returning workers avoiding the difficult situation in the target country. And trying to cross the border illegally and through unofficial channels.
In relation to migration work, Sar Kheng outlined four key areas related to migration issues that the Ministry of Interior, together with inter-ministerial representatives, will discuss to prepare for the inclusion of common objectives as a result of the next year's action plan. Ensure that the migration of Cambodians to the target countries as well as migrants from abroad into the Kingdom of Cambodia will be safe, orderly and legal.
For the four sectors related to migration issues that Samdech Krala Hom raised, including:
* First: Protection of Migrants: Both regular and non-regular migrants, both those planning to leave the country and those staying and working abroad and returning.
* Second: Data management: Establishing a database system for recording and managing specific data on migrants, both normal and irregular, to facilitate the implementation of measures to respond to situations that are a challenge for citizens and the nation. .
* Third: Supporting the process of repatriation and integration of migrants: Specific policies, measures and procedures need to be developed in collaboration with the governments of the countries concerned to obtain data on the conditions of repatriation, in particular the determination of measures. Protect women and children suspected of being victims of human trafficking.
* Fourth: Legal identification and identification, especially for children of Cambodian migrants born outside of Cambodia.
Please be informed that from March 21 to July 23, 2020, there were approximately 103,000 Cambodian workers who returned from migration during Kovid-19 and about 45% were women.
