Phnom Srok District Police Inspector Yor Sophal said that the drug addict was named Oung Sarom, 31, of Srah Chhouk East village, Srah Chik commune, Phnom Srok district, Banteay Meanchey province.
The victim's father said that his son had just returned from working in Thailand for six days and had been treated at a drug rehabilitation center several times, but was not recurring.
After a while, the villain came to sleep in a hammock and stabbed himself in six places, seriously injuring himself to end his life, but his parents and siblings saw him and rescued him. Phnom Srok District Referral Hospital.
