(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Minister of Economy of ASEAN, Cambodia, together with the Ministers of Economy of other ASEAN Member States, on July 29, 2020, held a special discussion with the Minister of Economy of Japan to introduce Some mechanisms address crisis caused by Kovid 19 as well as economic recovery.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Commerce, the meeting exchanged views on the situation of Kovid-19 in the region, shared measures to fight Kovid-19 and discussed economic recovery.
As a result, the meeting approved the "ASEAN-Japan Economic Strengthening Action Plan," the ministry said. The plan focuses on maintaining close economic ties between ASEAN and Japan, reducing the economic impact of the KV-19 virus and strengthening the economy.
During the meeting, Mr. Pan Sosak stressed the importance of connecting supply chains, cooperating on research on drugs and vaccines, maintaining market openness, as well as ensuring the flow of food and goods in the region.
In this regard, the Minister encouraged closer cooperation on trade and investment facilitation, eliminating trade barriers and using digital technology to restore the trust of businesses and customers.
The Minister also briefed the meeting on the effective measures and efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against Kovid-19 and thanked Japan for helping Cambodia to fight Kovid-19 through technical assistance and Medical equipment and so on.
To enhance the quality of online teaching, local educational institutions cooperate with leading institutions abroad to ensure the quality of education.
