(Phnom Penh): Lieutenant General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Commander of the Army, this morning, July 29, 2020, officially announced the transfer of the 911 Parachute Special Brigade to the Special Forces Command. Army Site Construction and Opening Ceremony of Disaster Relief Technical Training Course, 10th Generation Commando Training Course and 4th Generation Driver Training and Repair Training Course.
Speaking on that occasion, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet congratulated the 911 Parachute Special Brigade, which has been trusted by the Royal Government to decide to upgrade to the Special Forces Command under the Army Command, which is another new step. Proud of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
According to Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, for the Army as well as for the 911 Parachute Special Brigade, it also shows the recognition of the ability, will and effort of the soldiers throughout the unit.
So far, the 911 Parachute Special Brigade is in a new phase of history, having been reorganized by the Parachute Squadron in 1948 and became a brigade in 1995. The brigade in 1999 and became the Special Forces Command.
In 2020, which is a special year, because with the confidence of the Royal Government to organize the intervention force at the new organizational structure, the brigade also received new uniforms designed by the officers of the unit, but the mission remains the same. It is training to strengthen forces and prepare to implement regulations to protect the territorial integrity, protect peace, as well as participate in rescuing the people.
It is also important that as a Special Forces Command under the Army, which is responsible for the Special Forces training unit, not only within the Army, but also the unit has the task of training capacity building. This is for the entire Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, as well as the entire National Armed Forces, including the National Police.
