(Kep): Since 2016, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has identified the poor and disabled and provided policy to 16,410 poor people with disabilities in 15 provinces.
For 2020, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has launched four new provincial capitals, including Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville, Kep and Koh Kong. This was stated by Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, representing Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
Mr. Nhek Vannara said that the poor people with disabilities in Kep province will receive a government-sponsored policy to improve their living standards in the near future. This was stated by Mr. Nhek Vannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation during the opening ceremony of the seminar on the implementation of the policy regime for the poor and disabled in the community on Wednesday, July 29, 2020.
Mr. Nhek Vannara expressed his appreciation to the Kep Provincial Policy Management Committee, Provincial Disability Action Council, especially the Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, which have always cooperated in the implementation of disability and achieved many achievements. Of particular note is the initial data collection for the general disabled in Kep.
