At the same time, Mr. Som Piseth, Deputy Governor of Kep Province, said that Kep Province in the past as well as now pays high attention to the disability sector throughout the province because disability work is a multidisciplinary work that requires all of us. Take care to protect and promote the rights of people with disabilities, because people with disabilities are also a source of contribution to the development of the country.
In the past as well as now, the provincial administration has provided access to health services, education, vocational training with quality and equality, as well as enhanced the participation of people with disabilities in expressing opinions and access to information. In addition, the provincial administration encourages the participation of social activities for people with disabilities, such as cultural, religious, sports, arts, recreation and other activities.
In addition, Mr. Som Piseth also requested the Ministry of Social Affairs to provide new techniques related to the development of the disability and social sector to provincial social affairs officers to implement this work more effectively.
He strongly believes that by providing a policy regime for the poor with disabilities in the community is to improve the lives of people with disabilities in Kep to a better level and in accordance with the Law on Protection and Promotion Rights of Persons with Disabilities The Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities and the Decade of Persons with Disabilities in the Asia-Pacific region, the Unchean Strategy makes rights a reality.
