(Phnom Penh): General Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, issued a directive to all subordinate units to implement measures to ensure stability, security, public order and social safety during the five-day New Year holiday from the 17th. Until August 21, 2020. This is according to the instructions received by Fresh News.
In accordance with this instruction, General Neth Savoeun introduced the following units to:
* First, to pay attention to increase awareness of the situation related to security and social order, especially terrorist activities, transnational crime of all kinds, maneuvers, attempts to cause social unrest and other criminal activities to take effective measures to prevent and suppress in a timely manner. .
* Second, to actively promote the implementation of the "Safe Village-Commune" policy and to carefully manage all kinds of targets in the village-commune community, using all measures to eliminate the effectiveness before Give the target the opportunity to act to cause insecurity or danger to life and damage to people's property.
* Third: Security measures and public order must be strictly increased in the entertainment destinations of the people in order to maintain good order, especially to pay attention to the absolute safety of the King, the top leaders and Senior national dignitaries who travel and visit the people on this occasion.
At the same time, care must be taken to guard and protect the houses and property of the people who leave to meet relatives in their hometowns or to travel far away with their families.
* Fifth: Prevent and crack down on all activities such as: gangster activity, violence, gambling of all kinds, use of weapons, explosives, ammunition that lead to danger, cause fear to the people and lead to ineffective. Good for the honor and dignity of the society.
* Sixth: Promoting the enforcement of the Road Traffic Law and disseminating the Royal Government's Sub-Decree No. 39 dated March 17, 2020 on the Correction of Transitional Penalties for Violations of the Road Traffic Law and Planning First, to organize traffic order on national roads, towns, especially the entrances and exits of the capital, provinces, as well as other destinations to reduce congestion and accidents that may occur eventually.
* Seventh: Care must be taken to educate the people to be vigilant in the event of a fire or disaster, by organizing forces and means to be ready 24 hours a day to cooperate in rescuing when a fire or natural disaster occurs. .
* Eighth: To strengthen the work at all levels and be ready to intervene in all circumstances by cooperating with major media to provide up-to-date information such as traffic congestion, make people aware in advance to divert traffic. At the same time, all departments and units must be assigned to have regular shifts, and officers under the supervision of subordinates should be rotated so that all officers have the opportunity to take time off.
* 9th: To summarize the situation and the results of the implementation of security measures during this holiday, report to the General Commission of the National Police by the afternoon of August 23, 2020 as scheduled (report shall be from 15 to 23 August 2020).
