Officials explain the free trade that Cambodia and China have just negotiated (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodia and China have just concluded negotiations on free trade. As planned, the historic and first bilateral free trade agreement for Cambodia could be signed by the leaders of the two countries in late 2020 or early 2021.
The free trade agreement has been described by economic officials and economists as a new opportunity for Cambodia to open up trade to China and also to attract more investment to Cambodia.
What is free trade? Why just have free trade also expand trade? Who benefits from free trade?
Sok Sopheak, secretary of state at the Ministry of Commerce and chairman of the Free Trade Agreement Negotiation Group with China, explained that a free trade agreement (FTA) is an agreement between countries that waives tariff barriers. Who signed the agreement. This agreement will facilitate tax barriers, limiting the amount of goods that can be understood as a free market economy or in the sense of a unified economy.
This free trade agreement not only agreed on the exemption of tariff barriers, but also covered many other areas, such as investment services, trade facilitation, and the elimination of non-tariff barriers.
Mr. Sok Sopheak said that the free trade agreement between Cambodia and China will open up greater opportunities for Cambodia to import agricultural and processed agricultural products into China duty-free. According to Sok Sopheak, about 95 percent of Cambodia's 340 items will be tax-free after the agreement is signed. About 5% of the goods will be exempted from tax in the next 10 years.
For those who benefit from this agreement, Mr. Sok Sopheak emphasized that all cells in Cambodian society, including the Royal Government, investors, producers and the Cambodian people, especially farmers.
