(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement (FTA) has been negotiated and is ready to be officially signed soon, which will bring great benefits to both sides. The people of Cambodia have expressed their satisfaction and support for this agreement, but there are also a small number of negative comments.
A senior official of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Mr. Chan Sopheap, pointed out that the Cambodian people have benefited greatly from the preferential tariffs on exports to China, which means that when this agreement enters As a result, about 98 percent of goods will be automatically taxed.
In a press conference held by the Royal Government Spokesperson on the morning of July 28, 2020, Mr. Chan Sopheap told a small number of individuals to stop thinking negatively about the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement (FTA). China gains more than Cambodia.
The senior official of the Ministry of Economy stressed that the main purpose of the FTA is to reduce import duties, which are the sovereignty of each country, but when the FTA enters into force, both sides will provide concessions. Give to each other.
Mr. Chan Sopheap added that the negotiating team had made efforts to facilitate some of the necessary conditions required when exporting goods, but then for the conditions to be met, it was in the private sector combined with government intervention. To boost exports.
The Free Trade Agreement (FTA) is an agreement between countries that sign the agreement. This agreement will be facilitated with tariff barriers, limiting the amount of goods which can be understood as a free market economy or in the sense of a unified economy.
