This afternoon, the Royal Academy of Cambodia held a roundtable discussion on the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement.
(Phnom Penh): Free trade talks between Cambodia and China officially closed in June, with a free trade agreement between the two countries scheduled for late 2020. Or early 2021.
The free trade agreement between Cambodia and China is Cambodia's first agreement with a trading partner in order to expand its trade. The free trade agreement between Cambodia and China has become a hot topic both nationally and internationally.
On the afternoon of July 28, 2020, the Royal Academy of Cambodia will hold a roundtable discussion on trade between Cambodia and China. The forum will be attended by Mr. Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, Mr. Ky Sereywat, President of the Chinese Studies Center of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, and Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
This discussion was held to provide more understanding to the people as well as investors on the free trade between Cambodia and China.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Li Keqiang, Prime Minister of China, during a bilateral meeting on January 20-23, 2019 in Beijing, decided to study the possibility of establishing a bilateral free trade agreement between Cambodia and Cambodia. China to expand trade, investment, services and cooperation to achieve a total trade target of 10 billion US dollars by 2023.
The agreement was handed over to the governments of the two countries to examine the possibility of finding a suitable time to formally sign.
It should be noted that the trade volume between Cambodia and China in 2018 reached about 7.4 billion US dollars, of which Cambodia's exports to China amounted to 1.377 million US dollars, an increase of 37% and imports. From China, it is worth 6 billion US dollars, an increase of 26%.
The Ministry of Commerce claims that based on the joint principles agreed by the negotiating team, if the two governments agree on the text of the proposed agreement and market opening, Cambodia's export growth is expected to increase. Up about 20 percent.
Implementing Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Recommendation, a concrete road with a length of more than 500 meters provided to people in Ban Kam commune, Prey Kabas district was opened this morning
(Takeo): A concrete road 545 meters long and 5 meters wide, which is a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia to the people in Thlok Daun Tum village, Ban Kam commune, Prey Kabas district Takeo province will start construction on Tuesday morning, July 28, 2020 under the chairmanship of Mr. Khan Sokha, Deputy Governor, represented by Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor of Takeo.
Speaking on the occasion of the construction of a concrete road donated by Samdech Techo to the people, Mr. Khan Sokha said that in response to the request of the people who asked Samdech Techo to help improve and widen the road in the village, which is difficult to do. People's trip on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit to Prey Kabbas district, Takeo province on July 21.
At that time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed the Takeo provincial authorities to study this road as soon as possible and open the construction site for the concrete road for the people to prevent easy travel and transport of agricultural products to sell in the market. Timely.
The Deputy Governor of Takeo Province continued that Samdech Techo Hun Sen always thought about the well-being of the people everywhere, especially when Samdech visited the farmers in Prey Kabbas District, Takeo Province recently. Provide rice sowing machines to hundreds of farmers and build some roads at the request of farmers.
The provision of rice sowing machines as well as helping to repair and improve the roads of Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government to the people, is to take care of your livelihood by working so that the people can transport the agricultural crops that you harvest. Get on the market quickly and at a reasonable price.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Unity Command and Parks Officer of Provincial Department of Environment demolished 43 slums in Prek Teuk Sap, Kbal Chhay
(Preah Sihanouk): Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administrative Unity Force, in cooperation with Preah Sihanouk Municipal Administrative Unity Force and Parks Officer of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Department of Environment, on July 27, 2020, implemented administrative measures to dismantle 43 huts. And destroying many new mango seedlings planted by the squatters in Prek Teuk Sap Kbal Chhay.
According to a press release from the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Department of Environment, obtained by Fresh News on July 28, 2020, a group of villagers have built slums on privately owned land. After being evicted from the private land, the villagers came to settle in the O Trav area, Village 1, Sangkat 01, Sihanoukville, Sihanoukville Province.
According to the press release, on July 14, the rangers of the Provincial Department of Environment, in cooperation with the Sihanoukville Administrative Unity Command, conducted a training and demolition of slums at the above location. Already, but the people have asked to do the dismantling themselves.
In addition, on July 17, 2020, park officials inspected the actual site again and found that there was no demolition, but instead they built more houses and cottages.
