On the morning of July 28, 2020, a water purifier was handed over to Calmette Hospital by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The senior minister said that this pure water machine extracts air from the atmosphere to produce pure water. According to Mr. Sun Chanthol, this machine costs more than 60,000 US dollars.
Mr. Sun Chanthol recalled that when he attended the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, he saw the greatness of this water machine and can meet the needs of the people of Cambodia at various public service facilities. He also informed the Prime Minister to buy and put in the hospital.
Prof. Chheang Ra, Director General of Calmette Hospital, welcomed and expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for sponsoring this water purifier to meet the needs of the hospital. In particular, more than 6,000 patients per day are hospitalized and consulted in hospitals and caregivers.
According to Chheang Ra, the water purifier not only meets the needs of patients, but also for a team of nearly 2,000 doctors and staff.
Mr. Chheang Ra said that this pure water has high health benefits and also contributes to environmental care by reducing the use of plastic through the use of bottled water.
The director of Calmette Hospital pointed out that the gift of this water machine is very expensive.
During the handover ceremony this morning, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol called on people to seek services at Calmette Hospital to take care of this water machine for long-term use.
