(Rattanakiri): Dissemination Workshop on "Law on Management of Petroleum and Petroleum Products" and Training on "Station Risks and Safety Circuits for Preparation of Petroleum and Gas Stations" and Training on Risks to Local Authorities in Ratanakkiri Province Mining and Energy was held on the morning of July 28, 2020 at Rattanak City Hotel under the chairmanship of Mr. Sok Khavan, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province.
After Mr. Thong Savun's welcome, Mr. Sok Khavan said that over the years, despite the Ministry of Petroleum Regulations 1991 and the Circular on Safety for the preparation of gas stations, gas stations and gas stations and Gas, but these regulations are not yet sufficient to allow the Ministry of Mines and Energy to fully function.
Traders and relevant authorities also have difficulty and uncertainty in conducting business and carrying out their work related to the oil and gas sector in accordance with laws and regulations.
He said that now is the beginning of a new era, with the law on the management of oil and petroleum products approved by the King on July 12, 2019. Meanwhile, according to the provisions of the new law, the Ministry has appointed a Petroleum Inspection Officer, consisting of officials from the General Department of Petroleum and the Provincial Department of Petroleum, who will be trained as judicial police.
In addition, the Ministry has established a working group to inspect and inspect the oil field, led by the leadership of the Ministry has the role of coordinating the work of oil inspectors in the following goals:
* To strengthen compliance, including education and training * Enforcement of law enforcement, and third, the implementation of legal action, including fines and the preparation of documents to the court * Inspection and inspection team in the oil sector will also review The possibility of decentralization * and decentralization of labor at the sub-national level in the near future.
Senior official of the Ministry of Mines: Petroleum resources are a valuable national capital for economic promotion and development
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Ing Ieng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, on July 28, 2020, stated that oil resources are a valuable national capital for economic promotion and development and raising people's living standards. Also.
