(Mondulkiri): On the morning of July 28, 2020, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, together with Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment And implement land registration plans, resolve land disputes, and support land use planning in Mondulkiri.
The meeting was held at Mondulkiri Provincial Hall with the participation of HE Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Mondulkiri Provincial Board of Governors and other relevant officials.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, there are a total of 550 inter-ministerial working groups, of which about 300 are from the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and 50 are from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. And the Ministry of Environment, about 200 people.
