In a press conference organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on the morning of July 28, 2020 on "Results of the negotiations on the establishment of a free trade agreement between Cambodia and China," Mr. Sok Sopheak stressed that this free trade agreement. Yes, instead of the European Union EBA.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Commerce stated, "I would like to inform you that this is not a one-month, two-month plan. This plan has been done for many years. "And took the results to the respective governments (Cambodia-China) to decide."
According to Sok Sopheak, after the entry into force of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, Cambodia's exports to China will increase by about 25 percent. As of 2019, Cambodia's exports to China have reached $ 1 billion, and imports from China have reached nearly $ 7 billion.
Mr. Sok Sopheak stressed that most of the goods that Cambodia imports from China are machinery and other goods that serve the construction sector.
It should be informed that the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement has been completed and is ready to be officially signed in August 2020. However, after the signing, both parties plan to implement from January 2021 onwards.
The free trade agreement not only agreed on the exemption of tariff barriers, but also covered many other areas, such as investment services, trade facilitation, and the elimination of non-tariff barriers.
7 Deputy Commissioners and Police of Prey Veng Province Stand on Violence and Take Money from Drug Suspects
(Phnom Penh): General Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police General Commission, decided to temporarily suspend the work of Deputy Commissioner and Police Officer of Prey Veng Provincial Police in charge of 7 drugs after they used violence and took money. 4 million Riel from the suspect during the crackdown on drug cases.
According to the information, this action was taken after on 20 July at 20:30, the specialized force of Prey Veng Provincial Police cracked down on drug trafficking in front of the gate of Rong Damrey pagoda in Village 6. Sangkat Kampong Leav, Prey Veng Province.
According to the information, during the operation, the police arrested the suspects, 26-year-old Thai Samad and 28-year-old Hoeun Rath. The suspects claimed that Prey Veng provincial anti-drug police officers pulled out a pistol from their waists, hit them on the head and summoned their accomplices to the police station, tortured them and extorted another 4,000,000 riel. Also in return and release.
According to Lt. Col. Touch Theara, Deputy Director of the Prey Veng Provincial Drug Bureau, the 4 million was handed over to the Prey Veng Provincial Prosecutor in exchange for the victim's release.
After receiving this information, on the afternoon of July 26, 2020, General Prum Santhor, Commissioner of Prey Veng Provincial Police, on behalf of General Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, apologized and handed over the money to his family. Located in Andong village, Mesor Prachan commune, Pearang district, Prey Veng province.
Mr. Sok Sopheak said that in the past, the goods that Cambodia imported to China included: pepper, which was taxed by the Chinese side with a 20 percent tax, but after the signing of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, Cambodian pepper was taxed at an additional 0%. From here, the dried pepper that farmers grow in Takeo province is also taxed at 0%, including dried pepper, so all these are the goods that Cambodia received from the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement.
At this point, Mr. Sok Sopheak stated that, for example, that Cambodian pepper, which was taxed at 20 percent in the past, is no longer taxed after the bilateral free trade agreement came into force. In addition to Cambodian pepper, fruits, fish, meat and other marine species are also duty-free for export to the Chinese market.
As for the goods that the Chinese side charges duty on Cambodia, it is various types of machinery and vehicles. In addition, the taxation of these goods is not a problem for the Cambodian side, because Cambodia is not a country that produces all these materials. This was further confirmed by Mr. Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of July 28, 2020, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Vice President of the Mines Authority, stated that the donor community has shown its commitment and continued support for the Royal Government of Cambodia to achieve the goal of a landmine-free Cambodia. 2025.
On behalf of Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Action Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch praised the implementation of the demining project for results from 2006 to June 2020, which cleared the land and provided land safe from landmine threats. About 245 square kilometers and more than 1 million people.
The Senior Minister also thanked the donor countries and development partners for their continued involvement with the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fourth phase of demining projects, including UNDP, Australia, the Republic of Korea and New Zealand. The Senior Minister considered UNDP to be a strong partner in joining the Royal Government of Cambodia in the demining project for results.
Mr. Nick Beresford, Representative of the United Nations Development Program (UNDP) in Cambodia, congratulated the Mines Authority on the successful implementation of the demining project for the past three phases, and also expressed strong support for continuing to work together for the fourth phase. He also welcomed New Zealand and the Republic of Korea for their support in the fourth phase of the project.
Australian Representative Ryan Tierney, First Secretary of the Australian Embassy in Cambodia, expressed his support for the project implementation process and confidence in the Mine Action Authority's ability to implement the project until 2025 and coordination with UNDP Partner Mine Action Phase IV. Will succeed according to the agreed plan. Australia will help plan for the fourth phase, although the world is diverting some of its funding to fight Covid-19.
Representatives of the Australian Embassy also thanked mine authorities and provincial planning officials for interviewing workers returning from Thailand due to the Covid-19 outbreak.
Embassy representatives hope to have the opportunity to inspect and learn about the needs of demining operations in Cambodia one day after the end of the Covid-19 outbreak.
At the same time, Senior Minister Ly Thuch hoped that the participation of KOICA of the Republic of Korea in this project from 2021 will help Cambodia achieve the goal of demining.
The meeting agreed on a number of major points, including:
The Mines Authority and UNDP are organizing activities in response to the national capacity building to continue to manage the clearance of mines and explosive remnants of war after 2025. * Allow the Mines Authority to continue its activities to strengthen the effectiveness of project implementation from 2021 onwards. * Support a joint visit to Pailin to inspect demining operations and to interview project demining beneficiaries.
The Phase 4 Demining Project for the results of the six-year period from 2020-2025, with a total value of 20 million US dollars, focusing on three major outcomes: First: Demining and Explosive remnants of war: Second, support for disaster relief activities, education on mine risk and gender mainstreaming, and third: strengthen national capacity.
General Knowledge: Why the "Nobel Prize" was created?
While some called him the "merchant of death" because of the creation of these explosives, Nobel was, in fact, a pacifist, and later began to worry deeply about the impact of his discovery. To the world as well.
The Swedish Academy selects the winner of the literary award, and a committee nominated by the Norwegian National Assembly decides on the Nobel Peace Prize. The Nobel Prize ceremony is still held every year, on December 10, the anniversary of Nobel death. Each Nobel Prize is accompanied by a cash prize of nearly $ 1.4 million, and the winner also receives a gold medal with the Nobel Prize engraved on it.
Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Recommends to Strengthen Anti-Human Trafficking Work
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province and Chairman of Kampong Cham Provincial Anti-Human Trafficking Committee, made some recommendations to subordinates to implement in the fight against human trafficking to get good results.
The recommendation of the Provincial Governor was made on the morning of July 28, 2020 during the first half-year meeting of the Provincial Committee for Combating Human Trafficking.
After praising the results of the first half of the work of the Provincial Anti-Human Trafficking Committee, the provincial governor said that in order to implement the work of combating human trafficking to achieve good results in the future, he asked Recommend the following 5 points:
* First, the Secretariat should continue to provide training so that local officials are competent enough to carry out their work.
* Second, the Secretariat must continue to review and implement its action plan as we are experiencing the Kovid 19 crisis, so follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
* Third: Relevant to the six expert groups must actively carry out their work in accordance with their duties as stated in the joint decision.
* Fourth: The municipal, district and commune level should continue to cooperate with the administrative police station to disseminate through the 9 points of safe villages, communes to the people widely, safe migration to avoid defeat. Cheating brokers who can lead to victims of human trafficking.
* Fifth: Regarding the issue of children for Kampong Cham City, he asked the Victims Protection Working Group and the Provincial Department of Social Affairs and Veterans to co-operate with the Kampong Cham Municipal Authority to take procedural measures to manage all subjects in an orderly and efficient manner. Avoid Kovit 19 as well.
