Phnom Penh Police Detain Suspect in Daun Penh Motorcycle Theft Case
The Information and Quick Reaction Team of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police confirmed that in this case, the competent officers of the Criminal Police Office arrested the suspect in the case of motorcycle theft on July 9, 2020 in Sangkat Boeung Reang, Khan Daun Penh.
According to the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, on July 27, 2020, at around 12:30, the Bureau of Minor Offenses searched and arrested a 45-year-old suspect named Teang Tol alias Kang Kep at Street 90. Sangkat Srah Chak, Khan Daun Penh, in the crime of stealing a black Honda C125 2020 series motorcycle with license plate Phnom Penh 1IF-5189 in front of House 54, Street 184, Sangkat Boeung Reang, Khan Daun Penh on July 9, 2020.
After receiving the suspect's confession, the police proceeded to arrest another suspect, a member of the faction named Ros Tith alias Mao, 47 years old, at the point of Railway No. 273, Sangkat Srah Chak, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh and arrested Exhibits of Honda C125 2020 motorcycle with license plate Phnom Penh 1IF-1909 sent to the office to complete the legal action.
After being detained for questioning, the two suspects confessed that they had indeed stolen the motorcycle.
