(Central): A joint commission consisting of customs officers, CamControl officers, branch officials, consumer protection, competition and anti-fraud officials, and relevant officials at the border inspected imported vegetables, which in the past found six kinds of vegetables containing chemicals.
The above action took place on the afternoon of July 27, 2020, led by Mr. On Sinuon, Head of Kandal Provincial Customs and Excise Department, with the guidance of the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise. Cambodia has led the Customs and Excise Force of the Chrey Thom Customs and Excise Office in collaboration with the Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud Branch (Kandal) in Kandal Province.
Authorities inspected vegetables imported from Vietnam through the Customs and Excise Office at Chrey Thom, especially six vegetables that were previously found to contain unsafe pesticide residues for use and were temporarily suspended.
After the officers of the mobile food laboratory of the DPRK removed the samples for about 3 hours and showed the results that are safe for consumption, these vegetables were allowed to be imported regularly and under Regularly inspect the procedures in force for the next import. Visit the gallery of international events of July 27, 2020 (Photo inside)
