For July, support for poor and vulnerable families increased from more than $ 23 million to $ 28 million, as the number of poor families who have just received the new equity card increased by about 50,000.
The Support Program for the Poor and Vulnerable People 19 Kovid, launched by the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on June 24, 2020, has really alleviated poverty to some extent. The beneficiaries thanked the Royal Government for establishing this program.
A poor family living in Teuk Khleang village, Teuk Khleang commune, Lvea Em district, Kandal province has already received a June allowance. He is also preparing to pay the allowance for July.
The poor family, who also has two young sons and a disabled husband, described with tears in their eyes that the Royal Government's support really helped their family's livelihood, especially to fund their children's care.
Chum Sam Onn, chief of Teuk Khleang commune, Lvea Em district, stated that in his commune, there were 87 poor families with equity cards for June and 3 more newly identified families in This July.
The commune chief confirmed that in his commune, there is no fee or percentage deduction from the poor and vulnerable families, the budget is paid in full.
Allowances for the Poor and Vulnerable 19 for June 2020 have been completed by July 24, 2020. More than 530,000 families came to pay the allowance, while more than 20,000 families did not pay. Through this first month, the Royal Government team gained a lot of experience and considered the opening for this first month as a success.
The Royal Government has set out phases for the program of support for the poor and the most vulnerable to Kovid 19, with the first phase lasting two months, June and July. After the end of the first phase, it will enter the second phase, which lasts for two months, from August to September 2020, and may follow, depending on the status of the epidemic.
Please be informed that during the meeting with farmers in Prey Kabbas district, Takeo province on July 21, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that despite the continuous discovery of poor and vulnerable families, the Royal Government of Cambodia has not stopped Also, continue to search for more social assistance and not to let any people die of starvation without the knowledge of the Royal Government.
Samdech Techo stated that the provision of social assistance to poor and vulnerable families is not permanent, it will end when Kovit 19 disease declines, and this subsidy is not a complete adoption. But it is only a compensation for what is lacking and affected. Summary of important news events for July 27, 2020
