Spokesman for the General Commission: On July 27, another 1,376 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 88 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to July 27, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 120,635 vehicles, including 89,370 motorcycles and 31,265 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 88 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for July 27, 2020, traffic offenses throughout the country also occurred 12 times, in which 7 people died, 15 people were injured (08 seriously injured).
