Two New Houses Donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to Veterans in Prasat Sambo District, Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): Two new houses donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, through General Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, were promoted by Major General Som Sun Kampong Thom Military Operation Area: President of Kampong Thom Cambodian Veterans Association handed over to two families of veterans in two different villages in Prasat Sambo district, Kampong Thom province.
The first new house was handed over to 58-year-old veteran Sin Srey, who enlisted in the army in 1982 at the 30th Battalion of the Kampong Thom Provincial Army. He was crippled on July 25, 1994 in the battle of Ny Pech, Ny Pech commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province. Mr. Sin Srey has a wife and four children in charge of Taing Krasau village, Taing Krasau commune, Prasat Sambo district, Kampong Thom province.
New House 2: To Nam Heng, a 59-year-old disabled veteran who joined the army in 1994 in the 14th Intervention Brigade stationed in Pursat province and was wounded in the Battambang Provincial Battle. Landmines in 1998. Mr. Nam Heng has a wife and two children in his care, currently living in Chhouk Boeung village, Chhouk commune, Prasat Sambo district, Kampong Thom province.
Lt. Gen. Som Sun also reminded the people to take care of their health and protect themselves from the 19 epidemics of Kovid, which is spreading in our world. Implement work in raising livestock, farming to provide for the livelihood of each family.
During the handover ceremony of the 166th house and the 167th house, Lt. Gen. Som Sun also brought a gift from Lt. Gen. Dr. HUN Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army. The family received 50 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 2 bags of fish sauce, soy sauce and some money.
The local authorities, the people and the families of the veterans are very happy and would like to express our deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for taking care of all the difficulties and livelihoods of the people as well as the veterans. And please support the prince to lead the ship of Cambodia in peace and development. Veterans Association signs agreement on Korean Veterans Livelihood Improvement Project
(Central): The Cambodian Veterans Association and the South Korean company "Phang Phang" have signed an agreement on a project to improve the lives of veterans by protecting and supporting agricultural products produced by veterans.
The signing ceremony was held on July 27, 2020 under the chairmanship of Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Association. Korean company "Phang Phang" is a multidisciplinary agricultural company. Through this agreement, the company will support veterans in the production of organic duck eggs and meat from Korea, which ensures the right quality by using plants. From Korea as an ingredient in duck feed.
Speaking at the ceremony, the Senior Minister praised the company "Phang Phang" for participating in the strategy to improve the lives of Cambodian veterans.
The senior minister encouraged the company to continue to cooperate to find more partners and expand other agricultural activities in addition to organic duck eggs and meat. He also urged the company to help teach and establish family-level farms for veterans' families by considering growing organic vegetables.
The senior minister urged the company to accept family members of veterans as farm laborers and to learn these important techniques so that they can return to expand their local jobs. CPP Team Visited Stung Meanchey 2 Sangkat and Donated to Help 3 Elderly Families
(Kampong Cham): The working group of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) in Stung Meanchey 2 Sangkat brought some money and some food items to support the three elderly families living in Trapeang Chey Village, Krala Commune, Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province on July 27. This year 2020.
After receiving the information, Mrs. Teav Thida and Mr. Thong Sarath, the working group of the Cambodian People's Party to help Stung Meanchey II, also assigned a representative to bring the amount of money and food to help the families of the three elderly people. Above to help solve daily needs.
On that occasion, Ms. Teav Thida sent a message and wished the three elderly families a speedy recovery and strength from the disease.
At the same time, the elderly family also thanked the working group of the Cambodian People's Party to help Sangkat Stung Meanchey II, which has donated money to his family now and wish them happiness and prosperity. Success forever.
It should be noted that the working group of the Cambodian People's Party to help Stung Meanchey II always take care of the poor, and this activity is also part of his contribution to reducing poverty of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Heng Samrin University Tbong Khmum and Global Peace Federation of Cambodia jointly provide students with opportunities to strengthen their leadership skills
(Tbong Khmum): Heng Samrin University, Tbong Khmum and the Global Peace Federation of Cambodia (UPF) have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) to provide students with the opportunity to exchange experiences, increase knowledge in leadership, especially in the study of various skills together.
The ceremony took place at Heng Samrin Tbong Khmum University on the morning of July 27, 2020, presided over by Mr. Pin Vannaro, Rector of Heng Samrin Tbong Khmum University and Mr. Hajime Saitou, Regional Vice President of the Global Peace Federation of Cambodia.
Mr. Pin Vannaro thanked the Global Peace Federation of Cambodia for its cooperation with Heng Samrin Tbong Khmum University as a partner to help strengthen knowledge on various skills, create many study and job opportunities for students and civil servants in the province. Gems as well as additional suggestions on learning Korean.
Please note that this organization focuses on educating young people to understand peace issues, as well as how to live in harmony and for the benefit of society. The organization operates in support of the United Nations Principles for the Training of Human Resources, Peace, especially to help people live with dignity and help with hunger. Cambodian Senate President sends condolences to Ouk Chan's family
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, expressed his deepest condolences and sadness over the death of Mr. Ouk Chan, a personal adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In his condolence message to his family on July 27, 2020, Samdech Say Chhum considered Mr. Ouk Chan's death as the loss of his beloved father and grandfather and the loss of a great dignitary. Physical, mental, intellectual, daring to sacrifice everything to contribute to the restoration and development of the country to progress.
