According to the announcement, the press conference was attended by Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Mr. Sok Sopheak, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, Dr. Ky Sereyvath, President of the Chinese Studies Center of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and coordinated by Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Cambodian Institute of International Relations.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Li Keqiang, Prime Minister of China, during a bilateral meeting on January 20-23, 2019 in Beijing, decided to study the possibility of establishing a bilateral free trade agreement between Cambodia and Cambodia. China to expand trade, investment, services and cooperation to achieve a total trade target of 10 billion US dollars by 2023.
It should also be noted that a free trade agreement is an agreement between one country and another to promote the free exchange of goods, services and services, unhindered by tariff barriers and other obligations. In general, the free trade agreement is aimed at promoting trade between each other in order to promote the economic growth of the two countries.
