(Phnom Penh): Mr. Song Saran, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation, said that this year, according to Chea Vichea, Cambodia will achieve 1 million tons of rice exports.
Mr. Song Saran continued, "On behalf of the Cambodian Rice Federation, we have high hopes of achieving 1 million tonnes of rice exports this year, and as leaders and members, we have worked hard. "We are working hard to achieve this goal of 1 million tons."
He said that if the supply chain of the agricultural production community as well as the mills of our member government are together, we will be able to achieve almost 1 million tons in 2020. On the other hand, if we look at the history of exports, we always export more than 55% in the second quarter, if you look at the first quarter, 400,000 tons, and if you analyze the data on the history of exports, about 500,000. Tons, about 900,000 tons.
He said that due to the efforts of the Royal Government, the Federation of Cambodian Rice and farmers want 1 million tons this year, if nothing changes, we will prepare better in 2021.
Mr. Song Saran added that currently, Cambodia's rice exports in the first quarter have improved, although Cambodia as well as the world are facing 19 cases of Kovid, and the federal plan is to promote the government's policy. To export 1 million tons of rice.
Please be informed that Cambodia achieved 397,660 tons of rice exports in the first six months of 2020, an increase of more than 41% compared to the same period in 2019, which exported only 281,538 tons. Exports earned more than 264 million US dollars. Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Commerce Introduces New Building, Minister of Commerce Tells Officials to Pay Attention to Provide Services
(Kampong Speu): The Department of Commerce of Kampong Speu Province on July 27, 2020 officially launched the new administrative building to facilitate the work of officials and provide services to the people. Along with the inauguration of the new administrative building, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, reminded the officials in the Department of Commerce of Kampong Speu to pay attention to serve the people better.
The inauguration ceremony of the Department of Commerce in Kampong Speu was presided over by Mr. Pan Sosak and attended by Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu, as well as leaders and officials of the Ministry and the Department of Commerce.
On that occasion, the Minister expressed his pleasure at the presence of the new administrative building of the Provincial Department of Commerce of Kampong Speu and thanked Mr. Yim Sokhom and Mr. Vy Samnang and provincial officials who have always cooperated with the Department of Commerce. Achieve good results.
The Minister of Commerce also mentioned the achievements of the Ministry in the past and some other important tasks that the Ministry has been actively working on, including the preparation of various legal documents for the trade sector. .
In addition to inaugurating the building of the Department of Commerce, the Minister also met with officials of the Department of Commerce and officials of the Branch of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud (CPC) in Kampong Speu. .
On that occasion, the Minister instructed and requested the civil servants of the Department of Commerce to continue their efforts to further expand their knowledge, both in terms of skills and foreign languages, through further study, research and experience from civil servants in the Ministry. Trade.
Mr. Pan Sosak also requested the officials of the Department of Commerce to continue to cooperate more closely with the local authorities to participate in the widespread dissemination of the Royal Government's in-depth reform program. In particular, the Ministry of Commerce's in-depth reform of trade policies aimed at facilitating trade and facilitating exports.
The Minister instructed to strictly avoid demanding informal fees from producers and traders, which is contrary to the content of the joint declaration on the public service package between the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
In order to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, the Minister also requested all institutions to participate in disseminating information on the prevention of this disease to people at all levels to follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to make our country more contagious. Out of the wave of the disease for the second time. Tomorrow morning, the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit will hold a press conference on "Final Results of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement Negotiations"
