(Phnom Penh): Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Say Saron, on the afternoon of July 27, 2020, issued an order to detain three scammers and money launderers after the crackdown by the Criminal Police Department. A while ago.
The investigating judge decided to charge the three fraudsters with "aggravated theft" in Phnom Penh in early February 2020. This offense is punishable under Articles 353 and 357 of the Penal Code.
It should be noted that the Criminal Police Department of the Ministry of Interior on July 23, 2020 launched a search operation to arrest three suspects involved in fraud and theft of money through Wing technology, who often steal people's money. Many victims.
The operation was carried out under the command of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, and Lt. Gen. In Bora, Deputy Commissioner for Planning and with the guidance of Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, Director of the Criminal Police Department, and led the operation. Brigadier General Cheav Vibol, Deputy Director of the Criminal Police Department, and Lieutenant Colonel Hem Bona, Director of the Bureau of Serious Crimes.
In front of the police, the suspects admitted that they had indeed cheated and stolen money through the Wing system, using the method of stealing passwords from customers through social media, fraudulently selling Facebook accounts of online sellers and making phone calls. Go to that customer to get a Wing password and another way is to pretend to be a customer at a money laundering agency to steal another customer's password.
After getting the password and phone number to be paid, But Panha used an application and gave the world name and Yon Pito to pay through the money transfer agent. When the money agent checked the phone number, he did not see the scammer's number, but instead saw the real recipient's number.
Brigadier General Chiao Vibol considered that these activities of the suspects are very dangerous, they use modern technology and can not be suppressed, not a few people will suffer a lot of money. The brigadier general called on all citizens to be careful when depositing money at the deposit point, fearing that there are fraud suspects nearby and stealing the code.
