(Phnom Penh): After the signing of the "Measures to prevent and eliminate interference in the air navigation system in the air of Cambodia" on July 27, 2020, the three Ministers agreed to prepare standard principles to How to prevent the infiltration of air navigation system frequencies, especially in the airspace of Cambodia.
Such a commitment by Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, and Mao Havanal, Minister in charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, was made after some interference in the frequency of the navigation system and Disobedience to the law and the instructions of the owners of some radio stations.
Mr. Chea Vandeth is determined: "In the past, the three ministries cooperated well, but we cooperated on a case-by-case basis, but after this joint declaration, our three ministries and institutions will prepare standard principles. In order to prevent this interference (interference into the frequency of the air navigation system) does not occur, especially in the airspace within the airspace of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Vandeth said that the interference in the frequency of the air navigation system is dangerous and a big problem for the country, so the Ministry of Information, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and the Secretariat of Civil Aviation have agreed to sign the agreement. Measures to prevent and eliminate interference into the air navigation system in the airspace of Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Vandeth said that as the Ministry in charge of radio frequencies, it will do its best to ensure the safety of Cambodia's airports. In this regard, the Ministry of Posts also considered strengthening the radio frequency control unit to be able to scan, test and check for any shortcomings that may occur.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith said that currently in Cambodia there is another signal that is very important is the rain betting that they use icom and this point is also difficult. Therefore, all ministries and institutions should work harder to do this work.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith said that in another case, in principle, if any radio was found to be interfering with the frequency transmission of the air navigation system, the Ministry would order an immediate shutdown and assign a specialized team to inspect the situation. Technically, the Ministry has now put in place devices to prevent leaks.
The Minister of Information confirmed that the transmission of noise into the frequency of the air navigation system may be caused by the use of antennas too close.
Mr. Mao Havnall said that as the leader of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, he tried to instruct all subordinates to liaise with the Ministry of Information on the issue of interference between civil aviation and airwaves. Ministry of Information radio broadcasts that could seriously affect the civil aviation sector.
"Therefore, after signing the agreement between our three ministries and institutions, I am confident that we will implement it effectively and that the concerns of civil aviation will be reduced. "The air between civil aviation, the Ministry of Information, as well as the Ministry of Posts, we will try to eliminate to a level that we can all accept."
