Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Introduces 6 Points to the Police Academy of Cambodia to Implement Continuing Training (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Promote the implementation of the five-year strategic plan to continue to achieve more success and new achievements in the training of the Cambodian National Police.
Introduction by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng on the occasion of closing the meeting to summarize the results of the implementation of the five-year strategic plan (2015-2019) and the work direction for the next five years of the Police Academy of Cambodia on the morning of July 27 The year 2020 includes:
* First, the General Department of Logistics and Finance must review the 2021 budget of the Academy that has been cut and must strive to coordinate with representatives of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to maintain the budget at the request of the Police Academy of Cambodia to support Courses to be trained.
* Second, all relevant units must pay attention to giving value and encouragement to competent and qualified officials who have graduated from the Academy or abroad.
* Third: The Academy must continue to build a quality culture in training the police force to have the ability and true professional ethics to meet the needs of society.
* Fourth, the Academy must promote police science research and must gather information related to the use of trained human resources in various force units. In this regard, Samdech requested all relevant units to provide good cooperation with the research team of the Academy.
* Fifth: Regarding the National Police Museum, which is planned to be newly built in the premises of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Academy, it has already been mentioned in the previous meeting. Therefore, Samdech requested Mr. Chan Ean, Mr. Mao Bunnarin, Mr. Seng Youan and General Seng Phally to meet to discuss the transfer of management and construction of the National Police Museum.
* Sixth, the Academy must continue to pay attention to implement measures to prevent and prevent the transmission of Kovid-19, such as wearing a mask, washing hands with soap and alcohol, measuring temperature, keeping a safe distance.
Drinking together until an argument leads to violence, one jailed and one died in Dangkor district
(Phnom Penh): A man was arrested immediately after using violence to take a stick to a friend who was drinking together, causing death on July 26, 2020 at 20:30 at House no. Street Lum, Kandal Village, Sangkat Rolous, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
According to the police, the body of the victim, Som Chenda, alias Suong Chenda, male, 36 years old, ethnic Khmer, occupation: carpenter, living at the construction site, Kork Ovleuk village, Sangkat Spean Thmor, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh, his hometown is Dey Dus village, Prek Prosop commune, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province. .
As for the suspect, his name is Ban Piseth, male, 30 years old, ethnic Khmer, occupation: carpenter, living at the construction site, Kork Ovleuk village, Sangkat Spean Thmor, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh, his hometown is Prey Kou village, Prek Prosop commune, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province.
Police said that before the incident, the suspect and the victim, along with a total of four accomplices, had been drinking together, and when drunk, the suspect and the victim had a heated argument and fought with each other, then the suspect He jumped to pick up an 84-centimeter-long wooden stick near the drinking spot on the victim's head and face, causing serious injuries to the victim.
Residents saw the incident, called the police to intervene, and the police arrived at the scene, arrested the suspect and exhibits and called an ambulance to transport the victim to the Sourly Clinic on Street 217 in Russey Village, Sangkat. Stung Meanchey, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh. Upon arrival at Sour Clinic, the doctor told that the victim was dead.
After that, the police reported to the Technical and Scientific Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and the court doctor to inspect the body of the victim. After examining the body and the scene, Mr. Oknha Dr. Nong Sovannaroth concluded that the victim Died of severe head trauma.
Som Leakena, alias Pheaktrana, a 40-year-old female, the sister of the victim (corpse), filed a complaint at the Rolous Administrative Police Station for the authorities to deal with the suspect legally, and the police handed over the body to Relatives take to the traditional festival in the hometown of Kratie province. Khmer Breweries' "Srok Srok Yeung" is back, performing at the end of every month at Chip Mon No Rom Mall
The re-launch of the "Srok Yeung Srok" project shows the ambition to continue to inspire all Cambodian children, especially the younger generation, to support the talents and works of Cambodian art that have been inherited for a long time.
Dr. Im Sothearith, Public Relations Director of Khmer Breweries, said that the decision to return the "Art of Our District" project, held in the center of Phnom Penh, will make it easier for Cambodian art fans to visit as well. To participate in preserving the Khmer art form to become more famous than before.
It should be noted that the "Art of Our District" program is held six times from this July until the end of December 2020, held every last Sunday of each month at the Chip Monoromol Mall. Phnom Penh Municipal Police Rejects News on Social Media That Man Hanged Himself Due to Inability to Pay Bank Debt in Daun Penh
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Police on July 27, 2020, issued a press release completely rejecting the news on Facebook, posting that a man hanged himself because he had no money to pay the bank in Sangkat Srah Chak, Daun Penh district.
Immediately after receiving this information, the Information and Quick Reaction Team of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police would like to completely reject this Facebook account as false information based on the following grounds:
* First: On July 16, 2020 at 13:30 in front of Wat Preah Puth Khou Sachar, Street 47, Village 14, Sangkat Srah Chak, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, there was a case of a homeless person committing suicide by tying A. According to the police who conducted the autopsy, the man committed suicide by hanging himself and was not involved in any debt.
* Second: According to the detailed report of Daun Penh District Police Inspectorate, Srah Chak Police Station and the medical team also pumped urine (10cc) from the body to analyze the positive results of methamphetamine.
* Third: After the situation arose, the specialized units of Khan and Post guarded the scene and reported to the Prosecutor, Technical and Scientific Office, Office of Serious Crimes and Physicians of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to establish a forensic examination committee. That the man died by hanging himself and had drugs in his body.
* Fourth: After examining the body, the technical police office handed over the body to the police officer of Srah Chak Administrative Police Station to be taken to Wat Tuol Sak Lok for a traditional ceremony. Authorities Detain Assailant in Krakor District, Pursat Province
(Pursat): A drunken man broke into a woman's house and tried to arrest her, but she refused, then complained to the authorities to detain him in a defamation case.
This incident happened at 23:30 on July 25, 2020 at the victim's house in Thkol Touch village, Ansa Chambok commune, Krakor district, Pursat province.
As for the suspect, his name is Soeun Soeum, male, 30 years old, Khmer, farmer, living in the same commune, his wife is Mer Et, 30 years old, Khmer, farmer, they have 3 children, 2 girls.
The suspect is currently being held at the Krakor District Police Inspectorate on the orders of Mr. Koy Kanya, Prosecutor of the Pursat Provincial Prosecutor's Office, at 012 678 293, dated July 26, 2020, at 7:59 PM. Proceed according to the procedure. Strong-minded man fights in prison, resentful, comes out in revenge for cutting two people, seriously injured, was sent back to prison by the authorities
(Banteay Meanchey): A strong-minded man fights in prison with resentment in revenge for cutting two people seriously.
After receiving the complaint, following the order of Major General At Cam, the Provincial Police Commissioner of Poipet City, the police conducted a search and, with the identification of the victim, the police arrested the suspect, Meas Sopheak, male, 30 years old. Occupation: Worker living in Palilei 1 Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province. They confiscated a long knife and some smoking materials.
It should also be noted that the suspect was a person who used to actively smoke drugs until the authorities arrested him in the past. In front of the police, the suspect confessed that he and Rin Miley had a fight in prison and used to fight at the General Market at the casino.
Based on the victim's complaint and the suspect's confession. The suspect was sent to the provincial police commission by the Poipet City Criminal Police Force and sent to the prison on the morning of July 26, 2020 to be punished according to the law. Mr. Sar Sokha will take the example of the green school that has been implemented in Banteay Meanchey province and disseminate it to other schools throughout the country.
(Banteay Meanchey): Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, together with the accompanying delegation, presided over the implementation of the Green School project under an agreement between the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Caritas Switzerland in Banteay Meanchey province.
The event was also attended by Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey, Deputy Governor, Mr. Mark Clarkler, Country Director, Caritas Switzerland, Director of the Department of Education, Governor of the city, district office, teachers in the provincial hall. Banteay Meanchey in the morning of July 26, 2020.
Mr. McClellan said that he was very pleased with the excellent cooperation from the provincial leadership, especially the Ministry and the Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports in the implementation of the Green School project in Banteay Meanchey to contribute to the promotion of education as well. Promote a clean and green school environment.
Mr. Sar Sokha also thanked Caritas Switzerland for selecting Banteay Meanchey and for funding the implementation of the Green School by selecting 45 schools to implement the project.
Mr. Sar Sokha stated that he will take the model of green school that has been implemented in Banteay Meanchey province to promote to other schools across the country in the implementation of green school to improve the aesthetics of the school to be beautiful. Comfortable and arranged as a flower garden, toilet, hand wash and so on.
With the implementation of the Green School project, Mr. Sar Sokha also stressed that all school management to implement this Green School project, please participate in the implementation of this program well and all schools to participate in the implementation of this project to increase The aesthetics of the school are comfortable and beautiful.
Two dirt roads with a length of more than 1 km in 3 villages of Sre Thmei commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province turned into concrete roads
(Kampong Chhnang): Two red gravel roads in Village 3, Sre Thmei Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province, with a length of 1,172 meters. To facilitate traffic for local people, this is another new development under the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister.
Nou Khean, chief of Sre Thmey commune, said on the evening of July 26, 2020 that according to the unanimous meeting of the commune council in 2020, the commune has decided to spend the commune fund plus the people's contribution. 29,311,949 Riels for the people in the commune to build two red gravel roads back into concrete roads to make it easier for people to travel.
Regarding the construction of this road, Mr. Sok Han, President of the above concrete road construction contractor, said that the construction of a 855-meter-long road in Kdei Tnaot and Chamkar Tamao villages was built according to the possible standards. In the next 2 months. The road at Trapeang Along in Trea Cheung village will be rebuilt when the concrete road in Kdei Tnaot and Chamkar Tamao villages is completed.
Residents in the three villages that received the new concrete road also said that every year, people in every village in the commune pay a contribution of 1,000 riel per family to build the road, but some families who have some relief. Also pay 5,000 or 10,000 Riels for building a local road to make it easy for everyone to travel.
The people would also like to express their deep gratitude to the commune authorities, especially the head of the Royal Government, for providing the commune fund with the contribution of the people in the commune to build the above concrete road to alleviate the difficulties for the people. Three Ministries Sign Measures to Prevent and Eliminate Frequency Interference in Cambodia Air Navigation System
(Phnom Penh): On July 27, 2020, the Ministry of Information, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications and the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation signed the "Measures to Prevent and Eliminate Frequency Interference in the Air Navigation System of Cambodia". .
The signing ceremony was presided over by Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications and Mr. Mao Havanal, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation at the Preah Vihear Hall of the Ministry of Information.
After the signing ceremony, a press conference was held on the official launch of this inter-ministerial proclamation.
