Mr. Kun Kim urged the CPP working group in Oddar Meanchey province to try to solve all the problems of the people
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Kun Kim, Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Working Group, on Sunday, July 26, 2020, chaired a meeting to review the work achieved by the working group in July and set work directions for the following month.
The meeting was also attended by Mr. Pen Kosal, President of the Cambodian People's Party in Oddar Meanchey Province and Mr. Siprasit, Vice President of the Party.
In this meeting, the working group reviewed the work achieved in July, such as meeting with people in the backyard, helping people living in poverty and those affected by Covid-19 disease throughout the province, as well as helping Donate money to them. As well as helping to solve various problems.
During the meeting, Mr. Kun Kim praised and appreciated the team's efforts to respond to the difficulties of the people in a timely and effective manner.
However, Mr. Kun Kim reminded the members of the working group that the mission to the grassroots to help solve all the problems of the people, so must do their best to solve the problems that happen to the people. He also instructed the working group to cooperate with the district and provincial authorities and professional institutions to try to solve the remaining remaining challenges.
Mr. Kun Kim stressed that all working groups must remember the advice of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and Prime Minister that "the suffering of the people is the suffering of our party of our officials."
He added that under any circumstances, the participation of local people in solving problems must be implemented in accordance with the slogan that the CPP originated from the people, belongs to the people and to People.
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Touch Poliva, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province and Chairman of the Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party to Assist Thna Thnong Commune, Romduol District, Svay Rieng Province, reminded the Commune Council to pay attention to implement the Royal Government's cash subsidy program for families. Poverty During the spread of Kovid 19, properly targeted and transparent procedures for the truly poor.
This statement was made by Mr. Touch Poliva at the meeting to review the results of the first half of the year and to raise the work direction for 2020 of the working group of the Cambodian People's Party in Thna Thnong commune, Svay Rieng province, on the morning of July 26, 2020.
He said that the commune authorities need to strengthen the provision of better public services to the people, including request and service requirements and civil status, identity cards, marriage and death certificates, and all forces must strive to improve security and order, especially Implement the 9 points of safe villages and communes successfully.
He said that we must continue to educate our children to avoid all kinds of drugs, not only to obey the traffic law and to drive with a seatbelt wearing a helmet to avoid any accidents that may occur and to strive to grow rice. Rainy season in a timely manner and be very careful of natural disasters to find a safe place during the rainy season.
He stressed the need to strengthen internal unity, emotional and political issues, and jointly support the government's political program to be more effective.
Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An calls on people to adhere to the principles of maintaining the social gap and the measures of the Ministry of Health to prevent Kovid 19
(Kampong Speu): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, presided over a get-together with the Women of the Cambodian Women's Association for Peace and Development and Mothers (Sui Ethnic Group) in Ta Sal Commune, Oral District. Kampong Speu province, about 400 people in the morning of Sunday, the 6th day of the month of Srap, the year of Chuot Tosak, BE 2564, which is on July 26, 2020.
Speaking on this occasion, Ms. Men Sam An also sent a message of greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to all people throughout Kampong Speu province, both Samdech always think highly of daily life. People's Day.
She added that the event was organized because the country is peaceful and developed in all areas, especially for Kampong Speu province has also changed from a war-torn area to an area with attractive development potential. These developments also came from the contribution of women at all levels, including women in Kampong Speu.
She also called on all citizens to continue to respect and adhere to the principles of maintaining the social gap and the measures set by the Ministry of Health and to remain vigilant in preventing and preventing the spread of disease. Kovid 19 of the second wave at a time when the world is facing a severe pandemic due to Kovid 19.
She distributed gifts to women and people who attended the event with a sarong, a scarf and some money.
Border Police 815th Battalion Brings Money and Gifts to the Family of a Drowning Police Officer in Banteay Meanchey Province
(Banteay Meanchey): Colonel Suong Sao, Commander of the 815th Border Police, Battalion, on July 26, 2020, handed over some money and gifts to the family of a police officer whose father drowned.
Donations include: Colonel Suong Sao's personal budget of $ 100, 50 kg of rice, 20 sticks of pure water and the post of dead tiger, 100,000 Riels, 50 kg of rice, 4 sticks of pure water and 2 sticks of orange juice To offer condolences to Lieutenant Kong Seng Im, Post Officer Khla Ngab.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dim Sovannarom, Member and Spokesperson of the National Election Committee (NEC), thanked the Government of India for its continued assistance to the NEC. In particular, to help train NEC officials to strengthen their capacity to serve this electoral body.
Welcoming the presence of Ms. Manika Chen before starting yoga, Mr. Dim Sovannarom emphasized that the Government of India has always provided close cooperation with the NEC, which shows the good cooperation between the two countries. At the same time, the NEC has always received good cooperation with the NEC of India.
The spokesman reminded that the Government of India has provided scholarships to about 31 Cambodian NEC officials to participate in election-related training in India from 2015 to 2020. In February 2020, for the first time, the NEC of Cambodia received special training on electoral management for 22 NEC delegates from the Government of India through the Embassy of India in Cambodia.
On behalf of the NEC, Mr. Dim Sovannarom expressed his deep gratitude to the Government of India as well as the Embassy of India for the good cooperation so far. The NEC will continue to welcome any cooperation with the Government of India for the benefit of both nations.
Tea Seiha's wife donates 69 beds worth over 20,000 USD to Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital
(Siem Reap): Ms. Teang Eng Tea Seiha, Vice Chairman of the Branch Committee, Representative Mr. Tea Seiha, Chairman of the Branch Committee and colleagues on the morning of July 26, 2020, handed over 69 beds at a cost of 20 $ 010 to Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital to be deposited in the hospital building for inpatients.
The Vice President thanked the staff, officials and management of this hospital as well as the officials of the Department of Health and expressed the care of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross. Always thinking about the well-being and hardships of all the people all over the country, especially the poor people who have a lot of diseases to be hospitalized.
She added that this is also a contribution to the Royal Government of Cambodia in accelerating the reduction of poverty, protection of dignity and humanitarian values of humanity. On the other hand, it is in support of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and a national figure at the United Nations Secretary-General's Joint Action Plan for the Health of Women and Children.
She added that in order to contribute to the humanitarian work to save the lives of Cambodians and humanitarian values, the Cambodian Red Cross Siem Reap branch brought $ 20,010 to support the Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital to help fill the shortage. Hospital and to facilitate patients who need to be treated at this hospital.
Ms. Teang Eng Tea Seiha added that although the amount of money donated was limited, we hope that it will make a significant contribution to support the rescue activities of our people.
After the handover ceremony, she and her delegation visited patients who were being treated and inspected new beds and locations.
It should also be noted that Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital is an office of the Provincial Health Department that provides 3 sets of complementary activities with only 370 hospital beds. People in Siem Reap and people from other provinces also need to expand the hospital.
