(Phnom Penh): On July 25, 2020, Mr. Duong Dara, Personal Assistant to the Prime Minister and Undersecretary of State in the Office of the Council of Ministers, facilitated the conciliation of the one-year-old dispute. Horm Horm, a Cambodian-American and Mr. Mak Pheap in Battambang province, on the principle of winning over Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
This love affair led the two to reach the sacrificial ceremony, which was heard by the neighbors and the village and commune authorities. After living together for a while, Mr. Mak was dissatisfied with Ms. Horm because he drank alcohol and insulted her and her siblings. Mr. Mak Pheap was lying on his back and did not give his phone number to his girlfriend, Ms. Horm Horm. Their love affair broke down and they parted ways.
In fact, the two have been arguing with each other for almost a year. Because everyone is strong and wants to win, there is no solution together, even with the help of the village chief and the commune chief. On July 20, 2020, Ms. Horm Ham sought a letter from Samdech Techo asking for his help in seeking justice for her, alleging that a Cambodian man from Battambang had cheated her out of money and heart.
On Saturday, July 25, Mr. Duong Dara, Samdech Techo's personal assistant and Undersecretary of State in the Office of the Council of Ministers, visited the house to check the situation and met with them and Mr. Mak Pheap's two sisters. Po Battambang village chief Muon Ray as well.
