(Preah Vihear): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, accompanied by Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province and his colleagues, this morning, July 26, 2020, met with farmers and distributed plastic tents. Frogs and fish feed to 50 farmers in Po Khoeun village, Po commune, Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province.
In addition, other partner projects have contributed to providing technology to 250 fish farming families and compiled into 2 farmer clusters to facilitate negotiations with the market.
The director of the department also shared his experience of raising frogs and catfish in plastic tents of farmer Ou Hok Ly living in Po Khoeun village, Po commune, Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province. The farmer started to try to raise frogs in plastic tents in 2018, 5 tents totaling 60 square meters and catfish in 2 plastic tents totaling 40 square meters.
On average, he can raise frogs and catfish three times a year, of which 1,800 kilograms of frogs are sold for a profit of about 10.5 million riels and 2,700 kilograms of catfish are sold in One year, earn more than 24 million riels.
Taking this opportunity, Minister Veng Sakhon expressed his pleasure to meet with the farmers and the Minister also brought greetings to all farmers from Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kittiprittbandit. Both of them always miss and care about the well-being of the people everywhere.
He said that in the context of the Kovid 19 epidemic, to ensure food security, increase employment opportunities and income for farmers, Samdech Techo Prime Minister launched a campaign to promote the implementation of aquaculture activities across the country this morning, the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry. Hunting and fishing brought some materials to distribute to 50 virtual farmers, each family received 700 catfish or 400 frogs and 100 kg of feed.
(Banteay Meanchey): Provincial Administration, Local Officials, in collaboration with the Department of Health, launched a campaign to prevent dengue fever and chlamydia in Banteay Meanchey Province this morning, July 26, 2019, with the participation of Mr. Ly Sary, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, Mongkul Borei District Administration and teachers. Doctors from many health departments.
Mr. Ly Sary said that after the outbreak of bird flu in Poipet to six villages, the provincial administration has ordered the launch of a campaign to prevent dengue fever and chickenpox. Situation.
He added that only on the morning of July 26, he and his team applied Abate in the local village in Mongkul Borei district for a whole day. He said that in the campaign to put Abet in the village, he also promoted the prevention and prevention of dengue fever and chickenpox to the people in Mongkul Borei district.
He further stated that in launching the education campaign to prevent and prevent dengue fever and dengue fever, the aim is to educate all people in Banteay Meanchey province to understand about dengue fever and dengue fever, it is a deadly disease. Let everyone work together to prevent the spread of dengue fever and chikungunya to reduce the mortality rate of these two diseases.
He said that dengue fever, especially dengue fever in 2029 is different from previous years, because in the past the disease was only on children, but today it is on people of all ages, so the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as subordinate institutions. Issued guidelines for officials and people to cooperate with the provincial health department to prevent the spread of dengue fever and chickenpox to people in all areas.
He added that today, the team is launching a campaign to educate people through mobile vehicles, putting abattoirs in water bottles in people's backyards and cleaning up the environment, eliminating tiger mosquito habitats and continuing the campaign. In some other districts there were outbreaks of dengue fever and chikungunya.
He added that if we suspect that our child has symptoms such as high fever for more than 2 days, red rash on the skin, abdominal pain and body aches, must be sent to a hospital near the house immediately, not more than 8 days. Doctors can save.
Phnom Penh Municipal Police Rejects Information Accusing Traffic Officials of Kidnapping Money at Chom Chao Roundabout
(Phnom Penh): The Information and Quick Reaction Team of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police on July 26, 2020 issued an explanation clarifying and rejecting the information posted that a traffic officer kidnapped money at the Chaom Chao roundabout.
