Payment of benefits to the poor in June was completed, more than 530,000 families paid (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Payment of allowances for the poor and the most vulnerable to Kovid 19 The first for June 2020 was completed by July 24, 2020 yesterday. More than 530,000 families came to pay the allowance, while more than 20,000 families did not pay.
According to a statement from the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, obtained by Fresh News on Saturday, July 25, 2020, the payment of allowances for the poor and vulnerable for June is Closed at 6 pm on July 24, 2020.
The press release also said that the budget of the Royal Government donated a total of 94,551,876,000 Riels, equivalent to more than 23 million US dollars.
According to preliminary figures, up to 560,000 poor and vulnerable families are receiving government subsidies. But those who came to receive the allowance were just over 530,000 families.
Sam Heng Boros, secretary of state at the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and an operational officer, told Fresh News that most of the families who did not pay the allowance were not at home. Mr. Sam Hengbros confirmed that according to the report of the local authority, most of the families who did not come to receive the allowance migrated.
According to Mr. Sam Heng, the family man who did not come to pay the allowance is tantamount to not accepting the allowance, and their share will be dropped back into the national budget for next month.
After closing the allowance payment for June, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation will start preparing the allowance payment for July from July 25 onwards. The ministry has called on families who have already verified in June to open at any Wing specialized bank without being required to visit the commune hall again.
Separately, poor and vulnerable families who have a valid equity card that has not been verified in June and poor families who have just received a new equity card must go to a commune / sangkat for verification for July. .
According to the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the number of poor and vulnerable families that will be subsidized for July has reached 610,000, with a budget of more than 28 million US dollars. .
It should be noted that in order to solve the hardships of people who are poor and vulnerable to Kovid 19, the Royal Government of Cambodia has released a national budget of about 125 million US dollars for monthly support for them. The first phase of this sponsorship takes place in June and July. However, if Kovid 19 has not disappeared from Cambodia, the Royal Government will continue to support it in the coming months.
To receive this allowance, poor and vulnerable families must have a valid equity card based on poverty level: poor level 1 (poor) or poor level 2 (poor) and go to verify the list of cash aid programs. Poor families during the fight against Kovid 19 at a commune hall.
