Spokesman for the General Commission: On July 25, another 1,105 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 86 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to July 25, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 11,8464 vehicles, including 87,677 motorcycles and 30,787 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 86 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for July 25, 2020, traffic crimes across Cambodia also occurred 10 times, in which 4 people died, 19 people were injured (12 seriously injured).
