Raising chickens is being evaluated in Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province, senior officials of the Ministry of Agriculture and provincial governor urge farmers to increase the raising of farm chickens
(Kandal): Agricultural business clusters have been established in 4 out of 8 communes, 24 clusters of farmers, a total of 761 families, in which many agricultural occupations are seen as farmers are busy cultivating and raising animals. The most prominent occupation in Khsach Kandal district is "raising chickens in the field".
According to the district agriculture official, this business is the most popular among the farmers, as raising chickens is hitting the market as demand increases.
Khsach Kandal District Agriculture Officer said this in front of the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Huot Bunnary, and Mr. Kong Sophorn, Governor of Kandal Province, and many other officials during the visit to promote agricultural production. In Sanlong and Chey Thom communes, Khsach Kandal district, on July 24, 2020.
Mr. Huot Bunnary praised the farmers who have been working hard to build this agricultural business for the benefit of all farmers to exchange experiences and help each other to increase agricultural production as much as possible. Yes.
