(Siem Reap): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, accompanied by a delegation from the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Fisheries Administration and colleagues on July 25, 2020 visited the frog hatchery. Mr. Kong Kim Chhay's shop is located in Angkor Village, Kantraing Commune, Prasat Bakong District, Siem Reap Province.
The scholar started breeding in 2017 after graduating with a Bachelor of Science in Fisheries at the end of 2016, starting with breeding 30 pairs of breeds and now he has 2,000 breeds and 5,000 reserve breeds. The head covers an area of about 2,500 square meters. On average, out of 2,000 breeds, he is able to incubate and sell offspring for a monthly income of about $ 2,000.
Mr. Kong Kim Chhay confirmed to Minister Veng Sakhon that the problem in raising frogs is the price of food because we use imported food.
