The following is the Royal Decree of the King: Tang Krasang Health Center in Kampong Thom Province received a new building as a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Kampong Thom): A new two-story building has been donated to Tang Krasang Health Center in Santuk District, a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to facilitate the local people.
The donation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's new two-story building was donated to Tang Krasang Health Center through Mr. Chea Chanto, Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the National Task Force to Assist Santuk District on July 24. 2020.
Mr. Chea Chanto said that the new building was a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to Tang Krasang Health Center. And health promotion for the people in this area and for the health center to be able to diagnose and treat various diseases.
He added that the new building will be built in the future, with a length of 45 meters, a width of 16 meters, a height of 2 floors and 28 rooms. In that, he requested the doctors to pay more attention and be more responsible in treating people.
He added that at the same time, people must continue to be educated on how to prevent the spread of Kovi 19 as instructed by the Ministry of Health.
Mr. Men Sinath, Director of Tang Krasang Health Center, said that the health center now has a lot of need for examination and treatment for the people, especially the room for the patient's accommodation because the building of the health center is dilapidated from the past and There is less room, which is why there is a lack of room to receive patients.
Mr. Men Sinath and all the doctors expressed their deep gratitude to Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for their devotional spirit, who always think about the health of the people. In fact, by providing a new building to Tang Krasang Health Center, it is clear that where there are difficulties, there is always a double prince.
During the visit, Mr. Chea Chanto also provided Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to patients and doctors. Banteay Meanchey provincial police continue to patrol the border to prevent illegal entry into Thai territory while preventing Kovid-19
(Banteay Meanchey): The 815th Border Police Force of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police continues to patrol the border and prevent illegal border crossing in Malai District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Mr. Suong Sao emphasized that the regular patrols of the police force are aimed at preventing various crimes that occur along the Cambodian-Thai border, especially to prevent Cambodian workers from crossing the border illegally into Thai territory while Thailand is also preventing Kovid-19.
At the same time, Mr. Suong Sao also warned Cambodian workers not to cheat brokers further, while currently crossing the border into Thailand is not allowed. In addition, taxis in Thailand do not dare to transport Cambodian workers, because if taxis dare to transport people without a proper medical examination will be fined.
The commander also did not forget to instruct the forces to pay attention to the implementation of the orders of the higher level, which instructed and educated the people to protect the health and hygiene of the Ministry of Health to avoid Kovid-19. .
Bodyguard Command Closes Closing Ceremony and Presents Royal Cambodian Martial Arts Certificate to Intervention Force 594
(Kandal): The Bodyguard Command organized the closing ceremony of the training course and handed over the Royal Cambodian Martial Arts Certificate to the officers and deputies of the 594th Intervention Brigade, which is the bodyguard base of Phnom Penh. The ceremony was presided over by Lt. Gen. Duong Heng, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Deputy Commander of the Bodyguard Command.
Speaking on the occasion, Lt. Gen. Yin Chanthuon, Commander of the 594th Intervention Brigade, emphasized that this is the first time that the 594th Intervention Brigade has included the Martial Arts Program in the training program aimed at enhancing the strong capabilities of the soldiers in their roles. Special tasks contribute to the preservation of the national cultural heritage, Khmer ancient martial arts, which is an indispensable heritage of Khmer ancestors.
The lieutenant general added that in addition to this new martial art, the trainers have been trained in other disciplines in order to strengthen and expand their capacity to cooperate in cooperation with the authorities at all levels, the armed forces of all kinds in the fight against prevention. Changes in national security.
Defend the peace, oppose the color revolution, strengthen the image of national defense, security, protect the integrity of Cambodian territory to be even stronger, especially in the protection of security, security to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen And the family to achieve 100 percent.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Dr. Duong Heng and Mr. You Sinath highly appreciated and commended the officers, deputies and soldiers in the 594th Intervention Force of the Prime Minister's Bodyguard Command, who made every effort to find All methods of training as well as raising the awareness of the competent forces.
Lt. Gen. Duong Heng continued that this new martial art is not to serve the fighting between our nations, but to be the energy and wisdom for all nations to maintain health, to maintain health and energy to the forces. We. Afterwards, the delegation distributed certificates to the participants and gave some money.
Murder! A young man was killed in a banana plantation of Hang Anh Company, Kon Mom District, Ratanakkiri Province on suspicion of jealousy
(Ratanakkiri): A young man was found dead in the banana plantation of Hang Anh Company, Sre Pok Thom Village, Serey Mongkul Commune, Kon Mom District, Ratanakkiri Province at noon on July 24, 2020.
The report of the Kon Mom District Police Inspectorate, which was received by Fresh News this morning, July 25, 2020, said that immediately after receiving the information, the serious criminal police force, in cooperation with the Serei Mongkul Administration Post, arrived at the scene to Inspect the body. As a result, it was found to be a murder case (stabbed with a knife and beaten with a stick) with multiple scars on the neck and several knife operations.
According to the investigation, at 20:10 on July 23, 2020, the victim, Kim Saroeun alias Tong, 26 years old, was born in Tron village, Boeung Nay commune, Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province. Drinking with the suspect named Bak Nan, 24 years old, was born in Boeung Kampot village, Banteay Chakrei commune, Preah Sdach district, Prey Veng province.
After drinking, at about 8 pm, the day of the incident, they asked each other to look at the frog and have been missing ever since. Until 15:00 on July 24, 2020, the bodies of the victims were found.
According to the competent experts, the murder of the above victim was suspected of jealousy, which led to the murder. Authorities said the suspect had been working at the Hang Anh banana plantation for six months after fleeing. After an autopsy, the body was handed over to the family for a traditional ceremony.
In relation to the above case, Brigadier General Phen Dina, Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Planning of Ratanakkiri Province, told Fresh News Agency in Ratanakkiri Province on the morning of July 25, 2020 that the authorities have identified the target and are taking legal action. . The King issued a Royal Decree conferring the honorary title of "Honorary Doctor" to Mr. Nguon Nhel
