Chinese Embassy: Cambodia's Banana Plantation Increases to 15 Companies with More Than 8,000 Hectares of Cultivation, Authorized to Export Fresh Bananas to China (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Chinese Embassy in Cambodia on July 25 By 2020, up to 15 banana plantations in Cambodia, with more than 8,000 hectares of banana plantations and 21 packaging factories, have been approved by the Chinese government to be exported to China. .
The Chinese embassy confirmed that the Chinese customs administration recently allowed five more companies to package Cambodia's banana exports to China for the fourth time, bringing the total to 15 companies.
Please be informed that in the first half of 2020, the export of bananas was more than 140,000 tons, valued at more than 68 million US dollars. This is according to the figures recorded by the Ministry of Commerce.
(Siem Reap): Finally, the man who raised a knife threatened to kill his aunt and destroy property by carrying a machete, walking alone on the street and cutting a motorbike, as well as stealing a car of a citizen, causing surprise and fear in Siem Reap He was arrested by the authorities from the top of Tbeng Meanchey mountain, Preah Vihear province.
Brigadier General Huot Sothy, Deputy Commissioner for Security Planning, who led the operation, said that with the guidance and attention of the Provincial Unity Command, the man who caused the fear had been arrested. On the afternoon of July 24, 2020, on the top of Tbeng Meanchey mountain in Kraing Dong village, Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province.
He added that the Siem Reap Provincial Police Force was led by and directly involved in the administrative police force of Sangkat Svay Dangkum, Siem Reap City, in cooperation with the security plan of the Tbeng Meanchey District Police Inspectorate of Preah Vihear Provincial Police, and arrested the suspect named Em Panha. 27 years old, living in Vihear Chen village, Svay Dangkum commune, Siem Reap city.
Please be reminded that on July 18, 2020, near Build Bright School in Vihear Chen Village, Svay Dangkum Sangkat, Siem Reap City, the above-mentioned person used a machete to cut himself on the street and cut a motorbike and drove a citizen's car. Escape items left in Prasat Bakong district.
According to the authorities, because such cases occur, the Siem Reap provincial authorities have been hunting because he has made some people worried. The suspect went into hiding on Phnom Poul, Phnom Tbeng Meanchey to stay temporarily.
Currently, the authorities have brought the suspect to Siem Reap to build a case for legal action.
