The performance of the Hajj or Hajj is in accordance with the Qur'an and Sunnah, or the actions of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, more than 1,377 years ago.
The Supreme Council of Islam of Cambodia has set Wednesday, July 22, 2020 as the first day of the month of Zul-Hijjah, so the Raya Hajj festival will start on Friday, July 31, 2020, which is Friday, the tenth of Zul-Hijjah. Until August 3, 2020. In particular, some who did not go on religious pilgrimages in Mecca and Madinah could donate money to buy cattle, goats, sheep, or camels to share with their neighbors and the poor.
But at the same time, Satan (the devil) tried to persuade Ibrahim not to obey this command, but Ibrahim responded by throwing stones at Satan. Ibrahim obeyed, but at the same time Allah accepted his faith and his son by letting him kill the beast instead of his son. That is why in this Hajj, Muslims are required to kill animals such as cows, sheep or camels and distribute them to their neighbors.
