Taking this opportunity to improve the quality of fair and just trials, as well as to improve the provision of justice services easily, quickly and cleanly, the Minister instructed the judges, prosecutors, court officials and all civil servants of the school. First and the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, as well as in other courts throughout the country as follows:
* Second: Judges, prosecutors, as well as all court officials must adhere to their strictness in applying the law properly in order to provide an impartial trial to ensure fairness to the people in particular. Abstinence from the four virtues: will, will, guilt, delusion, and delusion, as all judges and prosecutors have sworn in before taking office.
* Fifth: Judges, prosecutors, as well as all court officials and civil servants must pay attention to their work by strengthening internal unity and strengthening good cooperation with relevant authorities and institutions to ensure the good functioning of the institution. Courts, as well as the effectiveness of providing justice to the people.
It should be noted that Mr. Chreung Khmao, former Prosecutor of the Kampong Cham Provincial Prosecutor's Office, has been transferred to the position of Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, replacing Mr. Keo Sothea, who has been transferred to work at the Ministry of Justice through a Royal Decree. July 18, 2020.
