The following is a list of 184 countries and territories showing the total number of cases, deaths and cures of COVID-19: Ministry of Commerce formally adopts e-commerce strategy
A meeting to review and approve this strategy was held on Thursday, July 23, 2020 at the Ministry of Commerce, chaired by Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, and was attended by officials from other relevant ministries.
Mr. Pan Sosak said that in the context of the Industrial Revolution 4.0, digital technology is the key to boosting the competitiveness of enterprises, businesses and business processes, which contributes to increasing productivity, increasing exports, creating jobs and boosting growth. National economy.
In response to the Royal Government's strategic policy, the Ministry of Commerce has developed an e-commerce strategy as a roadmap for the development of e-commerce, a new sector with high potential for creating growth sources. New for the Cambodian economy.
The e-commerce strategy is designed in a cellular manner and responds to the recommendations set forth in other trade-related strategic documents, including the Cambodia Trade Integration Strategy 2019-2023, as well as strategies and Policy documents and sectoral strategies of relevant ministries and institutions.
Mr. Pan Sosak also said that the e-commerce strategy was developed at the right time, while Cambodia has the e-commerce law, which was promulgated on November 2, 2019. Go.
The e-commerce law will serve as an important legal basis for the development of e-commerce. In particular, to protect the interests and build high confidence of customers in the use of e-commerce, as well as attract local and foreign investors to invest in e-commerce in Cambodia.
