Rangoon: The first satellite of the Union of Myanmar will be launched into space in the near future to assist in the early detection of natural disasters that could save millions of lives. This was released by CNA on Friday afternoon, July 24, 2020.
Myanmar's satellites, which are preparing to launch into orbit around the planet, are in a joint project with nine Asian countries to target typhoons, earthquakes and water resources, as well as research data. About the use of land that is useful for growing crops and preventing infectious diseases.
This is the first space investment for Myanmar, considered one of the least developed countries in Asia. The development of the joint satellite network above also involves some ASEAN countries such as the Philippines, Vietnam and Indonesia.
Myanmar plans to spend about $ 16 million on its first satellite launch as part of a budget of up to $ 100 million. The official launch will take place in early 2021 from Japan, and Myanmar has already set up a satellite control center on its territory.
