Senior Minister Kun Kim, together with the Governor of Siem Reap and other relevant officials, met on July 24, 2020 to address the issue of social land concessions for abused veterans.
The report shows that in 2017, the Royal Government of Cambodia provided 1,369 hectares of land in Khnar Sanday and Khun Ream communes, Banteay Srei district, Siem Reap province, to provide concessions to underprivileged Cambodian veterans for housing and crop production.
So far, only 384 hectares of land have been allotted to veterans, while nearly 600 hectares have been encroached upon by villagers. According to the report, some people have encroached on more than 5 hectares of this land.
Senior Minister Kun Kim said that in Siem Reap there are about 6,546 veterans and about 313 families of veterans do not have land or houses.
According to the Royal Government's policy, the families of needy veterans will be provided with half a hectare of land for housing and 2 hectares of land for cultivation. Such encroachment and encroachment on social land concessions by the people will make the Veterans Association lack land to distribute to the families of the veterans.
The senior minister warned that those who encroached on the veterans' land would not return the land to the Veterans Association, and the association would take legal action.
