(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thor Koeun, Under Secretary of State of the Ministry of Cults and Religions, this morning, July 24, 2020, led a Buddhist delegation to visit the Chinese Cultural Center in Phnom Penh. The visit was to exchange work experiences and discuss some work to strengthen cooperation between the Buddhist Academy and the Chinese Cultural Center in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Thor Koeun and the delegation were warmly welcomed by Mr. Chhean Yean Kang, President of the Chinese Cultural Center in Phnom Penh. Mr. Koeun also thanked Dr. Chea Monirith, Advisor to the Chinese Cultural Center in Phnom Penh and President of the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association, for facilitating the visit.
Mr. Thor Koeun and his delegation were visited by Mr. Chhean Yean Kang at the Chinese Cultural Center and presented some of the achievements of the Center to achieve the strengthening of relations and cooperation between Cambodia and China.
During his visit, Thor Koeun recalled the history of Cambodia-China relations, initiated by His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk and Chinese Prime Minister Zhou Englay in 1958. He also highlighted the current development of relations between the two countries under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the leadership of China.
He said that through the care and support of the leaders of the two countries today, the two countries' relations have become a full-fledged strategic partnership and fruitful political results. Economy, trade, culture, humanity, as well as regional and international affairs.
In addition to highlighting and recalling the history of the two countries' relations as well as achievements, Mr. Thor Koeun expressed his desire to see the Buddhist Academy and the Chinese Cultural Center in Phnom Penh increase cooperation with each other. More too.
To strengthen this cooperation, Mr. Thong Koeun provided four concepts, including:
1: Buddhism and Chinese Cultural Center should sign a memorandum of understanding between the two institutions after Buddhism drafted a joint content with the Chinese Cultural Center in Cambodia to come to me to submit to the Minister for decision.
2. A joint workshop should be organized to promote the traditional relationship between the people and the people of our two countries, especially the Buddhist relationship.
3: Should provide opportunities for leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Cults and Religions, in general, Buddhists, in particular, to visit to learn more about Chinese culture and library work, and if there is an opportunity to visit more at Xingzhi Bookstore .
4: The first Chinese-Khmer language training course should be organized in Buddhism to facilitate more successful communication between the cultures of the two countries in the future, and research should be expanded. Together and widely published.
Mr. Thor Koeun told Fresh News that the concept as well as the four proposals mentioned by Mr. Chhean Yean Kang, President of the Chinese Cultural Center in Phnom Penh agreed to consider and will respond in the near future. Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Environment Holds First Half Meeting and Continues Work to Strengthen Environmental Efficiency
