It should be reminded that "Insurance Day" was held for the first time on July 25, 2019 in order to promote the growth of the Cambodian insurance market and help raise public awareness, as well as encourage institutions. Insurers who run their business with good governance as well.
The insurance sector is now moving forward with vigor, with progress coming from the energetic joint efforts of all stakeholders. In fact, as of now, Cambodia has 16 general insurance companies, 13 life insurance companies and 5 micro-insurance companies engaged in doing business in Cambodia.
This is a testament to the confidence of both domestic and foreign investors in the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as the growing public awareness of the importance of insurance. In 2019, the total insurance premiums of the insurance market reached about 251.6 million US dollars, an increase of 29% compared to 2018, and paid compensation to customers about 35.47 million US dollars, an increase of 46% compared to last year. 2018.
Insurance is a part of the financial system that has played an important role in the development of the national economy and contributes to the provision of hedging mechanisms for individuals and legal entities. The growth of the insurance sector is one of the factors driving the growth of many other sectors through the investment of excess funds of insurance companies, such as real estate, bonds of Cambodia, the securities market of Cambodia, insurance and banking.
At the same time, the Royal Government of Cambodia has focused on modernizing the payment system, strengthening the legal and regulatory framework, governance and transparency, and the security network of the Fourth Industrial Revolution and the digital economy, which has largely supported the The financial system operates efficiently and securely and has played an important role in contributing to the growth of the insurance sector in Cambodia.
