Kandal Provincial Police Chief Denies False Information in Case of Man Hanging Himself for Upset for Not Going to Work in Korea
(Kandal): Kandal Provincial Police has issued a clarification letter regarding the case of a man who hanged himself because he was upset and did not go to work in Korea because he did not pass the exam due to poor health. Suicide.
The provincial police have completely rejected this information and taken action against those who spread false information, leading to social unrest. This is according to the clarification letter of Kandal Provincial Police, which was received by Fresh News Agency in Kandal province on the evening of July 24, 2020.
Kandal Provincial Police confirmed that on July 22, 2020, information related to the death of an unidentified man was found at a plot of land in Ang Snuol village, Peuk commune, Ang Snuol district, Kandal province.
After receiving this information, the specialized force of Kandal Provincial Police investigated and obtained the following information:
* First: On July 22, 2020, at 11:40 AM, a man named Mao Sarath, 32 years old, Khmer, unspecified occupation, resided at Orda village, Buor commune, Phnom Prek district, Battambang province, hanged himself at The lot is located in Ang Snoul village, Peuk commune, Ang Snoul district, Kandal province.
* Second: According to the explanation from Uon Soy, male, 59 years old, ethnic Khmer, occupation Farmer, living in Prek Heang village, Kork Po commune, Borey Chulsar district, Takeo province (the victim's name) Went to work in Korea but failed the exam due to health problems.
* Third: Based on the autopsy results of the competent experts and doctors, it was concluded that the victim, Mao Sarath, actually committed suicide by hanging himself. The cause of suicide may be due to a mental crisis, health problems and unwillingness to go to work in Korea.
