(Svay Rieng): At least two people were killed and another was seriously injured when a motorbike overtook and collided with a car in the opposite direction.
This incident happened at 10:30 on July 24, 2020 on National Road 1 in Kampot Chrouk Village, Sangkat Prey Angkunh, Bavet City, Svay Rieng Province.
Arriving at the scene above, overtook a Highlander car in the same direction, oversteered and collided with a Sienna car traveling in the opposite direction from birth, sinking like lightning, causing scattering under another car. Two people were killed and another was seriously injured when they were taken to Chi Phu Hospital.
According to authorities, the identities of the two victims who died are not yet known and are still searching for relatives.
General Sao Sokha announces the appointment of a new Commander of Pursat Provincial Armed Forces after the death of the former Commander
(Pursat): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, this morning, July 24, 2020, presided over the appointment and inauguration of the new Commander of the Royal Gendarmerie. Pursat Province, after Brigadier General Ouk Samon, former Commander, recently passed away.
The above ceremony of announcing the position of Pursat Provincial Gendarmerie Commander was held at the meeting hall of Provincial Gendarmerie Command in O Sdao Village, Sangkat Phteah Prey, Pursat City, Pursat Province with the participation of Mr. Mao Thunin, Provincial Governor. Commanders, officers and deputies in large numbers.
Pursuant to Prakas No. 266TT / 0720 dated 21 July 2020 of the Ministry of National Defense, Colonel So Sovandy was appointed to replace the position of Deputy Commander and Chief of Staff of the Pursat Provincial Gendarmerie Command. .
Separately, Lieutenant Colonel Duch Samphors, Deputy Chief of Staff, has been appointed Chief of Staff of the Pursat Provincial Gendarmerie Command.
Two houses and a large amount of property were engulfed in fire due to a power outage in Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province
(Prey Veng): At least two houses were engulfed in flames, along with a large amount of property due to power outages. This case happened at 3:18 pm on July 23, 2020 in Prey Stor village, Smaong Cheung commune, Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province.
Siv Sokhom, police chief of Kamchay Mear district, said that two houses were on fire due to a short circuit while the owner was busy shopping in front of the house.
The inspector further stated that while the fire was burning heavily and spread to another house, the owner of the house shouted for the authorities to intervene, but the authorities arrived and the fire was already burning.
He said that the owner of the first house: Sao Than, a house with a tiled roof and walls, and Ron Theary, a house with two tiled roofs. Damaged items on the burnt house, including rice mills, bulldozers, totaled tens of thousands of dollars.
Union of Youth Federation of Cambodia Kampong Thom Visits 7-Year-Old Man
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Chea Van Chan, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Kampong Thom Province, and his colleagues handed over gifts to his younger brother, Sam Piseth, in O'Kanthor Tbong Village, Sangkat O'Kanthor, Stung Sen City. July 2020.
Sam Piseth said that he was 20 years old and had been paralyzed for seven years due to a traffic accident with a bulldozer when he was about 10 years old. Piseth has a father named Suon Sam and a mother named Eng Heng.
Due to the lack of livelihood, the parents were left alone in a small hut, miserable, without food, only the neighbors were kind.
Piseth said that because of poverty, your parents have to go far away from home to do business, leaving you to live alone without taking care of you.
Piseth continued that at first, your condition was normal, you can walk for a long time, but then you feel that it is difficult to travel until you have no legs to support your body to walk, but can move and lift. Up a little.
At the same time, Piseth appealed to Dr. Tevda Chea Sokheng and philanthropists to help him. Mr. Chea Van Chan expressed his sorrow and sympathy for Sam Sam Piseth, who was disabled and living in poverty, and he will do his best to find a philanthropist to help him recover.
During the visit, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia in Kampong Thom province brought 50 kg of rice, 1 kg of dried fish, 1 stick of soy sauce, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 box of noodles, 1 stick of fish and some money.
