Spokesman for the General Commission: On July 23, another 1,311 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 84 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to July 23, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 115,680 vehicles, including 85,547 motorcycles and 30,133 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 84 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for July 23, 2020, traffic crimes throughout Cambodia also occurred 6 times, in which 3 people died and 9 people were injured (06 people were seriously injured).
Senior Minister Kun Kim tells to speed up the procedure to hand over land to 153 families of veterans in Kampong Thom province
(Kampong Thom): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on the morning of July 23, 2020, instructed the leaders of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Kampong Thom province to cooperate with relevant institutions to expedite the process to hand over land to 153 families of veterans. Difficult.
Senior Minister Kun Kim's introduction was made during a meeting to review the performance of the Kampong Thom Veterans Association, which was attended by Mr. Sok Loo, Governor of Kampong Thom Province and Honorary President of the Provincial Veterans Association, as well as many other relevant officials. .
According to the report of Mr. Som Sun, President of the Provincial Veterans Association, in the first half of 2020, the Association has settled the payment of death allowances to the families of 44 veterans, equal to 176 million Riels, and built a house donated by Samdech Techo. Hun Sen donated 27 houses to poor veterans.
According to Mr. Som Sunkit, so far, veterans from all over Kampong Thom province have received 170 houses donated by Samdech Techo, President of the Association. Separately, those who have landless and 43 families who do not have suitable houses, the association must continue to deal with. In addition, there are 153 homeless families whose associations are preparing social land concessions to address them.
