(Phnom Penh): Major General Sok Samnang, Takeo Provincial Police Commissioner, in a press conference organized by the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit this morning, July 23, 2020, announced his strong commitment to crack down on drug crimes. Locally, like the early rain.
Major General Sok Samnang also raised the issue of drugs, although it is a global challenge, but requires the relevant authorities to crack down, because if drugs reach any place, it will lead to disaster there. Not to be missed.
Major General Sok Samnang said, "Takeo, like other provinces, we are victims of the drug problem, but while we are victims, we have measures to prevent trafficking and consumption. "The reduction, no matter how effective, we still maintain the crackdown like rain."
In addition to this commitment, the Takeo Provincial Police Commissioner presented three key measures to reduce drug offenses, including: First, the use of total measures, total force and total means, and second, educational measures to be disseminated. People, schools, public forums, and third: use professional measures to crack down on drugs.
The General Commissioner claimed that the police officers also need to increase their education and understanding about the drug problem, because if the police officers themselves do not understand the drug problem, they will not be able to crack down on drugs.
According to the report of Major General Sok Samnang, in the first half of 2020, Takeo Provincial Police cracked down on 29 drug offenses in 29 cases, arrested 58 people and arrested 8 people on 8 warrants. Captured evidences including: 53.48 grams of methamphetamine (Ice) and other exhibits, suspects and exhibits to build a case to the provincial court.
In particular, 59 out of 49 crimes were committed compared to 2019, an increase of 10 times, in which 8 out of 13 criminal offenses and 51 out of 36 misdemeanors resulted in 58 out of 59 cases. 73 suspects were arrested, including 7 out of 8 crimes, 12 suspects were arrested and 51 out of 51 misdemeanors were arrested, 61 suspects were arrested. Phnom Penh Gendarmerie Commander Releases 100 Tricycles for Technical Inspection
