(France): Napoleon Bonaparte was a famous emperor of the French Empire during the late 18th to early 19th centuries, but one problem arose in his life: the failure of The beauty of a hot widow in Italy and another princess in the Austrian Empire.
* Love story with Josephine
After the overthrow of the French monarchy in 1794, Napoleon, a major revolutionary, became commander-in-chief of the new republican army in 1795 and led the army to suppress the uprising against parliament. France in Italy, which was then a vassal state of the French Empire.
It was then that Napoleon met a widow with two children, Josephine, who fell in love with him after meeting her in a beauty salon. The captain who used to win all the battles, big and small, failed to fall in love, broke his courage because of the beauty of this beautiful widow.
At first, Josephine did not have much in common with Napoleon, but the young Napoleon always tried to stop her from meeting her, pleasing her to avoid quarreling, spreading clear words of love, beautiful proverbs, swearing at the widow. All turned to sympathy, thought, reciprocated the love to the groom, Bon Sak Udom Kray highlighted the love history for many months.
A great love affair took place between the two of them as the widow of Josephine accepted the love of Napoleon and they married in 1796.
Josephine was said to be a prostitute because she owed him a lot of money and ordered Napoleon to give her a lot of money to pay off her debt, and Napoleon knew about it, but he did not. No matter, because Napoleon's love for his wife was buried in these little things. Although they fell in love as a legal couple, Josephine suddenly became infertile.
In 1804, Napoleon became emperor of France with such great fame that many empires and peoples feared his power, and Josephine became the mother of the French Empire.
In the title of Empress Dowager, Josephine did not qualify for the monarchy at all, as she squandered her royal wealth on luxury items, seemingly carefree cosmetics. Her husband is at war in the distance.
* Love story with Princess Maria:
Before invading the Russian Empire, Napoleon invaded Austria in 1810. But during the battle with the Austrian army, he saw a princess with a beautiful, attractive face. This princess was named Maria Lewis, the daughter of the Austrian king.
Napoleon originally blamed himself for not being able to have children with his first wife, Josephine, but when he saw that his second wife, Mary, was pregnant, he changed his mind.
Napoleon also promoted his son to the rank of warrior king of Italy, but unfortunately Napoleon II went to rule Italy and died at a young age on July 22, 1832. Vienna, Austria.
The love affair between the exiled King Napoleon and Princess Maria has faded, with Napoleon suffering on a remote island in the middle of the sea, while Princess Maria is enjoying the status of empress in that glorious palace.
Towards the end of his reign, Napoleon was repeatedly defeated and again exiled by his allies to the island of St. Elena in the middle of the Atlantic Ocean, where he died in 1821.
