Why did the US close the Chinese consulate in Houston?
According to experts such as Jeff Moon, a former assistant to the US-China trade representative, there are five consulates in the United States, so if the closure of the Chinese consulate is to protect the intellectual property and private information of the American people. Why did the Donald Trump administration close only the Consulate in Houston?
* Chinese reaction
The Chinese Foreign Ministry has denied the allegations and called the US decision "unprecedented". Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman Wang Wenbin even warned that Beijing would retaliate if the United States did not withdraw its decision.
Speaking to reporters on Wednesday, Wang stressed: "China has asked the United States to rescind this wrong decision ... but if the United States does not agree, China will retaliate. Instead. ” The Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman added that Beijing has shown goodwill to US diplomats in China and promoted Sino-US relations through the Chinese ambassador to the United States.
US President Donald Trump has claimed that other Chinese consulates in the United States are also facing closure after receiving reports that officials at the Chinese consulate in Houston were set on fire. Discard some documents to eliminate evidence after being ordered to close.
