The meeting was held on the afternoon of July 21, 2020 at the Ministry of Economy and Finance, with the participation of relevant leaders and officials of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and international experts.
This "Initiative for the Establishment of a Credit Guarantee Corporation" is an urgent response mechanism of the Royal Government in line with the fourth round of measures to manage the impact on key sectors of the national economy during the Kovid-19 crisis and to restore and stimulate economic growth. Cambodia after the crisis.
"Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation" has the role of providing credit guarantee services to businesses in the priority areas severely affected by the Kovid-19 crisis to increase access to financing for those companies to secure working capital. Business Sustainability and Adaptation to the New Business Context After the Kovid-19 Crisis
Overall, after discussing the objectives, forms of establishment, expected challenges in the development process and action plan of project implementation, the Meeting agreed in principle on the conceptual document for the establishment of a credit guarantee corporation in Cambodia.
As a follow-up, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, with the General Department of Financial Industry as its secretary, will continue to process the necessary regulatory frameworks and cooperate with stakeholders to launch the credit guarantee corporation as soon as possible.
In the meantime, to ensure that credit unions provide effective targeted credit guarantees in the immediate aftermath of the Kovid-19 crisis, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, with the General Department of Policy as its secretary, will develop policies for The provision of this credit guarantee by identifying the sector, type of company and type of business, etc. that have the potential to receive credit guarantee from the Cambodian Credit Guarantee Corporation.
The Deputy Prime Minister thanked the leadership, relevant professional officers as well as international experts for their efforts in preparing the concept document for the establishment of the credit guarantee corporation.
