Cambodia launches PRISM disaster information system
PRISM is a system for collecting information on disasters via phone / tablet. The system provides a platform for providing timely information to assist in monitoring, evaluating, updating up-to-date information, easy for users and especially for decision makers. In addition, this forum is a place to integrate the flow of information of the Royal Government from relevant ministries to communicate with each other.
Senior Minister Kun Kim said that the PRISM Information and Situation Monitoring System was established under an agreement between the National Committee for Disaster Management and the World Food Program on Joint Action for Crisis Management and Risk Reduction. Disaster in the Kingdom of Cambodia, signed on November 20, 2019, which covers the 2017 Memorandum of Understanding.
He said the agreement establishes a cooperative framework to be ready to respond to disaster risk by developing national and sub-national capacity.
According to Senior Minister Kun Kim, after the announcement of the PRISM system, the National Committee for Disaster Management will train officials at the national and sub-national disaster management committees at the provincial and district levels to Gained hands-on experience in using tablet devices to enter data, exposure, damage, loss by disaster.
In addition, the National Committee for Disaster Management will also prepare guidelines for disaster preparedness planning, which requires the input of all relevant ministries, institutions, development partners, national and international organizations.
The director said that access to information quickly and promptly is essential to provide timely assistance in disasters.
She expects that the launch of this system will contribute to reducing the impact of disasters and also contribute to the achievement of the 2030 development strategy goals of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Dr. Sok Touch: The Royal Academy of Cambodia opens its heart to accept talented people from all over
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and Permanent Vice President of the Academic Council of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that the Royal Academy of Cambodia is open to capable people from all over to come together to explore new things. To help develop the country to be more prosperous.
Dr. Sok Touch said this at the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Royal Academy of Cambodia, National University of Management and the Prek Leap National Institute of Agriculture, which was held this morning, July 22, 2020 at the Khmer Art Heritage Hall, Indra Devi Building. Of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
Dr. Sok Touch emphasized that Cambodian scholars must think and research together to find input for the Royal Government, scholars and researchers in defining the vision and mapping for sustainable national development.
Mr. Sok Touch said that today's signing of the Memorandum of Understanding is to promote cooperation between the three institutions in documenting all areas, especially reflecting the concept of "theory linked to the implementation of ethical binding". The MoU also worked on four issues: joint research, joint environmental work, joint training, joint publication.
Dr. Sok Touch added that the Royal Academy of Cambodia has a lot of cooperation with foreign institutions such as institutions in Japan, Korea, Thailand, Singapore and other institutions to learn from each other.
He said that this is the first time for domestic institutions to cooperate with these two higher education institutions to promote research together with professors, students and researchers in social and environmental sciences. Publish research bulletins on various topics for the benefit of society as a whole.
It should be noted that the Royal Academy of Cambodia has the main mission to study both social sciences and real science to find input for the Royal Government and play a role in training and research from master's degree to doctoral degree.
More than 20,000 luxury saplings replanted in Sre Krasaing community forest area in Stong district, Kampong Thom province
Mr. Sok Lou said that the tradition of planting seedlings is a legacy left by King Norodom Sihanouk, called the Tree Day, and the ceremony was specifically designated by the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to celebrate the planting. This sapling grows every year all over the country.
In particular, the main purpose of this cultivation is to restore the lost forest for freshwater use, because the forest is very important and beneficial to people, animals, the environment.
He said that forests not only help people, animals and the environment, but also as a barrier to wind erosion, prevent erosion, prevent landslides, prevent natural disasters, storms, droughts, etc. and provide beauty. Attract more and more national and international tourists, which is an important source of income for the community and the nation as a whole.
He said that planting trees has a deep meaning for the movement to inspire people to love the forest to participate in planting and protecting the forest, as well as to help people in their daily lives to grow agricultural products to increase well-being. Families as well as help improve the social environment.
In addition, tree planting plays an important role in maintaining ecosystem function by helping to regulate climate change, reducing the negative effects of climate change, such as floods, hurricanes, and carbon sequestration.
On that occasion, he also called on all farmers to take care of the protection of forests and natural environment for the benefit of their livelihoods, communities and all kinds of wildlife and biodiversity. In particular, reduce natural disasters such as hurricanes, floods, droughts and so on.
According to the report of Mr. Pen Vanrith, Director of the Department of Community Forestry, Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Thom Province, there are 83 community forests in the province, and these saplings are planted on 40 hectares on a total area of 12,615 Hectares.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of National Defense is preparing to set up military historical sites in a number of locations. Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, stated that the organization of this military historical site is to protect and preserve the historical evidence for future generations to know.
This statement was made by Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the opening ceremony of the meeting on "Preparation of Military Historical Areas" on July 22, 2020, with the participation of The leadership of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, too.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh stated: "This workshop is to organize a chain of events to be one of the most important things, the defense sector and the protection of territorial integrity, in addition to the defense of evidence. "All that history has left is to be stable."
In addition, the Minister of Defense said that the workshop was held to discuss the search for geographical locations that are related to the battle at all stages that can be identified as military historical sites, especially documents, photographs and materials to compile and preserve. As a historical document for the next generation of soldiers to study.
Samdech said that in order to consider this, the Ministry of National Defense has held a workshop on "the preparation of military historical sites" to make all people aware that all these evidence is very important for history. These factors and the evidence of military history can be leading to document.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh added that in relation to the work of organizing the military historical site, the team had to research many major historical events that took place by identifying the location left behind to find witnesses to confirm the history and information related to Each location.
