CNC TV station announces lawsuit against Facebook owner "Knower, Rememberer" for stealing his logo to use to fabricate socially polluting information
CNC TV has confirmed that the Facebook page of "Knowers Remember" stole the CNC logo and put it in its video to be used for malicious purposes, to discredit the CNC TV station and to confuse and pollute the society.
With this rejection, CNC TV also announced that it has filed a complaint to the relevant authorities to take legal action against Facebook.
The following is the announcement of CNC TV: Senior Minister Kun Kim requested the authorities and the armed forces to be ready to respond to the floods
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, requested and appealed to the relevant authorities and all armed forces to be ready to respond to floods in a timely manner during the rainy season this year.
The senior minister said that as a disaster manager, all relevant officials must anticipate the preparation of measures for the response and initial recovery from the disaster.
The Senior Minister also requested to pay attention to disaster preparedness, so the Capital, Province, Municipality, District, Khan, Commune, Sangkat, Village must prepare a disaster preparedness plan by limiting the resources available from all stakeholders and property capabilities. Disaster Relief Assistance and the National Committee for Disaster Management will guide the forms to be implemented at all levels.
The First Vice-Chairman of the Disaster Management Committee also requested that the Sub-National Disaster Management Committee convene a meeting with local partners on pre-flood and drought preparedness measures. At the same time, partner organizations must cooperate to share information with each other to avoid overlapping support at any affected base. African swine fever still makes farmers in Svay Rieng dare not raise pigs again!
(Svay Rieng): Since the outbreak of African swine fever and the importation of pigs, farmers in Svay Rieng province who used to raise pigs have not dared to raise pigs again.
Mr. Kol Muon, 37, a pig distributor living in Bak Ronas village, Sangkor commune, Svay Rieng city, Svay Rieng province, which is the largest pig distributor in Svay Rieng province, said that currently at the market in Svay Rieng province need 150 to 200 pigs a day. Some days more than 200 head, and live pigs that traders collect at home 5 to 10 heads a day, cheaper than the company's pigs and pigs imported from Thailand.
Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Public Works closes Chhay Chhay Chhean truck repair site due to technical error
(Banteay Meanchey): The Department of Public Works cooperated with the Provincial Traffic Office this morning, July 22, 2020, to inspect and close the Chhay Chhean truck repair site in Kordathan Village, Sangkat O'Ambel, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
The garage caused several accidents and officials and authorities went to investigate the implementation of the contract of Chhay Chhean's car repair garage, finally found that the owner of the garage does not adhere to the business contract.
Contracts include: The garage owner must:
1: Vehicle technician within 6 months after obtaining business law 2: Do not violate and use the land for pedestrians 3: Comply with state law, do not install cages, thighs, wrong size, technical standards 4: Protect the environment, especially oil spills Slip out 5: Do not disturb the lives of neighbors 6: Reserve safety equipment, fire extinguishers.
Mr. Chhay Chhean, the owner of the garage, said that he only respected some of the contract and asked for six months to complete the remaining work and move to a new location.
Chhay Chhean's car repair garage has caused a series of incidents, such as:
Not only that, the garage is also frightening by the flames, smells and noise day and night, causing the oil spill on the sidewalk, affecting the people living nearby due to the loud noise.
Experts say that the garage asked for a license to open a business repairing large vehicles, not recycling, but secretly processing vehicles that are not technically correct and do not have a permit.
The traffic police and the provincial public works department have instructed the garage owners to apply for a permit first, and ask the mechanic to have a clear resume, no driver's license, do not charge, do not use the wrong technology to cooperate with the authorities.
