According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, within 83 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to July 22, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected And fined a total of 114,369 vehicles, including 84,555 motorcycles and 29,814 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet offense, offense, no license plate, drunkenness and cell phone use. In particular, the offenses for cars are mostly speeding, overcrowding, no belts, offenses, no license plates, overweight, using mobile phones and so on.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 83 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for July 22, 2020, traffic offenses throughout the country also occurred 8 times, including 5 deaths, 8 injuries (3 serious injuries).
