(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation held a ceremony to officially launch the PRIMERO case management system on July 22, 2020 at Sunway Hotel, Phnom Penh.
Premaro Technology Case Management System, developed by UNICEF and USAID, provides both technical and financial support. The establishment of PRIMERO is another new development to facilitate case management, family incident monitoring and family reunification, designed as a child protection information management system for use in Cambodia.
The system will assist case managers with case management staff to improve the quality of maintenance and efficiency through the creation and maintenance of secure and scalable online platforms to manage security-related data.
The official launch program was attended by Mr. Touch Channy, Technical Director General of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and a representative of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Mr. Jala Abdel Wahhab, UNICEF Vice President Cambodia, John Collins, Deputy Director of the Office of Education and Public Health of the United States Agency for International Development (USAID), and other relevant ministry officials.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Touch Channy would like to commit and encourage to ensure that the PRIMERO case management system can operate in all capitals and provinces, and he and professional officers will also monitor the progress of Implement this system and any potential challenges.
In addition, Mr. TOCH Channy also requested the technical and financial development partners, especially in the presence of USIAD today, to continue to provide material support until the system works well and successfully at the local level and all relevant staff are competent. And skills in using this system and reporting.
Addressing UNICEF and USAID Representative Toch Channy, he expressed hope that the PAMARO system would be an effective tool for analyzing the needs and gaps associated with this work and would be further refined in the future. Add other requirements that may be available when preparing this standard form. This will help establish a common child protection case management system for Cambodia.
