Tropical storms can occur when the wind blows very quickly after receiving heat from warm seawater. Then, when the air cools down, it is pushed to one side by the hot air rising from below it. This cycle of phenomena has caused storms. Tropical storms typically have winds of more than 117 kilometers per hour, while severe storms have even stronger winds.
Asteroid bigger than a spinning basket in London will fly closer to Earth this week
