Report: Preparation of private schools before reopening in Kovid era
(Phnom Penh): Some private schools are ready to set up protection systems and upgrade schools, while the government will reopen 20 schools with high safety standards during August. The coming year 2020.
It has been five months since March 16, 2020, that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has issued a guideline that requires students of all levels across the country to take early leave (small vacation). There is a new notification. The decision of the Ministry of Education is made as a precautionary measure to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 virus.
Kouch Mengly, Founder, Chairman and CEO of Mengly J. Kouch Education Co., Ltd., which manages AIS and Aii, said his private school was ready to have high safety standards before opening. Re-in the 1940s. The preparation is in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health of Cambodia and the World Health Organization (WHO).
Mr. Kouch Mengly said that in the classroom, there should be no more than 15 students, and the distance from one table to another is one and a half meters. In addition, there are signs on the campus from hand washing methods, masks, alcohol or gel and hand soap.
Mr. Kouch Mengly stated: "In general, from the heat, from the alcohol, from the soap, from the class gap, from the temperature, we always maintain 24 degrees. We trained the staff, taught the students and made videos for the people, parents and students to understand the measures in the school. We have a doctor who is the first school and the only one who has a doctor at the school. ”
"We have spent a lot of money on the equipment and the preparation, but we do not know the details," he said. We have a lot of students, we need to buy a lot of soap, alcohol and materials, and we need extra hygiene to clean everywhere. "We spend a lot of money, considering the cost before Kovid is 1 times 10."
Many private schools are preparing to reopen their schools in August, according to the guidelines of the Ministry of Health and the Ministry of Youth Education. And sports, as well as international safety principles.
Pech Bolen, CEO of Wesleyan Education Group, said: "Wesleyan School is well-prepared and we take the Ministry's guidelines as a basis for distribution, as well as some of the standards that other countries, such as Singapore and Hong Kong. And so on. ”
Wesleyan School has created a mask for students, teachers and staff to have a conversation so that small drops of saliva do not come into contact with each other, which is a good measure and avoids various respiratory infections. In addition, the school has a proper cleaning schedule, how to keep the campus clean, and for teachers and staff who have to go abroad, they must be monitored to ensure good health before he returns to campus. Back to school.
"As for the temperature measurement, we plan to use some automated systems to avoid the ones we measure with small devices," he said. "We can use a bit of sophisticated equipment to measure the temperature easily."
He added that Wesleyan currently has 13 locations and 13,000 students. As for the budget, he briefly calculated $ 100,000 to be ready to participate in protecting and preventing Kovid when the school reopens.
He stated that in order to reach the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding to test the first phase during August 2020, according to the letter of the Office of the Council of Ministers dated July 21, 2020, the Ministry of Education continues to guide, monitor and evaluate the organization. Of 20 private educational institutions on the following requirements:
1: Organizing the school environment, school buildings and classrooms (the number of students in the classroom who respect the safety gap) must follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health and the World Health Organization, especially educational institutions must be disinfected. Regularly equipped with standard disinfection equipment.
2: Teachers, students and staff of the educational institution must be tested for 19 Kovid virus before the school starts.
3. In the event that these educational institutions are negligent or violate the Memorandum of Understanding, those educational institutions will receive a warning and lead to a temporary suspension.
4: These educational institutions must continue to implement a variety of study methods, such as electronic distance learning, along with learning in the classroom, and adhere to the safety protocol of study health.
5. The Ministry will issue guidelines on the requirements for the promotion of educational health in the context of Kovid as a basis for the preparation of educational health safety protocols of educational institutions.
6: Educational institutions must implement the required measures.
Mr. Ros Sovacha added that based on the experience and evaluation of the implementation of the first phase, the Ministry of Education can determine the next steps for the second phase and the third phase.
