(Phnom Penh): General Chhorn Sarane, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Logistics and Finance, Ministry of Interior, this morning, July 21, 2020, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a 252-meter-long and 10-wide-wide concrete road. The meter is located at Chbar Ampov High School in Boeung Chhouk Village, Sangkat Niroth, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
This concrete road was donated by him and Mrs. Sem Samphors and his family, and the groundbreaking ceremony was attended by the principal of Chbar Ampov High School, Deputy Director of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Phnom Penh, teachers and About 300 students.
Mr. Heang Sokheng, Principal of Chbar Ampov High School, stated that General Chhorn Sarane and Ms. Sem Samphors are the leading philanthropists at Chbar Ampov High School, which has been inaugurated for almost 40 years. Subsequent, including cement and budget.
He said that this is the seventh time so far, and obviously in the past, including the 2,500-square-meter concrete road at the volleyball site around the flagpole in this ceremony, the school fence is 3 meters high and 357 meters long. On the east side, the school is at the base of the bridge, and today is the opening of another new concrete road, 252 meters long and 10 meters wide.
The principal continued that the former students of Chbar Ampov High School have many other philanthropists, but for the philanthropist who pays high attention to support the high school, only the principal and his wife have sacrificed a lot of time, money and personal resources. To support and develop Chbar Ampov High School and have the best of hearts with the teachers.
On that occasion, General Chhorn Sarane said that when he stepped on the school grounds, he immediately remembered the countless memories he had built with his friends and teachers. As of now, 35 years have passed in the blink of an eye.
He mentioned the names of the teachers who taught in each subject, such as Khmer, mathematics, physics, chemistry, biology, geology and ethics, etc. He also mentioned the participation in social work, and especially Watch the school at night for male students with good memories from childhood who came to school until adulthood for 6 years at this school (Chbar Ampov High School, formerly Cuba High School) until entering High school in 1991.
Connecting this priceless emotion, he asked the principal to help find those teachers who used to give him advice and knowledge, even if they are now retired or dying. However, bring his budget (salary) to provide for them or his family who are still alive.
General Chhorn Sarane announced the dedication of his monthly salary of 2640,000 Riels to support 22 teachers, each receiving 120,000 Riels every month until the end of their lives in return for their gratitude in Training from 1985 to 1991.
