Ministry of Agriculture issues guidelines on establishing and strengthening agricultural business clusters, farmers' groups and farming communities to easily find markets
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has issued guidelines on the establishment and strengthening of agricultural businesses, farmers' groups and agricultural communities to easily find markets for agricultural products.
The guidelines, obtained by Fresh News on July 22, state that the Ministry of Agriculture has in the past introduced a series of measures to increase food production, rice, fish, meat to meet domestic demand and serve exports. Hold the international market, especially in the context of Kovid-19 disease, which is spreading around the world.
As a result, agricultural production, both food and non-food, has increased significantly and some farmers are facing market problems, the ministry said. To help solve these problems, the Ministry of Agriculture would like to advise the program director, the head of the unit under the Ministry and the director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of the Capital and Provinces to immediately implement some additional measures as follows:
1: To create more agricultural business clusters, farmers' groups and agricultural communities in order to fully increase supply capacity, especially to increase the ability to negotiate prices with buyers of agricultural products, which this measure will raise Encourage farmers to grow food crops, animal husbandry and aquaculture more actively and not worry about market issues.
2. To continue to strive for the production plan of the agricultural business group, the producer group and the farming community to produce in accordance with the needs and time to go to the company or collector of agricultural products that can avoid flood production. Tide and no clear market.
3. To cooperate well with all stakeholders to organize, establish and implement agricultural production in accordance with the contract between agricultural business groups, farmers' groups and agricultural communities to supply food, rice, fish, meat with confidence and efficiency.
4. Establish a farmers' market or any suitable location that allows farmers to sell safety products to help solve market problems, ensure supply and maintain market price balance.
5: To consider financing and training, active technical dissemination to agricultural business groups, farmers, producers and agricultural communities to strengthen technical capacity and effective management.
6. To work closely with the relevant ministries, institutions and relevant authorities to facilitate agricultural business groups, farmers' groups and agricultural communities to obtain loans with reasonable low interest rates from the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture and use electricity in the agricultural sector. By courtesy.
7. The Fisheries Administration must thoroughly examine the request to import fishery products from abroad, without allowing the import of fishery products that are highly competitive with domestic aquaculture products.
