"Because of this policy, Pailin province has been transformed from a conflict zone into a peaceful area like today," he said. "These are the unforgettable merits of the officers, deputies and soldiers of all parties who have made sacrifices in the period from the civil war to the end of the war to achieve full peace as it is today."
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet also praised and appreciated the great achievements and progressive development of Pailin Military Operation Area in the period from its inception to the present. Leading an organization, as well as leading a country, cannot build an organization forward without reminiscing about the achievements of previous generations of builders.
He added that internal unity is important because it ensures the sustainability of leadership through cooperation, trust, mutual understanding, joint task and problem solving based on hierarchy. Although the leadership of the organization can not be perfect, but must be guided by the principles of law and principles of the organization. As a strong collective, unity is a strong force, a chopstick does not break.
