General Director of Rural Development Bank Continues to Disseminate the Royal Government's $ 50 Million Financing Program to Farmers in Kampong Chhnang Province
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Kao Thach, Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, on July 21, 2020, under the coordination of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration, led his colleagues to continue to disseminate the credit policy under the special financing program of the Royal Government of US $ 50 million. To the community in Kampong Chhnang province.
Mr. Kao Thach added that in principle, this special financing program will provide loans from US $ 5,000 to US $ 300,000 with a low interest rate of 5% annually for working capital (short term 2 years). And for investment capital (long term for 7 years) at an interest rate of 5.5% per annum.
In addition, with regard to credit collateral under this special program, Mr. Kao Thach stated that the Rural Development Bank and Agriculture can provide up to 80% of the value of collateral, which is real estate, and the acceptance of collateral is very flexible. Accepting: equipment, machinery, inventory, letter of guarantee from the buyer or other guarantee, certificate of deposit other than real estate.
During a meeting with farmers in Prey Kabbas district, Takeo province, on the morning of July 21, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been working to promote agricultural work for 41 years since the Pol Pot era, but not enough. Not yet.
Samdech Techo added that in order to promote agricultural work, the Royal Government has continuously changed the infrastructure, rehabilitated the canal and prepared the main canal so that the farmers have enough resources to grow crops to support their families and the rest for export.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that in the past, in the past, before the Paris Agreement negotiations, the state tried to intervene in canals and pumps, but after that negotiations, the state abandoned this intervention. But after seeing the people facing water shortage, Samdech also considered to intervene again and consider the establishment of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology.
Later, with the attention of the Royal Government, farmers seem to be growing more vigorously than before, while in 2012, Cambodia still lacks food, but when the policy of exporting rice, Cambodia began to rest. According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the goal of exporting 1 million tons of rice per year is still the main goal and the agricultural policy 2015-2025 will continue to be implemented.
In fact, in 2019, Cambodia left more than 6 million tons of rice and more than 4 million tons of rice, but the prince said that the rice policy achieved only one thing is to evolve from lack of food to food. However, the export of 1 million tons has not been achieved yet. For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the goal of exporting 1 million tons of rice per year is still important and is expected to be achieved by 2021.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also saw that the current situation facing the agricultural sector in Cambodia is the lack of access to processing for export.
According to the current Prime Minister, Cambodia is trying to boost investment by building rice warehouses, rice mills and drying mills to encourage farmers. Samdech Techo said that when Cambodia exports rice abroad, it will cause the loss of farmers' jobs, the loss of rice husks, the loss of rice husks, the loss of rice husks and so on.
The Cambodian Prime Minister, who was born of a farmer's son and always cares for Cambodian farmers, said that Cambodia has invested $ 400 million from China to build rice storage facilities in the provinces, while the current rice yield has exceeded. Export processing capabilities.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that the agricultural sector, especially rice, must be in line with the industrial policy 2015-2025, which is aimed at attracting foreign investment to invest in processing in Cambodia. Samdech Tha Samdech led the country from the killing field regime to development and led the country from lack of food to more than 4 million tons of rice.
At the same time, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia also advised professional officers to increase the development of irrigation system to meet the needs of farmers, ie to take Prey Kabas district, Takeo province as a model for building this irrigation system in other agricultural areas. .
According to figures released by the Ministry of Agriculture, Cambodia exported 620,000 tons of rice (official figure), while the unofficial rice export in 2019 to Vietnam more than 2 million tons in border provinces such as Takeo, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng. Kandal and Kampot.
In the first six months of 2020, about 1 million tons of rice were exported to Kampot, Takeo, Kandal, Prey Veng and Svay Rieng to Vietnam. More than 400,000 tons of rice has been exported to 56 target markets.
