Cambodian Customs Chief and Duke Kith Meng Chair a Meeting to Solve Challenges for Trade and Investment
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhem, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia and Co-Chair of the Government Technical Working Group on the Customs-Private Partnership Mechanism and Duke Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and This morning, July 21, 2020, he co-chaired a special meeting of the Customs-Private Partnership Mechanism at the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia.
The special meeting was also attended by the co-chairs of each sector technical working group from the private and government sectors, and was attended by many important customs officials and members of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
Dr. Kun Nhem highlighted the achievements of the Customs-Private Sector Partnership in the past, especially through the organization of a series of meetings, mechanisms and expert working group meetings that have solved many problems with results. A good fruit.
In response, the duke stated that the Customs-Private Partnership Mechanism is a forum for dialogue in partnership to consult and seek solutions to all issues based on win-win and mutual understanding and support. The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has set out a number of rules to provide additional trade facilitation from time to time, especially during the outbreak of Kovid-19.
After discussing the above points, this special meeting agreed for each expert working group to continue to increase the discussion to solve future problems in a timely and effective manner and also agreed. On the organization of the 8th meeting of the Customs-Private Sector Partnership Mechanism in due course.
Duke Kith Meng also thanked Dr. Kun Nhem and thanked the Co-Chairs of the Customs Technical Working Group and Customs Officers, members of the Chamber of Commerce who were present for the whole meeting. Next to help facilitate trade in Cambodia.
In response, Dr. Kun Nhem also thanked the private sector for always providing input as well as providing information that the private sector is facing challenges and suggestions to the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia and the General Department of Customs and Excise Cambodia is waiting for cooperation in discussing solutions for the private sector, which will be mentioned in the future.
(Kampong Thom): Authorities have identified a case of murder of a woman and dumped her body in a pond in Kampong Thom province, where the perpetrator was her husband.
This woman was killed by her husband and her body was thrown into a pond, causing a great surprise this morning, July 21, 2020, in Kwan Teang village, Sala Visay commune, Prasat Balong district, Kampong Thom province.
Kampong Thom provincial authorities told Fresh News that the body of the victim, Srun Chantrea, 30, in the village where the incident took place, was a private doctor. The woman was stabbed in the left neck with a machete, causing her death, and was thrown into a pond about 100 meters behind the house.
According to the authorities, the suspect is her husband, Thol Thearith, 30 years old, and the family has three children (a girl). The case was investigated by special forces under the command of Major General Ouk Kosal, the provincial police commissioner, until 2:00 pm the same day, and the suspect's husband admitted that he had cut his wife to death.
The suspect told authorities that the cause of the murder was a family dispute.
The suspects are now being processed, while the bodies have been handed over to relatives for traditional rites.
