(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, July 21, 2020, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, inspected the rice fields and talked with local farmers. Prey Kabbas, Takeo Province.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with farmers for about 2 hours. The following are the main points of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech:
* At the beginning of the meeting with farmers in Prey Kabbas district, Takeo province, Samdech Techo Hun Sen had some questions for those farmers
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen's first question to the farmers of Prey Kabas district is, what is the easy job, what is the difficult for them?
* Farmers have many requests, including: the price of electricity, the price of rice, the request for a two-lane road in Prey Kabas district to make it easier to travel and transport.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the Minister of Rural Development to build two roads, one 3.5 km long and the other 3 km long, for the people of Prey Kabas district to travel easily
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces to provide 130 small rice sowing machines to 130 families in Prey Kabas district
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen In 2012, Cambodia still lacked food, but when the policy of exporting rice, Cambodia began to rest.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that before the Paris Agreement negotiations, the state tried to intervene in canals and pumps, but after the state negotiations abandoned this intervention.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that after seeing the people face water shortage, Samdech reconsidered the intervention and considered the establishment of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that after 1998, when the CPP won the election, Samdech decided to establish the Ministry of Water Resources.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that 20 years ago, Samdech came to Prey Kabas district to harvest rice with a machete, but 20 years later, Samdech used a rice harvesting machine.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expresses his appreciation to the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, as well as officials who have worked hard to help farmers change their attitude to farming as well as rice varieties.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that during the war, Takeo was the number one rice-producing province but now the number three in agriculture.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that under the efforts of the Ministry and officials, farmers agreed to change rice varieties.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Australia for its assistance to Cambodia's agricultural sector.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the beginning of the agricultural sector in Cambodia started a long time ago, not a new thing. From 1979, 10 Agriculture Ministers have been exchanged.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that during his term as Chan Sarun as Minister, the farmers changed their attitude the most.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that the people of Takeo have become leaders of many ministries and provinces.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has been working in the agricultural sector for 41 years since the post-Pol Pot era, but it is still not enough.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that about 1 million tons of rice was exported to Kampot, Takeo, Kandal, Prey Veng and Svay Rieng to Vietnam.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is in a situation where there is a shortage of gold and paper.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is currently investing in the establishment of rice mills, storage facilities and kilns.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the rice yield exceeded the processing capacity in export.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the future, Cambodia will become a country in the ASEAN Free Trade Area, so it requires equal competition.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the agricultural sector, especially rice, must be in line with the industrial policy 2015-2025, which is aimed at attracting foreign investment to invest in processing in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech led the country with more than 5 million people to almost 16 million people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in other areas, water problems will be solved as in Prey Kabas district to complete the development of agriculture.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks Australia to continue to help expand the irrigation system in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the Cambodian people had to be diverted from the beginning, 1 hectare of land to feed 5 people, now it is necessary to feed 10 people, 20 people and 30 people
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Kovid can destroy us to some extent, but can not kill us, we must make sure that Cambodians do not lack rice to eat
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that in the world, they can reduce flights, they can suspend travel, they can suspend buying clothes, they can suspend buying cars, motorbikes, but they can not suspend food for the stomach, this is an opportunity For agriculture
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that workers who lost their jobs due to factory closures or hotel closures must return to promote agricultural work with their families
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that we will have to increase the expenditure for more than 610,000 poor and vulnerable families about 28 million dollars this July
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that by 2030, agriculture in Prey Kabbas district, Cambodia will become a rice-rich country capable of self-cultivation and export
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen revealed that this morning, Samdech ordered 1,000 large and 1,000 small rice sowing machines, of which 130 small machines were distributed to 130 families.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen mocks some researchers who do not know at all what Cambodia has gone to become a researcher
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on people to use masks when necessary to prevent Kovid 19 infection
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on people all over the country to be careful of Kovid 19 and during the five-day holiday to pay for the coming New Year, gatherings should be avoided.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen ended his speech with farmers in Prey Kabas district at 10:18 a.m. the same day. Egypt agrees to send troops to Libya that could lead to direct conflict with Turkey
