(Kep): 74-year-old Mak Sun was evicted from her home by her 50-year-old daughter Ouk Puthy and barred from entering the 15,326-square-meter plot of land belonging to her. Since 2011. The disputed land is located in Thmey Village, Sangkat Prey Thom, Kep City, Kep Province, which she owned and had a title deed dated May 20, 1990.
After evicting the mother from the house, the daughter, Ouk Puthy, who is also a teacher and her husband, who is also a teacher, has occupied the land arbitrarily without a letter or recognition from the local authorities until now.
Mrs. Mak Sun has been struggling to resolve the land dispute with her daughter for more than nine years, but to no avail. She was not allowed to enter his land, as she confirmed in the letter to Samdech Techo. Although there is a grave of his mother in the land, the daughter does not allow the mother to go to the festival in that land.
Unable to bear the pain anymore, on July 14, 2020, Mrs. Mak Sun decided to apply for Samdech Techo Metta to help her find justice. Because the previous settlement was ineffective.
On July 17, 2020, Mr. Duong Dara, Personal Assistant to the Prime Minister and his team visited the scene and studied some evidence documents and listened to the explanation of the local authority, which confirmed that the daughter of He occupies the land above without a title deed.
Mr. Duong Dara tried to mediate between mother and child with the participation of Kep Mayor and the mayor, as well as local authorities, in which Ms. Mak Sun agreed to give more than 1 hectare of land to her daughter. He asked for only half a hectare, just sold the season to make ends meet, but the daughter refused.
The mediation that day was not accepted by the daughter as a teacher, as she argued that if she had more children, she would have to get more land. However, Mr. Duong Dara stated that if the mediation method can not be reconciled, only follow the law to find the culprit, which will take a lot of resources and time, and it is not certain that one side will win alone.
Mr. Duong Dara asked his daughter to consider because she is also his biological mother, and a small surplus is considered to be a celebration for her mother. But this compromise is that the children get two-thirds, which is enough to get. Then, on July 19, the teacher's daughter said she agreed.
Immediately after the thumbprints, all parties, including local authorities and cadastral officers, went to the disputed land and measured the distribution of the land to Mrs. Mak Sun and her daughter as agreed to issue a title deed to them. .
Mrs. Mak Sun was very happy and she expressed her deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for giving her the last minute of her life.
Mr. Duong Dara also expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Prime Minister for his support and gave him and his team the opportunity to mediate disputes in accordance with the principles of Samdech's win-win.
He said that Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit are always concerned about the well-being of people everywhere, regardless of political affiliation. Because the happiness of the people is the happiness of both Samdech.
At the same time, Mr. Duong Dara also thanked the Governor of Kep Province, the Governor of Kep City, the President of Kep City Cadastral and all relevant authorities who have always cooperated well in implementing the principle of win-win for Samdech Techo to be successful. .
He also called on all officials to work together to build good deeds and share love with people everywhere without discrimination. At the same time, Mr. Duong Dara also thanked the volunteer lawyer and Samdech Techo's lawyer who always participated in helping to get good results to this day, regardless of time or profit. 31 Poor Families in Kandal Province Receive Humanitarian Donations from Preah Chao Athikar Wat Chaktomukharam
