Mr. Chea Chanboribo established a project to raise frogs and grow sweet grapes for the poor people in Kralanh district
(Phnom Penh): Based on the old Khmer view of "poor but not poor", Mr. Chea Chanboribo, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information and Chairman of the Kralanh District Assistance Team in Siem Reap Province, decided to establish two projects: frog raising and grape planting. Sweet to poor people level 1 and level 2 in Ta An commune and Kralanh commune, Kralanh district, Siem Reap province.
For this project of raising frogs and sweet vines, Mr. Chea Chanboribo is the provider of breeding materials and trainers.
Mr. Chea Chanboribo said that for the frog raising project, he provided materials for breeding 500 frogs, fed and provided trainers to help raise and collect from the target group.
As for the trainer, Mr. Chea Chanboribo chose from the project of planting and raising animals to keep the pot, which he established in 2019 in Kralanh district.
Mr. Chea Chanboribo stated that he decided to create these two projects after he observed that most of the local people living below the poverty line always leave their village land vacant. Animals for eating or picking up pots.
He added that this is like shaking hands with the people to be diligent and have the owner to help themselves, not just waiting for help.
Please note that this pilot project is funded by Mr. Chea Chanboribo and his male friend. The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Information added that after the successful pilot project, he will expand the project to a larger scale.
