General knowledge: The three golden words of the scholar Socrates, first executed more than 2,500 years ago
Before Socrates was sentenced to death by the Athenian government for accusing him of being an atheist and inciting youth, many of his disciples and supporters arranged for him to escape from prison, but he refused. Three words, including:
1. The relationship between the state and the people is not the same as the relationship between parents and children, the state is indebted to the people because the people are the parents of the state. However, Socrates understood that all citizens, in any case, must obey the state and not betray their own ideals.
2. As a strict law-abiding citizen of Athens, he received provisions for his life. So he signed with Athens, so he had to obey Athenian law.
3: If you know the law, do not respect the law, who can obey the law? In other words, Socrates meant that if the rulers did not obey the law, there would be the most dangerous outcome in judging the case.
According to other documents and the BBC, another important reason why Socrates was sentenced to death by the Athenian administration was because he disagreed with the Athenian doctor on the issue of the earth's appearance. Socrates says that the earth is round like an orange, while Athens says that the earth is like a palm frond, and people live on it.
* Biography of Socrates:
Socrates's task is to seek the truth, to have common sense, to have moral and ethical values, which are the nature of the state and the law. If there is a discussion on morality and politics, he explains clearly and in a defensive manner.
* Socrates' personality:
To gain knowledge, Socrates used four methods: the method of laughing, the method of giving light, the method of common inference, and the method of defining. The four methods include:
2: The method of common inference: is that you make common inference to search for universal criteria.
3: Birth method: is to make people distinguish between good and bad, right and wrong.
4: How to define: is to define the precepts of each word in ethics. Socrates used these four methods, requiring communication and influencing each other. Chipmung Inc. Cement Ecocycle Project Inaugurates Industrial Waste Storage Facility in Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone
(Sihanoukville): The Ecocycle project of Chipmung Inc. Cement, a provider of modern and highly sustainable waste disposal solutions, has signed an agreement with the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone on the construction of an industrial waste storage facility located in the economic zone. Especially Sihanoukville.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone is located in Prey Nob District, Sihanoukville Province, built by Chinese and Cambodian private enterprises, as a major project of the "Belt and Road" initiative aimed at creating a good investment platform for "investing in ASEAN. To spread to the world ”of the enterprise.
In the first phase of the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, major industries include textiles and garments, bags and leather products, bags and leather products, construction equipment, home furnishings and chemicals.
In the second phase, there are now 165 enterprises from China, the United States, Europe, Southeast Asia and other countries and 30,000 workers.
Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone wants to become a well-functioning and complete ecological model industrial zone with a total of 300 enterprises with a total workforce of 100,000.
Jianjiang Cao, General Manager of Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, said: “During the development and construction process, Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has always adhered to the concept of" win-win cooperation "with eight points. One is to want environmentally friendly development to build a win-win relationship with the environment.
"We not only created greenery during construction, but also built drainage pipes to separate rainwater and sewage," he said. We are proud to say that our wastewater treatment plant is the best in Cambodia. ”
Waste management has become an important issue in Cambodia, which is becoming increasingly difficult amid high economic growth. The initiative will provide sustainable waste management solutions to enterprises in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone using a globally recognized technology called "Co-processing".
